(270, NULL, 'api', NULL, 'General Practitioner Telehealth Case Conferencing Clinic', 'Proactive Health', 'Remote', 'https://remoteOK.com/remote-jobs/remote-general-practitioner-telehealth-case-conferencing-clinic-proactive-health-1132867', '<p></p><p>Are you a GP looking for meaningful, flexible clinical work â one day in clinic, one day remote, without the full-time grind?</p><p>Veteran Pathways &amp; Proactive Care is seeking experienced General Practitioners to deliver chronic disease management and structured multidisciplinary case conferencing for veterans and patients with complex, multi-system health needs. The role runs across two structured days each week â an in-clinic day at our Ipswich partner practice and a remote telehealth case-conferencing day â with some flexibility on the days to suit you.</p><p>This is not a standard locum. You will provide clinical leadership within integrated Chronic Care Teams, working alongside allied health professionals and specialists to translate clinical findings into coordinated, evidence-based care plans. The work is structured, purposeful and genuinely multidisciplinary â a system that values thorough, evidence-based care over high-volume throughput.</p><p></p>Remuneration<p>First 3 Months (Guaranteed) = $240.00 per hour</p><p>After 3 Months = 70% of billings</p><ul><ul><li>Structured as an independent contractor arrangement.</li><li>Bulk-billing model across Medicare and DVA billing streams.</li><li>Sign-on bonus and anniversary incentive available (details on enquiry).</li><li>Ipswich is a DPA-eligible location â GPs with a 19AB exemption, including international medical graduates, are welcome to apply</li></ul></ul><p></p>Location &amp; working options<p>In-clinic day (Tuesday): an 8-hour clinic day at a well-established allied-health practice and a natural multidisciplinary home for chronic-care work.</p><p>Remote case-conferencing day (Thursday): an 8-hour telehealth case-conferencing session, delivered from your home office (a suitable space and reliable internet are all thatâs required). There is some flexibility on which days these fall, arranged around your availability.</p><p> </p>The Role<p>As a General Practitioner within our Chronic Care Team model, you will provide clinical leadership across in-clinic consultations and structured telehealth case conferencing:</p><ul><li>Conduct comprehensive GP consultations for acute, chronic and complex conditions within a Chronic Care Team framework (in-clinic and/or by telehealth).</li><li>Deliver preventative health assessments â cardiovascular risk, metabolic health, mental-health screening and lifestyle risk modification.</li><li>Undertake chronic disease management (CDM) reviews and care planning, including GP Management Plans (GPMPs) and Team Care Arrangements (TCAs).</li><li>Lead and participate in scheduled telehealth case conferences as part of multidisciplinary Chronic Care Teams, integrating clinical, pathology, imaging and allied-health input into coordinated care plans.</li><li>Initiate, review and manage pathology and imaging investigations; provide prescribing and medication management; and refer to allied health, specialists and community services.</li><li>Ensure clinical safety, prioritisation and escalation pathways are clearly identified and actioned.</li></ul><p>Working pattern: the role is built around two structured days each week â an 8-hour in-clinic day on a Tuesday at our Ipswich practice (consultations and chronic-disease reviews) and an 8-hour remote case-conferencing session on a Thursday (approximately 22 patient reviews, conducted entirely via telehealth). There is some flexibility on which days these fall, arranged around your availability.</p><p></p>Veteran Health &amp; DVA Focus<p>Veteran Pathways &amp; Proactive Care has a dedicated focus on veteran health and chronic disease management for both Medicare and DVA-funded patients. You will work with veterans who often present with complex, multi-system conditions including chronic pain, mental health comorbidities, musculoskeletal injuries, and the long-term effects of military service.</p><p>Experience with DVA billing, the Coordinated Veteransâ Care (CVC) Program, or veteran-specific health assessments is highly regarded but not essential â comprehensive onboarding and support will be provided.</p>\n<p>Essential</p><ul><li>Medical degree (MBBS or equivalent) and current registration with the Medical Board of Australia (AHPRA).</li><li>Fellowship with RACGP or ACRRM (VR GP), OR eligibility for a 19AB exemption in a DPA location such as Ipswich (IMGs welcome).</li><li>Experience in chronic disease management, preventative health and complex care coordination.</li><li>Competence in prescribing, referrals and investigation management.</li><li>Strong communication and collaboration skills within multidisciplinary teams.</li><li>For the telehealth pathway: a suitable home-office environment and reliable internet connection.</li></ul><p>Desirable</p><ul><li>Experience with telehealth consultations and digital-health platforms.</li><li>Experience within team-based or multidisciplinary care models.</li><li>Interest or experience in veteran health, DVA processes or the CVC Program.</li><li>Experience with GP Management Plans (GPMPs), Team Care Arrangements (TCAs) and chronic disease care planning.</li></ul>\n<p> </p><ul><li>Guaranteed $240/hr for the first 3 months, moving to 70% of billings thereafter.</li><li>Sign-on and anniversary bonuses to support your transition (details discussed at interview).</li><li>A balanced two-day rhythm â one in-clinic day at Ipswich and one remote case-conferencing day â with some flexibility on the days, arranged around you.</li><li>Meaningful, purpose-driven work improving outcomes for veterans and patients with complex chronic conditions.</li><li>Multidisciplinary collaboration within established Chronic Care Teams, with full administrative, nursing and allied-health support.</li><li>A structured clinical model that values thorough, evidence-based care over high-volume throughput.</li></ul><p></p><p>Apply now or contact our Head of Talent, Stuart Smith (stuart.s@pro-active.com.au) for a confidential discussion.</p><p></p><br/><br/>Please mention the word **EXCELENT** and tag RNjkuNTcuMTYyLjE0 when applying to show you read the job post completely (#RNjkuNTcuMTYyLjE0). This is a beta feature to avoid spam applicants. Companies can search these words to find applicants that read this and see they\'re human.', '<p></p><p>Are you a GP looking for meaningful, flexible clinical work â one day in clinic, one day remote, without the full-time grind?</p><p>Veteran Pathways &amp; Proactive Care is seeking experienced General Practitioners to deliver chronic disease management and structured multidisciplinary case conferencing for veterans and patients with complex, multi-system health needs. The role runs across two structured days each week â an in-clinic day at our Ipswich partner practice and a remote telehealth case-conferencing day â with some flexibility on the days to suit you.</p><p>This is not a standard locum. You will provide clinical leadership within integrated Chronic Care Teams, working alongside allied health professionals and specialists to translate clinical findings into coordinated, evidence-based care plans. The work is structured, purposeful and genuinely multidisciplinary â a system that values thorough, evidence-based care over high-volume throughput.</p><p></p>Remuneration<p>First 3 Months (Guaranteed) = $240.00 per hour</p><p>After 3 Months = 70% of billings</p><ul><ul><li>Structured as an independent contractor arrangement.</li><li>Bulk-billing model across Medicare and DVA billing streams.</li><li>Sign-on bonus and anniversary incentive available (details on enquiry).</li><li>Ipswich is a DPA-eligible location â GPs with a 19AB exemption, including international medical graduates, are welc