ome flexibility on which days these fall, arranged around your availability.</p><p></p>Veteran Health &amp; DVA Focus<p>Veteran Pathways &amp; Proactive Care has a dedicated focus on veteran health and chronic disease management for both Medicare and DVA-funded patients. You will work with veterans who often present with complex, multi-system conditions including chronic pain, mental health comorbidities, musculoskeletal injuries, and the long-term effects of military service.</p><p>Experience with DVA billing, the Coordinated Veteransâ Care (CVC) Program, or veteran-specific health assessments is highly regarded but not essential â comprehensive onboarding and support will be provided.</p>\n<p>Essential</p><ul><li>Medical degree (MBBS or equivalent) and current registration with the Medical Board of Australia (AHPRA).</li><li>Fellowship with RACGP or ACRRM (VR GP), OR eligibility for a 19AB exemption in a DPA location such as Ipswich (IMGs welcome).</li><li>Experience in chronic disease management, preventative health and complex care coordination.</li><li>Competence in prescribing, referrals and investigation management.</li><li>Strong communication and collaboration skills within multidisciplinary teams.</li><li>For the telehealth pathway: a suitable home-office environment and reliable internet connection.</li></ul><p>Desirable</p><ul><li>Experience with telehealth consultations and digital-health platforms.</li><li>Experience within team-based or multidisciplinary care models.</li><li>Interest or experience in veteran health, DVA processes or the CVC Program.</li><li>Experience with GP Management Plans (GPMPs), Team Care Arrangements (TCAs) and chronic disease care planning.</li></ul>\n<p> </p><ul><li>Guaranteed $240/hr for the first 3 months, moving to 70% of billings thereafter.</li><li>Sign-on and anniversary bonuses to support your transition (details discussed at interview).</li><li>A balanced two-day rhythm â one in-clinic day at Ipswich and one remote case-conferencing day â with some flexibility on the days, arranged around you.</li><li>Meaningful, purpose-driven work improving outcomes for veterans and patients with complex chronic conditions.</li><li>Multidisciplinary collaboration within established Chronic Care Teams, with full administrative, nursing and allied-health support.</li><li>A structured clinical model that values thorough, evidence-based care over high-volume throughput.</li></ul><p></p><p>Apply now or contact our Head of Talent, Stuart Smith (stuart.s@pro-active.com.au) for a confidential discussion.</p><p></p><br/><br/>Please mention the word **EXCELENT** and tag RNjkuNTcuMTYyLjE0 when applying to show you read the job post completely (#RNjkuNTcuMTYyLjE0). This is a beta feature to avoid spam applicants. Companies can search these words to find applicants that read this and see they\'re human.', 'new', NULL, '2026-06-06 15:20:10.804', '2026-06-06 15:20:10.804', '', '', 'Remote', 'Europe', '', 'RemoteOK', 'API', 'READY', '', '', '', 'api', 'https://remoteOK.com/remote-jobs/remote-general-practitioner-telehealth-case-conferencing-clinic-proactive-health-1132867', '', '[]', 'pending', '', NULL),
