(2419, NULL, 'api', NULL, 'Paid Media Specialist Meta & Google Ads', 'Noventra Group', 'Remote', 'https://remoteOK.com/remote-jobs/remote-paid-media-specialist-meta-google-ads-noventra-group-1134552', '<p>Noventra Group is hiring a remote Paid Media Specialist to support Meta Ads and Google Ads campaigns across selected partner-brand initiatives.</p><p>This role is focused on performance marketing, campaign optimization, reporting, and paid media execution for brands and commercial partners working within Noventra Groupâs partner-brand ecosystem.</p><p>About Noventra Group</p><p>Noventra Group is a European-based brand partnership and commercial growth group working with selected brands, ecommerce businesses, retail partners, consumer product companies, and commercial partners across multiple markets.</p><p>The companyâs work is centered on partner-brand development, market expansion, campaign coordination, digital acquisition, and performance-focused commercial operations.</p><p>Noventra Group is not positioned as a traditional marketing agency. The team works across partner-brand campaigns where paid media, commercial strategy, campaign performance, and clear reporting are important parts of the operating structure.</p><p>Role Overview</p><p>The Paid Media Specialist will work across Meta Ads and Google Ads campaigns for partner brands in ecommerce, retail, lifestyle, consumer products, premium goods, and service-based markets.</p><p>The role requires strong hands-on paid media experience, clear analytical thinking, practical optimization judgment, and the ability to communicate campaign performance in a structured and professional way.</p><p>The ideal candidate understands how to review paid advertising data, identify performance issues, improve campaign structure, test creative angles, monitor budget efficiency, and produce clear recommendations that support better business outcomes.</p><p>Key Responsibilities</p><p>- Plan, launch, monitor, and optimize paid advertising campaigns across Meta Ads and Google Ads<br />- Review campaign structure, audience targeting, budget allocation, bidding strategy, and conversion paths<br />- Monitor key performance indicators including CPA, ROAS, CTR, CPC, conversion rate, lead quality, and budget efficiency<br />- Identify issues in campaign setup, tracking, creative performance, funnel quality, and landing page conversion flow<br />- Review ad creatives, hooks, messaging, visuals, offers, and campaign angles<br />- Prepare clear campaign reports, optimization notes, and performance summaries<br />- Recommend practical next steps based on campaign data and commercial objectives<br />- Support campaign testing, scaling decisions, and performance improvement plans<br />- Work with remote teams across different markets and maintain clear written communication<br />- Keep campaign documentation organized, including changes, observations, results, and recommendations</p><p>Required Experience</p><p>- Hands-on experience managing Meta Ads campaigns<br />- Hands-on experience managing Google Ads campaigns<br />- Experience with Search, Display, Shopping, YouTube, Performance Max, or similar Google Ads campaign types<br />- Strong understanding of paid media optimization, campaign reporting, and performance analysis<br />- Ability to interpret advertising data and make practical campaign decisions<br />- Experience managing advertising budgets with measurable performance outcomes<br />- Good written English communication skills<br />- Ability to work remotely, manage priorities independently, and communicate clearly<br />- Organized, detail-oriented, and comfortable working across multiple campaigns or brand accounts</p><p>Preferred Experience</p><p>- Experience with ecommerce, DTC, retail, fashion, beauty, lifestyle, wellness, premium products, or service-based campaigns<br />- Familiarity with GA4, Google Tag Manager, Meta Pixel, Shopify, landing pages, CRM tracking, or conversion tracking setup<br />- Experience preparing weekly or monthly paid media reports<br />- Experience with creative testing, ad angle analysis, funnel review, and campaign scaling<br />- Experience working with international teams or multiple partner-brand campaigns<br />- Experience with business-managed advertising accounts, invoiced ad accounts, monthly billing structures, or partner-brand ad operations is a plus</p><p>Working Style</p><p>This is a remote role suited for someone who can work independently, communicate professionally, and provide structured campaign insights without requiring constant supervision.</p><p>Noventra Group values clear reporting, reliable communication, organized work, data responsibility, and practical problem-solving. The role requires a professional approach to campaign management, partner-brand communication, and performance improvement.</p><p>Compensation and Engagement</p><p>Compensation is based on experience, capability, availability, and engagement structure.</p><p>The role may be suitable for a long-term remote collaboration depending on experience, performance, communication quality, and alignment with Noventra Groupâs partner-brand operating standards.</p><br/><br/>Please mention the word **SOOTHE** and tag RMTU5LjE5OC42Ni4xNjM= when applying to show you read the job post completely (#RMTU5LjE5OC42Ni4xNjM=). This is a beta feature to avoid spam applicants. Companies can search these words to find applicants that read this and see they\'re human.', '<p>Noventra Group is hiring a remote Paid Media Specialist to support Meta Ads and Google Ads campaigns across selected partner-brand initiatives.</p><p>This role is focused on performance marketing, campaign optimization, reporting, and paid media execution for brands and commercial partners working within Noventra Groupâs partner-brand ecosystem.</p><p>About Noventra Group</p><p>Noventra Group is a European-based brand partnership and commercial growth group working with selected brands, ecommerce businesses, retail partners, consumer product companies, and commercial partners across multiple markets.</p><p>The companyâs work is centered on partner-brand development, market expansion, campaign coordination, digital acquisition, and performance-focused commercial operations.</p><p>Noventra Group is not positioned as a traditional marketing agency. The team works across partner-brand campaigns where paid media, commercial strategy, campaign performance, and clear reporting are important parts of the operating structure.</p><p>Role Overview</p><p>The Paid Media Specialist will work across Meta Ads and Google Ads campaigns for partner brands in ecommerce, retail, lifestyle, consumer products, premium goods, and service-based markets.</p><p>The role requires strong hands-on paid media experience, clear analytical thinking, practical optimization judgment, and the ability to communicate campaign performance in a structured and professional way.</p><p>The ideal candidate understands how to review paid advertising data, identify performance issues, improve campaign structure, test creative angles, monitor budget efficiency, and produce clear recommendations that support better business outcomes.</p><p>Key Responsibilities</p><p>- Plan, launch, monitor, and optimize paid advertising campaigns across Meta Ads and Google Ads<br />- Review campaign structure, audience targeting, budget allocation, bidding strategy, and conversion paths<br />- Monitor key performance indicators including CPA, ROAS, CTR, CPC, conversion rate, lead quality, and budget efficiency<br />- Identify issues in campaign setup, tracking, creative performance, funnel quality, and landing page conversion flow<br />- Review ad creatives, hooks, messaging, visuals, offers, and campaign angles<br />- Prepare clear campaign reports, optimization notes, and performance summaries<br />- Recommend practical next steps based on campaign data and commercial objectives<br />- Support campaign testing, scaling decisions, and performance improvement plans<br />- Work with remote teams across different markets and maintain clear written communication<br />- Keep campaign documentation organized, including changes, observations, results, and recommendations</p><p>Required Experience</p><p>- Hands-on experience managing Meta Ads campaigns<br />- Hands-on experience managing Google Ads campaigns<br />- Experience with Search, Display, Shopping, YouTube, Performance Max, or similar Google Ads campaign types<br />- Strong understanding of paid media optimization, campaign reporting, and performance analysis<br />- Ability to interpret advertising data and make practical campaign decisions<br />- Experience managing advertising budgets with measurable performance outcomes<br />- Good written English communication skills<br />- Ability to work remotely, manage priorities independently, and communicate clearly<br />- Organized, detail-oriented, and comfortable working across multiple campaigns or brand accounts</p><p>Preferred Experience</p><p>- Experience with ecommerce, DTC, retail, fashion, beauty, lifestyle, wellness, premium products, or service-based campaigns<br />- Familiarity with GA4, Google Tag Manager, Meta Pixel, Shopify, landing pages, CRM tracking, or conversion tracking setup<br />- Experience preparing weekly or monthly paid media reports<br />- Experience with creative testing, ad angle analysis, funnel review, and campaign scaling<br />- Experience working with international teams or multiple partner-brand campaigns<br />- Experience with business-managed advertising accounts, invoiced ad accounts, monthly billing structures, or partner-brand ad operations is a plus</p><p>Working Style</p><p>This is a remote role suited for someone who can work independently, communicate professionally, and provide structured campaign insights without requiring constant supervision.</p><p>Noventra Group values clear reporting, reliable communication, organized work, data responsibility, and practical problem-solving. The role requires a professional approach to campaign management, partner-brand communication, and performance improvement.</p><p>Compensation and Engagement</p><p>Compensation is based on experience, capability, availability, and engagement structure.</p><p>The role may be suitable for a long-term remote collaboration depending on experience, performance, communication quality, and alignment with Noventra Groupâs partner-brand operating standards.</p><br/><br/>Please mention the word **SOOTHE** and tag RMTU5LjE5OC42Ni4xNjM= when applying to show you read the job post completely (#RMTU5LjE5OC42Ni4xNjM=). This is a beta feature to avoid spam applicants. Companies can search these words to find applicants that read this and see they\'re human.', 'new', NULL, '2026-07-08 13:43:53.952', '2026-07-08 13:43:53.952', '', '', 'Remote', 'Europe', '', 'RemoteOK', 'API', 'READY', '', '', '', 'api', 'https://remoteOK.com/remote-jobs/remote-paid-media-specialist-meta-google-ads-noventra-group-1134552', 'https://remoteOK.com/remote-jobs/remote-paid-media-specialist-meta-google-ads-noventra-group-1134552', '[{\"url\":\"https://remoteOK.com/remote-jobs/remote-paid-media-specialist-meta-google-ads-noventra-group-1134552\",\"type\":\"applyUrl\"}]', 'pending', '', NULL),
(2420, NULL, 'api', NULL, 'Custodian', 'Hospitality Newfoundland and Labrador', 'St Johnâs,', 'https://remoteOK.com/remote-jobs/remote-custodian-hospitality-newfoundland-and-labrador-1134554', '<strong>Full-Time Custodian<br><br></strong>Do you take pride in making sure things are in clean and tip-top shape? Perhaps youâre a handy person thatâs not afraid to get their hands dirty with physical work? Do you have experience setting up for events both large and small?<br><br>If so, you might be a great fit as the C<strong>ustodian</strong> with the St. Johnâs Farmersâ Market team.<br><br>The <strong>Custodian </strong>will be responsible for the cleanliness and maintenance of the Farmersâ Market, will help with event setup, tear-down and cleanup, plus all other things facility related.<br><br><strong>Day-to-day duties will be wide-ranging but are likely to include:<br><br></strong><ul><li>Maintain the cleanliness of all areas of the building and grounds, including taking the lead on regular and ongoing cleaning of the building,</li><li>Supporting and supervising other cleaning staff by providing direction on priorities and best practices for cleaning</li><li>Helping to set up and tear down for events and markets.</li><li>Providing minor maintenance of the building, as well as routinely checking the building for potential facilities concerns.</li><li>Maintain OHS and Food Safety standards.<br><br></li></ul><strong>The ideal fit for this role would be a person who:<br><br></strong><ul><li>Is able to work every weekend as part of their weekly schedule. This is a required part of the role.</li><li>Can work with minimal supervision and is able to keep on top of facilities cleaning on an ongoing basis,</li><li>Is a handy-person who has some familiarity with maintenance and upkeep of commercial spaces,</li><li>Is capable of daily physical work such as cleaning, lifting and carrying tables, and setting up spaces for market and events,</li><li>Has the ability to lift or move up to 40 pounds,</li><li>Is comfortable guiding support staff in their work,</li><li>Is an outgoing, friendly, and flexible worker comfortable in a busy, very diverse, and inclusive environment.<br><br></li></ul><strong>Bonus Skills<br><br></strong><ul><li>If you are familiar with NL Food Safety Guidelines or OHS regulations it would be a definite bonus, but is not mandatory.</li><li>If you are familiar with commercial kitchen equipment or cleaning a restaurant kitchen, it would also be a bonus, but again, not mandatory.<br><br></li></ul><strong>Compensation And Schedule<br><br></strong><ul><li>This is a full-time position</li><li>The role will be 35 hours per week at $22.00 per hour.</li><li>We work weekends. This position will require working every Saturday and Sunday as part of your weekly schedule.<br><br></li></ul>Interested? Send us a resume and cover letter as soon as possible. We are looking to hire quickly and interviews will be starting on July 11th.<br><br>The St. Johnâs Farmersâ Market celebrates diversity, and welcomes applications from all qualified candidates.<br><br>We thank all applicants for their interest, however only those selected for an interview will be contacted.<br><br>Job Type: Full-time<br><br>Pay: $22.00 per hour<br><br><strong>Application Question(s)<br><br></strong><ul><li>We work weekends. Are you able to work both Saturday and Sunday each week as part of your regular schedule?<br><br></li></ul>Work Location: In person<br/><br/>Please mention the word **DESTINY** and tag RMTU5LjE5OC42Ni4xNjM= when applying to show you read the job post completely (#RMTU5LjE5OC42Ni4xNjM=). This is a beta feature to avoid spam applicants. Companies can search these words to find applicants that read this and see they\'re human.', '<strong>Full-Time Custodian<br><br></strong>Do you take pride in making sure things are in clean and tip-top shape? Perhaps youâre a handy person thatâs not afraid to get their hands dirty with physical work?