INSERT INTO `ai_training_entries` (`id`, `question`, `answer`, `is_active`, `created_at`) VALUES
(1, 'Who is Shagor?', 'Shahanur Islam Shagor is a software developer focused on full-stack product development, backend systems, AI-powered features, and maintainable web platforms. He also has interest and academic focus in autonomous systems, UAV coordination, and cybersecurity.', 1, '2026-04-28 00:00:00.000'),
(2, 'What kind of work does Shagor do?', 'He mainly works on web applications, backend APIs, admin dashboards, SaaS platforms, AI-assisted product features, deployment support, and long-term product improvements.', 1, '2026-04-28 00:00:00.000'),
(3, 'Is Shagor a frontend developer or backend developer?', 'He works as a full-stack developer. That means he can handle frontend interfaces, backend APIs, databases, admin dashboards, integrations, and launch support in one delivery flow.', 1, '2026-04-28 00:00:00.000'),
(4, 'What technologies does he use most?', 'His common stack includes React, Next.js, Node.js, Express, TypeScript, Prisma, MySQL, MongoDB, AWS, Docker, Nginx, and related modern web tools.', 1, '2026-04-28 00:00:00.000'),
(5, 'Does he work with Next.js and React?', 'Yes. Next.js and React are part of his core stack for building fast interfaces, product sites, dashboards, and scalable frontend experiences.', 1, '2026-04-28 00:00:00.000'),
(6, 'Can he build backend APIs?', 'Yes. Backend systems and API engineering are one of his strongest service areas. He can build secure, structured APIs for web apps, mobile apps, internal systems, and third-party integrations.', 1, '2026-04-28 00:00:00.000'),
(7, 'Does he build full-stack products from scratch?', 'Yes. He can take a product from planning to delivery, including UI, backend, database design, admin workflows, deployment, and post-launch support.', 1, '2026-04-28 00:00:00.000'),
(8, 'Can he join an existing project?', 'Yes. He can step into an existing codebase for bug fixing, feature development, refactoring, API work, performance improvement, or longer-term maintenance.', 1, '2026-04-28 00:00:00.000'),
(9, 'Can he review my current codebase before we start?', 'Yes. A short technical review is often the best first step for an existing product. It helps identify structure problems, risks, performance issues, and the safest path forward.', 1, '2026-04-28 00:00:00.000'),
(10, 'Does he build admin panels and dashboards?', 'Yes. He builds admin dashboards for operations, content management, workflow control, reporting, and role-based access.', 1, '2026-04-28 00:00:00.000'),
(11, 'Can he build a SaaS application?', 'Yes. SaaS projects are a strong fit. He can build authentication, role management, subscriptions, billing logic, dashboards, settings, and scalable backend architecture.', 1, '2026-04-28 00:00:00.000'),
(12, 'Can he build an MVP for a startup?', 'Yes. He can help shape and build an MVP with practical scope, fast delivery, and enough technical structure to avoid obvious future problems.', 1, '2026-04-28 00:00:00.000'),
(13, 'Does he work with AI features?', 'Yes. He has experience integrating AI assistants, prompt-driven workflows, structured AI outputs, and AI-powered product features into real applications.', 1, '2026-04-28 00:00:00.000'),
(14, 'Can he integrate OpenAI into a product?', 'Yes. He has experience using OpenAI-based features for assistant flows, trained business logic behavior, content generation, and product automation.', 1, '2026-04-28 00:00:00.000'),
(15, 'Has he built AI projects before?', 'Yes. His portfolio includes an AI-powered financial application and an AI-powered real estate platform, both involving production use cases rather than simple demo integrations.', 1, '2026-04-28 00:00:00.000'),
(16, 'Can he build a chatbot for my business?', 'Yes. He can build a chatbot or assistant for lead qualification, support, internal guidance, or workflow automation, depending on the business goal.', 1, '2026-04-28 00:00:00.000'),
(17, 'Can he train an assistant on my own dataset?', 'Yes. He can structure AI behavior around your business content, rules, and product workflow so answers stay relevant to your use case. The exact approach depends on how your data is stored and how reliable the output needs to be.', 1, '2026-04-28 00:00:00.000'),
(18, 'Can he build voice to text or document generation features?', 'Yes. He has experience with workflows such as voice-to-text processing and automated PDF generation inside production systems.', 1, '2026-04-28 00:00:00.000'),
(19, 'Can he build secure authentication systems?', 'Yes. He can build login flows, role-based auth, OTP verification, and practical access control for both public and internal systems.', 1, '2026-04-28 00:00:00.000'),
(20, 'Can he integrate Google login, Facebook login, or OTP?', 'Yes. He has experience with authentication flows that include social login and OTP-based verification when the project requires it.', 1, '2026-04-28 00:00:00.000'),
(21, 'Does he work with Stripe or subscriptions?', 'Yes. He can integrate subscription flows, payment events, and billing logic for SaaS or service-based products.', 1, '2026-04-28 00:00:00.000'),
(22, 'Can he build booking or travel platforms?', 'Yes. He has experience working on a travel agency application with multi-language, multi-currency, frontend UX, backend APIs, and deployment support.', 1, '2026-04-28 00:00:00.000'),
(23, 'Can he build publishing or newsroom systems?', 'Yes. He has worked on a newsroom management product and can build dashboards for content, editorial planning, and structured publishing workflows.', 1, '2026-04-28 00:00:00.000'),
(24, 'Can he build mobile app backends?', 'Yes. If you already have a mobile app or plan to build one, he can create the backend APIs, authentication, content flows, notification logic, and admin control needed to support it.', 1, '2026-04-28 00:00:00.000'),
(25, 'Can he work with databases too?', 'Yes. Database design and data modeling are part of his standard workflow. He works with MySQL, MongoDB, PostgreSQL, and ORM-based structures such as Prisma.', 1, '2026-04-28 00:00:00.000'),
(26, 'Can he improve a messy database structure?', 'Yes. He can review the current schema, identify weak relationships or scaling issues, and redesign or refactor the data model more safely.', 1, '2026-04-28 00:00:00.000'),
(27, 'Does he work with Prisma?', 'Yes. Prisma is part of his regular backend workflow, especially for schema design, query structure, and maintainable database access in Node.js applications.', 1, '2026-04-28 00:00:00.000'),
(28, 'Can he fix bugs in a live product?', 'Yes. He can investigate issues in frontend, backend, database, deployment, or third-party integrations. He usually focuses on root cause, not just a surface-level patch.', 1, '2026-04-28 00:00:00.000'),
(29, 'Can he optimize a slow website?', 'Yes. He can improve performance at the frontend, backend, database, or server level depending on where the bottleneck actually lives.', 1, '2026-04-28 00:00:00.000'),
(30, 'Can he help after launch?', 'Yes. He offers post-launch support for fixes, updates, performance work, maintenance, and ongoing product improvements.', 1, '2026-04-28 00:00:00.000'),
(31, 'Does he do deployment too?', 'Yes. He can help with deployment, production setup, environment configuration, server preparation, domain wiring, SSL, and launch stabilization.', 1, '2026-04-28 00:00:00.000'),
(32, 'Can he work with AWS?', 'Yes. He has worked with AWS-related services for hosting, email delivery, storage, and AI-connected product workflows.', 1, '2026-04-28 00:00:00.000'),
(33, 'Can he set up Nginx, PM2, or Docker?', 'Yes. He can configure production environments using common tools like Nginx, PM2, and Docker for Node-based applications.', 1, '2026-04-28 00:00:00.000'),
(34, 'Can he build cron jobs and automations?', 'Yes. He can add scheduled jobs, data sync tasks, reminders, content processing, or workflow automations where a product needs them.', 1, '2026-04-28 00:00:00.000'),
(35, 'Can he build real-time chat or live updates?', 'Yes. He can implement real-time product features such as chat, ticket updates, notifications, and event-driven interactions.', 1, '2026-04-28 00:00:00.000'),
(36, 'Can he build a portfolio website for a developer or agency?', 'Yes. Portfolio websites are a good fit when the goal is a polished online presence, strong service presentation, project highlights, and contact-ready conversion flow.', 1, '2026-04-28 00:00:00.000'),
(37, 'Can he redesign an old website?', 'Yes. He can modernize the design, improve usability, refresh structure, and rebuild the frontend or backend when needed.', 1, '2026-04-28 00:00:00.000'),
(38, 'Does he make websites responsive for mobile?', 'Yes. Responsive behavior across mobile, tablet, and desktop is considered a standard part of delivery, not an optional extra.', 1, '2026-04-28 00:00:00.000'),
(39, 'Can he create a CMS or content management system?', 'Yes. He can build editable systems for pages, blogs, FAQs, articles, projects, services, media, and admin-managed content.', 1, '2026-04-28 00:00:00.000'),
(40, 'Can he build blog and article systems?', 'Yes. He can build article publishing systems with categories, SEO metadata, content editing, comments, and admin workflows.', 1, '2026-04-28 00:00:00.000'),
(41, 'Can he set up analytics or visitor tracking?', 'Yes. He can implement useful analytics features such as page tracking, event metrics, custom reports, and admin-level usage insights.', 1, '2026-04-28 00:00:00.000'),
(42, 'Does he care about security?', 'Yes. Security is treated as part of product engineering. That includes validation, file handling, authentication, access control, and safer production configuration.', 1, '2026-04-28 00:00:00.000'),
(43, 'Can he work with confidential products?', 'Yes. He can work under confidentiality expectations and is comfortable signing an NDA if needed for the project.', 1, '2026-04-28 00:00:00.000'),
(44, 'Can he work with agencies as a development partner?', 'Yes. He can collaborate with agencies or product teams as a white-label or delivery-focused development partner when the scope and workflow are clear.', 1, '2026-04-28 00:00:00.000'),
(45, 'Can he work remotely with international clients?', 'Yes. He can collaborate remotely and across time zones as long as communication expectations and delivery rhythm are aligned clearly.', 1, '2026-04-28 00:00:00.000'),
(46, 'How quickly can a project start?', 'Many projects can start within a few days after the scope, timeline, and priorities are aligned. Larger builds may begin with a short planning phase first.', 1, '2026-04-28 00:00:00.000'),
(47, 'How long does a project usually take?', 'Timeline depends on scope, features, content readiness, revision flow, and technical complexity. Small websites move faster, while dashboards and SaaS products usually need phased delivery.', 1, '2026-04-28 00:00:00.000'),
(48, 'Can he build my full product in two weeks?', 'That depends on the actual scope. A focused landing page or smaller feature set may fit a short timeline, but a serious product should be scoped honestly so quality does not suffer.', 1, '2026-04-28 00:00:00.000'),
(49, 'How does he estimate project cost?', 'Cost is usually shaped by scope, complexity, number of features, integration depth, timeline pressure, and post-launch support needs. A clear brief leads to the most accurate estimate.', 1, '2026-04-28 00:00:00.000'),
(50, 'What pricing plans are shown on the site?', 'The current portfolio shows three example pricing levels: Starter, Professional, and Enterprise. They help frame engagement size, but final pricing still depends on the actual project scope.', 1, '2026-04-28 00:00:00.000'),
(51, 'What is the Starter plan for?', 'The Starter plan is positioned for smaller websites, landing pages, or quick launch support where the scope is focused and the delivery path is relatively simple.', 1, '2026-04-28 00:00:00.000'),
(52, 'What is the Professional plan for?', 'The Professional plan is better for growing products that need more depth, such as multi-page experiences, stronger UX, admin workflows, and structured product delivery.', 1, '2026-04-28 00:00:00.000'),
(53, 'What is the Enterprise plan for?', 'The Enterprise plan is for more complex work such as backend-heavy systems, long-term product support, larger custom builds, and architecture that needs to scale.', 1, '2026-04-28 00:00:00.000'),
(54, 'Can he work on a monthly retainer?', 'Yes. Ongoing monthly collaboration can be a good fit for teams that need regular development, support, iteration, and technical continuity.', 1, '2026-04-28 00:00:00.000'),
(55, 'Can he work on a fixed-scope basis?', 'Yes. Fixed-scope work is possible when the goals, required features, and boundaries are clearly defined before the build starts.', 1, '2026-04-28 00:00:00.000'),
(56, 'Will I get the source code?', 'Yes, if the engagement includes full delivery and handoff. It is best to make ownership, access, and delivery expectations explicit at the beginning of the project.', 1, '2026-04-28 00:00:00.000'),
(57, 'Does he use Git and GitHub?', 'Yes. Version control is a normal part of his workflow and helps keep development traceable, collaborative, and safer to manage over time.', 1, '2026-04-28 00:00:00.000'),
(58, 'Can he write technical documentation?', 'Yes. He can provide practical handoff notes, setup guidance, and project structure explanations so a team can continue using and maintaining the product properly.', 1, '2026-04-28 00:00:00.000'),
(59, 'Can he take over a half-finished project from another developer?', 'Yes. He can step into unfinished work, but the best results usually come after a careful review of the current codebase, infrastructure, and unresolved product decisions.', 1, '2026-04-28 00:00:00.000'),
(60, 'Can he migrate an old system to a new stack?', 'Yes. He can help migrate code, data, content, or hosting setup, with attention to keeping business logic and important data intact.', 1, '2026-04-28 00:00:00.000'),
(61, 'Can he integrate email delivery and notifications?', 'Yes. He can implement transactional email, OTP delivery, alerting flows, and related notification systems for product onboarding and operations.', 1, '2026-04-28 00:00:00.000'),
(62, 'Can he support file uploads and media management?', 'Yes. He can build file and image upload workflows, secure handling, storage integration, and the admin-side controls needed to manage them.', 1, '2026-04-28 00:00:00.000'),
(63, 'Can he help with SEO-friendly development?', 'Yes. He can build pages with clean structure, metadata, performance-minded rendering, and other technical foundations that help SEO.', 1, '2026-04-28 00:00:00.000'),
(64, 'Is he suitable for startup founders?', 'Yes. Startup work is a strong fit when the goal is practical execution, clear technical judgment, and a product that balances speed with maintainability.', 1, '2026-04-28 00:00:00.000'),
(65, 'Is he suitable for established companies too?', 'Yes. He can also support established teams that need dashboards, APIs, operational tooling, integrations, migration work, or focused product improvements.', 1, '2026-04-28 00:00:00.000'),
(66, 'What experience does he have?', 'His portfolio and seed data show experience across remote web development, onsite development work, backend systems, product UI, and self-driven engineering practice over several years.', 1, '2026-04-28 00:00:00.000'),
(67, 'What education background does he have?', 'He is studying Software Engineering at Voronezh State University of Forestry and Technology in Russia, and he also completed a Diploma in Computer Technology from Dhaka Polytechnic Institute in Bangladesh.', 1, '2026-04-28 00:00:00.000'),
(68, 'Does he have certificates or achievements?', 'Yes. The portfolio includes development-related certificates, awards, and technical recognition items that support his practical engineering background.', 1, '2026-04-28 00:00:00.000'),
(69, 'What skills are highlighted on the site?', 'The site highlights technologies such as React, Next.js, Redux, Express, NestJS, MySQL, MongoDB, Docker, AWS, TypeScript, and other modern development tools.', 1, '2026-04-28 00:00:00.000'),
(70, 'Can he work with Laravel or PHP too?', 'Yes. Although much of his recent work is in modern JavaScript and TypeScript stacks, he also has experience with Laravel and can support PHP-based work when the project is a good fit.', 1, '2026-04-28 00:00:00.000'),
(71, 'Can he help with cybersecurity-related software work?', 'Yes. His profile includes interest and specialization areas around cybersecurity, and he can contribute to secure product thinking, system design, and careful backend implementation.', 1, '2026-04-28 00:00:00.000'),
(72, 'Can he help with autonomous systems or UAV-related software?', 'Yes. His broader engineering profile includes autonomous systems and UAV coordination as areas of specialization. Whether he is a fit depends on the exact software problem, but he is open to technically serious discussions in that space.', 1, '2026-04-28 00:00:00.000'),
(73, 'How should I contact Shagor?', 'The best way is through the contact form on the portfolio site or by email at smshagor.ru@gmail.com. If you share your goals, timeline, and current situation, he can respond with a more useful next step.', 1, '2026-04-28 00:00:00.000'),
(74, 'Can I send my project brief first?', 'Yes. In fact, sending a clear brief first usually leads to a faster and better response. Helpful details include the goal, expected users, must-have features, timeline, and any existing links or materials.', 1, '2026-04-28 00:00:00.000'),
(75, 'What should I include when I reach out?', 'A strong first message should include what you want to build, whether it is new or existing, your target timeline, rough budget expectations, and any examples or references. That makes it much easier to suggest the right path.', 1, '2026-04-28 00:00:00.000'),
(76, 'Can he tell me right away if my idea is realistic?', 'Yes. He can usually give a grounded first opinion once the scope is clear. If something is too broad for the timeline or budget, the better approach is to reduce scope and define a stronger first phase.', 1, '2026-04-28 00:00:00.000'),
(77, 'Will he be honest if my plan is too big or unclear?', 'Yes. A good technical partner should be direct about scope, risk, and tradeoffs. If the plan is too broad, the usual recommendation is to simplify the first release instead of overpromising.', 1, '2026-04-28 00:00:00.000'),
(78, 'Can he suggest the right stack for my project?', 'Yes. If you explain the product goal, expected scale, admin needs, and timeline, he can suggest a practical stack rather than forcing a one-size-fits-all choice.', 1, '2026-04-28 00:00:00.000'),
(79, 'Can he work with my existing designer or developer?', 'Yes. He can collaborate with existing teammates as long as responsibilities are clear and the workflow is organized well enough to keep momentum.', 1, '2026-04-28 00:00:00.000'),
(80, 'What kind of questions is he best suited to answer on the site?', 'He is best suited to answer questions about his services, project fit, technical stack, AI capabilities, pricing direction, collaboration approach, portfolio projects, and the best next step for starting a build.', 1, '2026-04-28 00:00:00.000'),
(81, 'What services are listed on the website?', 'The current site highlights three main service areas: Full-Stack Product Development, Backend Systems and API Engineering, and Performance, Deployment, and Support.', 1, '2026-04-28 00:00:00.000'),
(82, 'What is included in the full-stack product development service?', 'That service focuses on end-to-end web product delivery. It covers modern frontend work, backend APIs, database design, and admin workflows so the product stays useful beyond the first launch.', 1, '2026-04-28 00:00:00.000'),
(83, 'What is included in the backend systems and API engineering service?', 'That service is for secure, scalable backend work such as authentication, content APIs, admin access control, integrations, and clean data modeling for growing products.', 1, '2026-04-28 00:00:00.000'),
(84, 'What is included in performance, deployment, and support?', 'That service covers launch preparation, hosting or server setup, production hardening, bug fixing, iterative improvements, and technical continuity after the initial release.', 1, '2026-04-28 00:00:00.000'),
(85, 'What projects are featured on the site?', 'The featured portfolio projects include an AI Powered Financial App, a Travel Agency App, an AI Powered Real Estate platform, and a Newsroom Management dashboard project.', 1, '2026-04-28 00:00:00.000'),
(86, 'What was Shagor\'s role in the AI Powered Financial App?', 'In that project, he worked as a backend developer and built API architecture using Express, TypeScript, OpenAI, AWS, and MongoDB, along with authentication, voice processing, and PDF generation workflows.', 1, '2026-04-28 00:00:00.000'),
(87, 'What was his role in the Travel Agency App?', 'He worked as a full stack developer on the travel product, covering both the frontend user experience and the backend API structure, including deployment support on AWS.', 1, '2026-04-28 00:00:00.000'),
(88, 'What was his role in the AI Powered Real Estate project?', 'He worked as a full stack developer on that platform, including backend APIs, OpenAI and Replicate integrations, subscriptions, billing support, and frontend delivery across one product flow.', 1, '2026-04-28 00:00:00.000'),
(89, 'What was his role in the Newsroom Management project?', 'He contributed as a full stack developer, with strong focus on dashboard frontend work using Next.js, Material UI, Redux, React Hook Form, and editorial workflow features.', 1, '2026-04-28 00:00:00.000'),
(90, 'What pricing plans are available on the site right now?', 'The current pricing section shows Starter, Professional, and Enterprise plans. These are reference packages that help explain engagement size, but final scope and quote still depend on the actual project.', 1, '2026-04-28 00:00:00.000'),
(91, 'How much does the Starter plan cost?', 'The Starter plan is listed at 49 per month in the current site data. It is presented as an entry-level package for smaller websites, landing pages, and quick launch support.', 1, '2026-04-28 00:00:00.000'),
(92, 'How much does the Professional plan cost?', 'The Professional plan is listed at 149 per month. It is aimed at growing products that need more design depth, multiple pages, admin-friendly structure, and ongoing iteration.', 1, '2026-04-28 00:00:00.000'),
(93, 'How much does the Enterprise plan cost?', 'The Enterprise plan is listed at 999 per year in the current seed data. It is positioned for deeper engagements involving complex systems, backend architecture, or long-term delivery.', 1, '2026-04-28 00:00:00.000'),
(94, 'What is the price of your services?', 'The site currently shows Starter at 49 monthly, Professional at 149 monthly, and Enterprise at 999 yearly. For custom work, the final price depends on the exact scope, timeline, and technical complexity.', 1, '2026-04-28 00:00:00.000'),
(95, 'What is the cost of building a project with Shagor?', 'There is no one universal project cost. The site includes reference plans, but a real estimate depends on the product size, required features, integrations, timeline, and the amount of post-launch support needed.', 1, '2026-04-28 00:00:00.000'),
(96, 'What is your rate?', 'There is no single public hourly rate in the database. The portfolio is structured more around project packages and scope-based delivery, so the best next step is to share the project details and get a tailored estimate.', 1, '2026-04-28 00:00:00.000'),
(97, 'What is your charge for website development?', 'The charge depends on the type of website and the level of work involved. Smaller projects may fit the Starter package, while more advanced business or product builds usually fit Professional or Enterprise level discussions.', 1, '2026-04-28 00:00:00.000'),
(98, 'What is your fee for a dashboard project?', 'Dashboard pricing depends heavily on user roles, data complexity, admin workflows, filters, reports, and backend requirements. Most dashboard projects are usually better aligned with a custom quote than a simple fixed package.', 1, '2026-04-28 00:00:00.000'),
(99, 'What is your budget range?', 'The visible pricing on the site starts with entry-level monthly packages and goes up to a larger annual engagement, but the true budget range varies based on what needs to be built. Sharing the project goals is the fastest way to narrow that down.', 1, '2026-04-28 00:00:00.000'),
(100, 'Can you give me a quote?', 'Yes. A tailored quote is possible once the project scope is clear. Helpful details include the product goal, feature list, timeline, whether the product already exists, and the level of design or backend complexity needed.', 1, '2026-04-28 00:00:00.000'),
(101, 'Can I get an estimate before starting?', 'Yes. Once the core requirements are shared, Shagor can usually provide a grounded first estimate or suggest the best package level and next step.', 1, '2026-04-28 00:00:00.000'),
(102, 'Do you offer monthly packages?', 'Yes. The current pricing section includes monthly packages such as Starter and Professional, which are useful for smaller launches and growing product needs.', 1, '2026-04-28 00:00:00.000'),
(103, 'Do you offer yearly plans?', 'Yes. The current site data includes an Enterprise plan billed annually, intended for more complex systems and longer-term engagement.', 1, '2026-04-28 00:00:00.000'),
(104, 'What is the monthly charge?', 'Based on the current pricing section, the visible monthly charges are 49 for Starter and 149 for Professional. Final custom work may differ depending on scope and delivery model.', 1, '2026-04-28 00:00:00.000'),
(105, 'What is the yearly charge?', 'The current yearly plan shown on the site is Enterprise at 999 per year. That package is framed around deeper, more technical product delivery.', 1, '2026-04-28 00:00:00.000'),
(106, 'Which package is best for a small business website?', 'The Starter package is the closest match in the current pricing section. It is designed for smaller websites, landing pages, and quick launch support with a simple scope.', 1, '2026-04-28 00:00:00.000'),
(107, 'Which package is best for a growing startup?', 'The Professional package is usually the better fit when the product needs multiple pages, stronger UX, admin structure, and room for iteration during development.', 1, '2026-04-28 00:00:00.000'),
(108, 'Which package is best for a complex system?', 'The Enterprise package is the closest published fit for larger systems, backend-heavy platforms, advanced integrations, and long-term technical delivery.', 1, '2026-04-28 00:00:00.000'),
(109, 'What does the Starter package include?', 'In the current pricing data, the Starter plan includes one landing page, basic support, design updates, and email support. It is intended for a faster and simpler launch path.', 1, '2026-04-28 00:00:00.000'),
(110, 'What does the Professional package include?', 'The Professional plan includes up to five pages, priority support, performance tweaks, and an admin dashboard. It is better suited to products that need more depth than a simple website.', 1, '2026-04-28 00:00:00.000'),
(111, 'What does the Enterprise package include?', 'The Enterprise plan includes custom scope, dedicated support, backend architecture, and deployment guidance. It is intended for advanced or long-term product work.', 1, '2026-04-28 00:00:00.000'),
(112, 'Are the prices fixed?', 'The listed packages are useful references, but final pricing is not always fixed. Larger or more custom projects usually need a scope-based discussion before the final number is confirmed.', 1, '2026-04-28 00:00:00.000'),
(113, 'Can pricing change based on requirements?', 'Yes. Pricing can change depending on complexity, integrations, number of user roles, delivery speed, content readiness, and whether the project includes post-launch support.', 1, '2026-04-28 00:00:00.000'),
(114, 'Do you charge more for urgent work?', 'Urgent work can affect pricing if the timeline is unusually compressed or if it requires reshuffling other delivery commitments. The final decision depends on the specific request and timeline pressure.', 1, '2026-04-28 00:00:00.000'),
(115, 'Do you offer custom pricing?', 'Yes. Custom pricing is appropriate when the project does not fit neatly into the published Starter, Professional, or Enterprise structure.', 1, '2026-04-28 00:00:00.000'),
(116, 'Can I hire Shagor for long-term support?', 'Yes. Long-term support is part of his positioning, especially through deployment, maintenance, iterative product improvement, and ongoing technical collaboration.', 1, '2026-04-28 00:00:00.000'),
(117, 'What does the home page say about his work?', 'The homepage presents Shagor as a software developer who builds scalable websites, dashboards, and backend systems with strong focus on clarity, performance, and long-term maintainability.', 1, '2026-04-28 00:00:00.000'),
(118, 'What does the service section communicate?', 'The service section is positioned around ambitious brands and product teams. It emphasizes scalable digital experiences, engineering discipline, thoughtful UX, and maintainable backend systems.', 1, '2026-04-28 00:00:00.000'),
(119, 'What do the stats counters show?', 'The current stats section highlights 50 plus projects completed, 30 plus happy clients, 5 plus years of experience, and 12 awards or wins.', 1, '2026-04-28 00:00:00.000'),
(120, 'What testimonials are on the site?', 'The homepage currently includes testimonials from Sarah Mitchell of Northwind Studio and Daniel Carter of BrightPath Labs. Both reviews describe organized execution, strong communication, and polished delivery.', 1, '2026-04-28 00:00:00.000'),
(121, 'What contact information is available?', 'The portfolio uses smshagor.ru@gmail.com as the main contact email and also shows a phone number in the site settings. The contact form is intended as the easiest path for project inquiries.', 1, '2026-04-28 00:00:00.000'),
(122, 'What resume or profile links are available?', 'The profile data includes a public resume link and social links such as GitHub, Facebook, LinkedIn, Twitter, Stack Overflow, and LeetCode.', 1, '2026-04-28 00:00:00.000'),
(123, 'Does the site show social profiles?', 'Yes. The portfolio includes social links for GitHub, Facebook, LinkedIn, Twitter, Stack Overflow, and LeetCode as part of the profile information.', 1, '2026-04-28 00:00:00.000'),
(124, 'What skills are shown in the hero section?', 'The hero section highlights core technologies such as React, NextJS, Redux, Express, NestJS, MySQL, MongoDB, Docker, and AWS.', 1, '2026-04-28 00:00:00.000'),
(125, 'What experience entries are available?', 'The current experience list includes remote work as a Web Developer at Explo-IT, onsite work as a Web Developer at DataSoft LTD, and earlier Python internship experience at Global IT.', 1, '2026-04-28 00:00:00.000'),
(126, 'What achievements are available on the site?', 'The current achievement data includes Top Performer Recognition from Explo-IT, a Full-Stack Development Certificate from Programming Hero, and Hackathon Finalist recognition from a university innovation event.', 1, '2026-04-28 00:00:00.000'),
(127, 'Can the assistant answer package, price, quote, charge, budget, fee, and cost questions?', 'Yes. Those words all point to pricing intent. The assistant should treat package, plan, quote, cost, charge, fee, budget, rate, and estimate as related questions about pricing and project scope.', 1, '2026-04-28 00:00:00.000'),
(128, 'If someone asks about rates, fees, or charges, what should the assistant understand?', 'It should understand that the visitor is asking about pricing. The best answer is to mention the visible published plans when relevant and then explain that a final quote depends on the actual project scope.', 1, '2026-04-28 00:00:00.000'),
(129, 'If a visitor asks how much it will be, how should the assistant respond?', 'The assistant should explain that there are published reference plans on the site, but real project cost still depends on scope, timeline, complexity, and support requirements. It should then guide the visitor to share the brief.', 1, '2026-04-28 00:00:00.000'),
(130, 'What should the assistant do when pricing information is requested but the project is custom?', 'It should avoid inventing a fixed number. Instead, it should mention the visible plan structure and explain that custom builds need a tailored estimate after reviewing the requirements.', 1, '2026-04-28 00:00:00.000');
