Rex3j4y80PQ15A3RjFr_4TIR6lBRwBBmH6ekv8c_sm1NQquSvsBmYZux7_LWec-u5QUFHJuKnBP03kuXnDsH74XADhDKns9wFLS_gK4pLxXAKKern27IRm7NbtM-b_HiIAp_tcpuRW9yusuvfwJzavdkabh1MldjNPGhcbozlsk_1b0B5wk8gHg0MxVyzS5H113lFyS5njTP25pLFDvMGdws8v0LSJwQ4Adml6L31uoFj6LIZ88V3I6n3dtAU06ZOOG3W4yp5J1TP7=&ARFXYWk6vxI4Amn1IA5QSGpOz4cX=&trackingId=TQtw9tWRjt7AXmPT08RO1g%3D%3D&refId=9JHzBdMEw5HS%2FtEe8sk0WA%3D%3D&lipi=urn%3Ali%3Apage%3Aemail_email_job_alert_confirmation_01%3BIbk9PROhSVer41ROesr8JA%3D%3D&midToken=AQHw9rRSnl3Tiw&midSig=1jWAgvwgKaScg1&trk=eml-email_job_alert_confirmation_01-email_job_alert_confirmation-0-view_job&trkEmail=eml-email_job_alert_confirmation_01-email_job_alert_confirmation-0-view_job-null-s2og1v~mq0wep4j~59-null-null&eid=s2og1v-mq0wep4j-59&otpToken=MTMwMzE3ZTcxNzJiY2JjM2I0MjkwZmViNDExNmU3YjI4OWNjZDM0ODliYWU4NzZmN2JkYTA3NmM0ZjUyNThmYWYyZDVkMGU5NzJlMWMxZmQ0MGE2Y2Q5OWVhOWI3MDRmYWExNjhhYThiYjM5NTk3NDliNGU3MmFmLDEsMQ%3D%3D\"\n  },\n  \"recruiter\": null,\n  \"match\": null,\n  \"settings\": {\n    \"tone\": \"professional-natural\",\n    \"maxEmailWords\": 300,\n    \"maxCoverLetterWords\": 600,\n    \"attachCv\": true,\n    \"attachCoverLetterPdf\": true\n  }\n}', 'I am writing to express my interest in the Software Engineering position in Germany. With a strong foundation in full-stack development and a growing focus on autonomous systems and AI, I am well positioned to contribute to engineering teams working on modern, scalable applications.\n\nMy professional experience spans over four years of web and full-stack development. I have worked extensively with Laravel and Next.js to build production-grade applications, including multi-vendor e-commerce platforms, real-time dashboards, and AI-powered financial tools. On the backend, I design RESTful APIs with Node.js and Express, manage relational databases like MySQL and PostgreSQL, and implement secure authentication, role-based access control, and payment gateway integrations.\n\nOn the frontend, I build responsive, SEO-friendly interfaces using React, Next.js, TypeScript, and Tailwind CSS. I have delivered real-time features using WebSockets and Socket.IO, and deployed applications on Linux servers with Docker, Nginx, and CI/CD pipelines. My work at Explo-IT involved optimizing Eloquent queries, implementing caching strategies, and integrating third-party services such as cloud storage and social logins.\n\nIn addition to my technical experience, I work effectively across multidisciplinary teams and communicate clearly with both technical and non-technical stakeholders. I am fluent in Bengali and English, have working knowledge of Russian and Hindi, and enjoy collaborating in international and cross-cultural environments.\n\nI have attached my CV for your review. I would welcome the opportunity to discuss how my skills and experience align with your team\'s needs.\n\nBest regards,\nMd Shahanur Islam Shagor', '/uploads/job-agent/cover-letter-149-1780663591692.pdf', '/uploads/job-agent/cv/agent-cv-1780650102256-c81c423a75e8.pdf', 0, 'REJECTED', '', '2026-06-07 18:41:45.406', 'duplicate', 'pending', '', '', NULL),
(150, 146, 17, 'dmaurath@linkedin.com', 'Application for Fullstack Developer (TypeScript, Node.js/Bun, ETL, Next.js)', 'Hello Hiring Team,\n\nI am writing to express my interest in the Fullstack Developer position at your company.\n\nMy strongest match is with TypeScript, Node.js, and Next.js. I have built and deployed full-stack applications using these technologies, including REST APIs, authentication, and database integration with MySQL and MongoDB.\n\nIn my previous Web Developer roles, I delivered scalable web applications using Laravel and Next.js, built RESTful APIs, implemented role-based access control, and optimized database performance.\n\nOne relevant project is Smart Finance, a full-stack personal finance platform built with Next.js, TypeScript, Tailwind CSS, and Prisma ORM. It includes real-time updates via SSE, Docker deployment, and a modular architecture.\n\nI\'ve attached my CV and cover letter for your review.\n\nBest regards,\nMd Shahanur Islam Shagor', 'DRAFT', NULL, NULL, '', '2026-06-05 12:46:38.724', '2026-06-07 18:41:37.701', 'cmq0x4q6c0003ksp4qxeav27z', NULL, NULL, 0, NULL, 0, 'DEEPSEEK', 'deepseek-chat', 'Task: Create a highly customized professional job application email.\nReturn strict JSON only: {\"emailSubject\":\"...\",\"emailBody\":\"...\"}.\nRead the complete job description before writing. Identify job title, company, required skills, preferred skills, responsibilities, domain, seniority, work type, tools, and soft skills.\nCompare the job description with the candidate profile in the context. Mention only matching skills, responsibilities, and projects that are supported by the profile.\nDo not mention missing skills in the final email.\nSelect the strongest single positioning based on the job type. Web: Laravel, Next.js, React, JavaScript, HTML, CSS, Tailwind CSS, REST APIs, MySQL, responsive UI, web application development. Backend: Laravel, Node.js, REST APIs, GraphQL, MySQL, PostgreSQL, Redis, authentication, RBAC, API development. Frontend: React, Next.js, JavaScript, TypeScript, HTML, CSS, Tailwind CSS, Bootstrap, responsive UI, SEO-friendly interfaces. Full-stack: Laravel, Next.js, Node.js, React, REST APIs, MySQL, authentication, payment gateway integration, deployment, full application delivery. AI automation: Python, AI-based projects, automation, computer vision, workflow systems, API integration, practical software engineering. Go: use Go only when the job mentions Go, backend systems, decentralized systems, mesh networking, APIs, or high-concurrency systems. DevOps/server: Linux, Docker, Nginx, Apache, CI/CD, AWS, Google Cloud, deployment, monitoring, server maintenance.\nSubject format: Application for {jobTitle}.\nEmail body should be 90-140 words and never exceed 300 words.\nGreeting format: Hello {Company Name or Hiring Team}. Use recruiter name only if provided.\nFirst sentence: I am writing to express my interest in the {Job Title} position at {Company Name}.\nSecond paragraph should mention the strongest matched skill group and specific supported responsibilities from the job description.\nAdd one concise paragraph about previous Web Developer work only when it is relevant to the selected positioning.\nMention one relevant project from the provided profile if it clearly relates to the job. Do not invent project names.\nMention education briefly only if space allows.\nIf attachments are enabled, include this exact sentence: I\'ve attached my CV and cover letter for your review.\nSound confident, polite, and human.\nNo emojis.\nNo markdown tables.\nDo not mention missing skills, weak fit, uncertainty, or anything negative.\nAvoid generic AI phrases: I am excited to leverage; dynamic professional; synergy; passionate individual; fast-paced environment.\nFinal quality check before output: every mentioned skill exists in the profile, every mentioned project exists in the profile, every claim is supported, no fake company information is added, and the email is tailored to the job.\nContext:\n{\n  \"applicant\": {\n    \"name\": \"Hi there, I\'m Shagor\",\n    \"designation\": \"Full-Stack & AI Engineer\",\n    \"summary\": \"Hi, I\'m Shahanur Islam Shagor. I am a Software Engineer specializing in Full Stuck Web Development, Autonomous Systems and AI Engineering Enthusiast focused on building intelligent real-world technologies that combine software engineering, robotics, cybersecurity, and distributed autonomous systems.\\nI am passionate about designing intelligent systems capable of operating in complex real-world environments where AI, autonomy, and cybersecurity work together to solve advanced technological challenges.\",\n    \"email\": \"smshagor.ru@gmail.com\",\n    \"portfolio\": \"md_shahanurislamshagor_\",\n    \"cvUrl\": \"/uploads/job-agent/cv/agent-cv-1780650102256-c81c423a75e8.pdf\",\n    \"skills\": [\n      \"HTML\",\n      \"CSS\",\n      \"Javascript\",\n      \"Typescript\",\n      \"React\",\n      \"Next JS\",\n      \"Tailwind\",\n      \"MongoDB\",\n      \"MySQL\",\n      \"PostgreSQL\",\n      \"Git\",\n      \"AWS\",\n      \"Bootstrap\",\n      \"Docker\",\n      \"Go\",\n      \"Figma\",\n      \"Firebase\",\n      \"MaterialUI\",\n      \"Nginx\",\n      \"Strapi\",\n      \"PHP\",\n      \"Laravel\",\n      \"Express JS\",\n      \"Node JS\",\n      \"GraphQL\",\n      \"C++\",\n      \"C#\",\n      \"Vue JS\",\n      \"Angular JS\",\n      \"React Native\",\n      \"Linux\",\n      \"Apache\",\n      \"CI/CD\",\n      \"CMake\",\n      \"Flutter\",\n      \"Kotlin\",\n      \"Jetson Nano\",\n      \"Google Cloud\",\n      \"Digital Ocean\",\n      \"Kubernetes\",\n      \"Prometheus\",\n      \"Grafana\",\n      \"Jest\",\n      \"PHPUnit\",\n      \"PyTest\",\n      \"Redis\",\n      \"Socket.IO\",\n      \"Microservices\"\n    ],\n    \"education\": [\n      \"[object Object]\",\n      \"[object Object]\"\n    ],\n    \"experience\": [\n      \"[object Object]\",\n      \"[object Object]\",\n      \"[object Object]\"\n    ],\n    \"strongestProjects\": [\n      {},\n      {},\n      {}\n    ],\n    \"optionalNotes\": \"\",\n    \"sourceTablesUsed\": [\n      \"Profile\",\n      \"Skill\",\n      \"Education\",\n      \"Project\",\n      \"Experience\",\n      \"CvProfile optional notes\"\n    ]\n  },\n  \"job\": {\n    \"title\": \"Md Shahanur Islam: your job alert for Web Developer in Germany has been created\",\n    \"company\": \"Unknown company\",\n    \"location\": \"Fullstack Developer (Typescript, Node.js/Bun, ETL, Next.js)- hybrid- up to 70k\",\n    \"description\": \"\",\n    \"sourceUrl\": \"https://www.linkedin.com/comm/jobs/view/4418758448?alertAction=markasviewed&savedSearchId=5308500625&savedSearchAuthToken=1&AQFFPAbYLCczmwAAAZ6W2CU5YDXw2CdsfApgqRS7cDyqLea6NTT4vgX_uU0c1oTBkqVJ9JrMiiVoMgKO8_L165GngVlGeXDysBsEJDGBcgH60NVZqDOxP61RdsBaSBRFmrqjaj1YG0EfZoc7BSgHLQWe238sBHnEjBBO2AVaDRB-OqRWoqGJY3bqVNjhvbTNJKBGxfx35RQfHo4FPldVZxT4kePlWAFtsEymSS6AP2TY38BKqyBEb6e160py9hxkx1n2MjUOnguLulUSbCpciXu0cVjbY5HAU3478y0g8dfJBhFv_LGh5rKV=&AbfJv9rSKEAo9Cb9dZFJlzIJ37fm=&trackingId=R7CbVtTu3GEMIyFQ39NkJw%3D%3D&refId=6pPj8aWVN0z3ShEYi%2BkuVg%3D%3D&lipi=urn%3Ali%3Apage%3Aemail_email_job_alert_confirmation_01%3BAeQsQEtaTruax1jWNS2cpg%3D%3D&midToken=AQHw9rRSnl3Tiw&midSig=1z7dseeJEiScg1&trk=eml-email_job_alert_confirmation_01-email_job_alert_confirmation-0-view_job&trkEmail=eml-email_job_alert_confirmation_01-email_job_alert_confirmation-0-view_job-null-s2og1v~mq0s4e2g~4k-null-null&eid=s2og1v-mq0s4e2g-4k&otpToken=MTMwMzE3ZTcxNzJiY2JjM2I0MjkwZmViNDExNmU3YjI4YWNiZDE0ODlhYTc4NzY4N2JkYTA3NmM0ZjUyNThmYWYyZDVkMGU5MTFkN2I5ZmQ1OGFlZWJhNmU0MzRkZGRjMjk3YWRiOGIwMmVmMTI0NmYzNzY1OGQ0LDEsMQ%3D%3D\"\n  },\n  \"recruiter\": null,\n  \"match\": null,\n  \"settings\": {\n    \"tone\": \"professional-natural\",\n    \"maxEmailWords\": 300,\n    \"maxCoverLetterWords\": 600,\n    \"attachCv\": true,\n    \"attachCoverLetterPdf\": true\n  }\n}', 'Task: Write a customized cover letter for this job.\nReturn strict JSON only: {\"coverLetterText\":\"...\"}.\nGenerate only the body paragraphs for a PDF cover letter. Do not include applicant header, contact details, date, greeting line, signature, or footer because the PDF renderer adds those automatically.\nUse 4-5 polished paragraphs in the style of a senior, research-capable engineer.\nOpening should mention the role/company and direct interest.\nSelect ONLY ONE role category with the highest match from the job title and description. Do not combine web, drone, AI, cyber, backend, and Go into one generic paragraph.\nNever start the important technical paragraphs with: My background aligns with this opportunity; I am excited to apply; I believe I am a strong fit.\nNever reuse the same middle paragraphs across different job categories.\nNever reuse previously generated role paragraphs. Generate fresh wording for every application even when the role category remains the same.\nBefore writing, identify the company industry, product/service, mission, customers, and technical domain from the job description. If sufficient information exists, add one concrete sentence explaining why the company/product/domain is interesting. If company information is unavailable, skip this section completely. Do not invent company information.\nIf the job description explicitly emphasizes startup, fast-growing company, research-driven company, enterprise environment, remote-first culture, or customer-focused culture, add one sentence connecting the applicant\'s working style to that environment. Skip completely if culture is unclear. Never invent culture information.\nDetermine seniority from the job description: Intern, Junior, Mid-Level, Senior, Lead, Principal, or Director. Adjust tone accordingly.\nIntern/Junior: emphasize learning ability, education, projects, and hands-on development.\nMid-Level: emphasize implementation, ownership, and delivery.\nSenior: emphasize architecture, technical decisions, practical mentoring/context sharing, and scalability.\nLead: emphasize cross-team collaboration, project ownership, and technical leadership only if supported by the profile.\nPrincipal/Director: emphasize systems thinking, strategy, automation, process improvement, and business impact only where supported by the profile.\nNever claim leadership experience unless supported by the profile. Never claim management experience unless supported by the profile.\nBefore writing, identify technologies, tools, responsibilities, and domain keywords explicitly mentioned in the job description.\nInside the selected role category, prioritize only skills that appear in BOTH the job description and the candidate profile.\nDo not automatically mention all skills from the selected category. Maximum technical mentions: 4 primary technologies and 3 secondary technologies.\nIf a skill exists in the candidate profile but is not relevant to the job description, do not mention it. If a skill exists in the job description but is not present in the candidate profile, do not mention it.\nSelect one project dynamically by ranking overlap with job-description technologies, responsibilities, domain, and selected role category. Do not use a fixed project for a category. Do not force a project if no project clearly matches.\nBefore writing technical paragraphs, determine the evidence source: professional experience, research work, academic work, or project work. Use accurate wording: \'In my professional experience...\' for professional evidence; \'Through research and development work...\' for research evidence; \'Through hands-on project development...\' for academic/personal project evidence.\nNever present research work as professional industry experience. Never present academic or personal projects as paid professional experience.\nUse accurate experience duration by selected category. Web/full-stack/backend roles: 4 years of professional web/full-stack development experience. Drone/UAV/robotics roles: more than 1 year of drone, AI, and autonomous systems experience. AI/machine learning roles: more than 1 year of applied AI and machine learning experience. Cybersecurity roles: 2 years of cybersecurity and secure communications experience. General roles: mention the split naturally instead of saying four years across every domain.\nWEB/FULL-STACK category: emphasize Laravel, PHP, Next.js, React, JavaScript, TypeScript, HTML, CSS, Tailwind CSS, REST APIs, MySQL, authentication, payment integration, responsive UI, real-time features, and database optimization.\nBACKEND category: emphasize Laravel, Node.js, Go, APIs, authentication, RBAC, databases, Redis-aware architecture, GraphQL, and performance optimization.\nGO category: emphasize Go, high-concurrency systems, APIs, distributed systems, backend services, networking, secure communication workflows, and performance.\nAI/MACHINE LEARNING category: emphasize Python, AI engineering, computer vision, YOLOv8-style object detection, machine learning, deep learning, NLP fundamentals, data processing, automation, model evaluation, and production integration.\nCYBERSECURITY category: emphasize cybersecurity, OWASP, JWT, OAuth, blockchain, Zero-Knowledge Proofs, post-quantum cryptography, secure systems, privacy, resilience, and risk mitigation.\nDRONE/UAV/ROBOTICS category: emphasize UAV systems, autonomous navigation, sensor fusion, EKF, VIO, UWB TDOA, ROS, C++, Go, Python, localization, distributed coordination, and resilient navigation architectures.\nMiddle paragraphs must be role-specific: first technical paragraph should explain why the selected category fits; second technical paragraph should connect the job responsibilities to matching experience from only that selected category.\nThe two technical paragraphs are the most important part of the cover letter. Paragraph 1 should describe selected-category technical positioning. Paragraph 2 should connect selected-category responsibilities to APIs/UI/performance/scalability/database/deployment for web; architecture/APIs/security/reliability for backend; distributed systems/performance for Go; real-world deployment and automation impact for AI/ML; privacy/resilience/risk mitigation for cybersecurity; or localization/coordination/navigation/deployment for drone/UAV/robotics.\nAfter the technical section, add this communication paragraph adapted naturally: In addition to my technical experience, I work effectively across multidisciplinary teams and communicate clearly with both technical and non-technical stakeholders. I am fluent in Bengali and English, have working knowledge of Russian and Hindi, and enjoy collaborating in international and cross-cultural environments.\nClosing should be polite and mention the attached CV if available.\nKeep it recruiter-friendly and ATS-friendly.\nKeep it under 600 words.\nPrefer natural human wording.\nVary sentence structure. Do not start every paragraph with \'I have\', \'My experience\', or \'This role\'. Mix natural starts such as \'Through...\', \'In previous work...\', \'One area that particularly interests me...\', \'A relevant example is...\', and \'What stands out to me...\'.\nNo markdown.\nUse plain text paragraphs separated by blank lines.\nNo fake achievements.\nDo not invent facts. Do not exaggerate. Do not mention missing skills negatively.\nAvoid generic filler and AI-style language.\nNever use these buzzwords: passionate, dynamic professional, leverage, synergy, fast-paced environment, cutting-edge, world-class, best-in-class, highly motivated.\nContext:\n{\n  \"applicant\": {\n    \"name\": \"Hi there, I\'m Shagor\",\n    \"designation\": \"Full-Stack & AI Engineer\",\n    \"summary\": \"Hi, I\'m Shahanur Islam Shagor. I am a Software Engineer specializing in Full Stuck Web Development, Autonomous Systems and AI Engineering Enthusiast focused on building intelligent real-world technologies that combine software engineering, robotics, cybersecurity, and distributed autonomous systems.\\nI am passionate about designing intelligent systems capable of operating in complex real-world environments where AI, autonomy, and cybersecurity work together to solve advanced technological challenges.\",\n    \"email\": \"smshagor.ru@gmail.com\",\n    \"portfolio\": \"md_shahanurislamshagor_\",\n    \"cvUrl\": \"/uploads/job-agent/cv/agent-cv-1780650102256-c81c423a75e8.pdf\",\n    \"skills\": [\n      \"HTML\",\n      \"CSS\",\n      \"Javascript\",\n      \"Typescript\",\n      \"React\",\n      \"Next JS\",\n      \"Tailwind\",\n      \"MongoDB\",\n      \"MySQL\",\n      \"PostgreSQL\",\n      \"Git\",\n      \"AWS\",\n      \"Bootstrap\",\n      \"Docker\",\n      \"Go\",\n      \"Figma\",\n      \"Firebase\",\n      \"MaterialUI\",\n      \"Nginx\",\n      \"Strapi\",\n      \"PHP\",\n      \"Laravel\",\n      \"Express JS\",\n      \"Node JS\",\n      \"GraphQL\",\n      \"C++\",\n      \"C#\",\n      \"Vue JS\",\n      \"Angular JS\",\n      \"React Native\",\n      \"Linux\",\n      \"Apache\",\n      \"CI/CD\",\n      \"CMake\",\n      \"Flutter\",\n      \"Kotlin\",\n      \"Jetson Nano\",\n      \"Google Cloud\",\n      \"Digital Ocean\",\n      \"Kubernetes\",\n      \"Prometheus\",\n      \"Grafana\",\n      \"Jest\",\n      \"PHPUnit\",\n      \"PyTest\",\n      \"Redis\",\n      \"Socket.IO\",\n      \"Microservices\"\n    ],\n    \"education\": [\n      \"[object Object]\",\n      \"[object Object]\"\n    ],\n    \"experience\": [\n      \"[object Object]\",\n      \"[object Object]\",\n      \"[object Object]\"\n    ],\n    \"strongestProjects\": [\n      {},\n      {},\n      {}\n    ],\n    \"optionalNotes\": \"\",\n    \"sourceTablesUsed\": [\n      \"Profile\",\n      \"Skill\",\n      \"Education\",\n      \"Project\",\n      \"Experience\",\n      \"CvProfile optional notes\"\n    ]\n  },\n  \"job\": {\n    \"title\": \"Md Shahanur Islam: your job alert for Web Developer in Germany has been created\",\n    \"company\": \"Unknown company\",\n    \"location\": \"Fullstack Developer (Typescript, Node.js/Bun, ETL, Next.js)- hybrid- up to 70k\",\n    \"description\": \"\",\n    \"sourceUrl\": \"https://www.linkedin.com/comm/jobs/view/4418758448?alertAction=markasviewed&savedSearchId=5308500625&savedSearchAuthToken=1&AQFFPAbYLCczmwAAAZ6W2CU5YDXw2CdsfApgqRS7cDyqLea6NTT4vgX_uU0c1oTBkqVJ9JrMiiVoMgKO8_L165GngVlGeXDysBsEJDGBcgH60NVZqDOxP61RdsBaSBRFmrqjaj1YG0EfZoc7BSgHLQWe238sBHnEjBBO2AVaDRB-OqRWoqGJY3bqVNjhvbTNJKBGxfx35RQfHo4FPldVZxT4kePlWAFtsEymSS6AP2TY38BKqyBEb6e160py9hxkx1n2MjUOnguLulUSbCpciXu0cVjbY5HAU3478y0g8dfJBhFv_LGh5rKV=&AbfJv9rSKEAo9Cb9dZFJlzIJ37fm=&trackingId=R7CbVtTu3GEMIyFQ39NkJw%3D%3D&refId=6pPj8aWVN0z3ShEYi%2BkuVg%3D%3D&lipi=urn%3Ali%3Apage%3Aemail_email_job_alert_confirmation_01%3BAeQsQEtaTruax1jWNS2cpg%3D%3D&midToken=AQHw9rRSnl3Tiw&midSig=1z7dseeJEiScg1&trk=eml-email_job_alert_confirmation_01-email_job_alert_confirmation-0-view_job&trkEmail=eml-email_job_alert_confirmation_01-email_job_alert_confirmation-0-view_job-null-s2og1v~mq0s4e2g~4k-null-null&eid=s2og1v-mq0s4e2g-4k&otpToken=MTMwMzE3ZTcxNzJiY2JjM2I0MjkwZmViNDExNmU3YjI4YWNiZDE0ODlhYTc4NzY4N2JkYTA3NmM0ZjUyNThmYWYyZDVkMGU5MTFkN2I5ZmQ1OGFlZWJhNmU0MzRkZGRjMjk3YWRiOGIwMmVmMTI0NmYzNzY1OGQ0LDEsMQ%3D%3D\"\n  },\n  \"recruiter\": null,\n  \"match\": null,\n  \"settings\": {\n    \"tone\": \"professional-natural\",\n    \"maxEmailWords\": 300,\n    \"maxCoverLetterWords\": 600,\n    \"attachCv\": true,\n    \"attachCoverLetterPdf\": true\n  }\n}', 'I am writing to apply for the Fullstack Developer position. With professional experience in TypeScript, Node.js, and Next.js, I build scalable full-stack applications that handle real-world complexity.\n\nIn my work as a Web Developer, I have delivered production applications using TypeScript, Node.js, and Next.js. I have built RESTful APIs, implemented authentication and role-based access control, and worked with both SQL and NoSQL databases. I also have experience with ETL-like data processing and real-time features using WebSockets and Socket.IO.\n\nOne project that reflects this is Smart Finance, a full-stack personal finance platform built with Next.js 16, TypeScript, Tailwind CSS, and Prisma ORM. It features 16 finance modules, real-time updates via Server-Sent Events, Docker-based deployment, and a modular architecture that reduced code duplication. I designed the API integration pattern and state management approach myself.\n\nIn addition to my technical experience, I work effectively across multidisciplinary teams and communicate clearly with both technical and non-technical stakeholders. I am fluent in Bengali and English, have working knowledge of Russian and Hindi, and enjoy collaborating in international and cross-cultural environments.\n\nI have attached my CV for your review. I would welcome the opportunity to discuss how my background aligns with your team\'s needs.', '/uploads/job-agent/cover-letter-150-1780663598727.pdf', '/uploads/job-agent/cv/agent-cv-1780650102256-c81c423a75e8.pdf', 0, 'REJECTED', '', '2026-06-07 18:41:37.700', 'duplicate', 'pending', '', '', NULL);
INSERT INTO `job_email_drafts` (`id`, `jobPostId`, `recruiterContactId`, `toEmail`, `subject`, `body`, `status`, `approvedAt`, `sentAt`, `providerMessageId`, `createdAt`, `updatedAt`, `trackingId`, `openedAt`, `lastOpenedAt`, `openCount`, `clickedAt`, `clickCount`, `aiProvider`, `aiModel`, `emailPromptUsed`, `coverLetterPromptUsed`, `coverLetterText`, `coverLetterPdfUrl`, `cvUrl`, `adminApprovalRequired`, `approvalStatus`, `approvedBy`, `rejectedAt`, `rejectionReason`, `sendStatus`, `skipReason`, `errorMessage`, `lastSendAttemptAt`) VALUES
(151, 147, 15, 'dmaurath@linkedin.com', 'Application for Web Developer Position', 'Hello Hiring Team,\n\nI am writing to express my interest in the Web Developer position in Germany.\n\nI have over 4 years of professional experience building responsive, SEO-friendly web applications using Laravel, Next.js, React, TypeScript, and Tailwind CSS. My work includes developing RESTful APIs, implementing authentication and role-based access control, and optimizing database performance with MySQL and PostgreSQL.\n\nIn my previous role at Explo-IT, I delivered scalable web applications end-to-end, integrated real-time features with WebSockets, and deployed production systems on Linux servers with Docker and CI/CD pipelines.\n\nI\'ve attached my CV and cover letter for your review.\n\nBest regards,\nMd Shahanur Islam Shagor', 'DRAFT', NULL, NULL, '', '2026-06-05 12:46:45.434', '2026-06-07 18:41:29.654', 'cmq0x4vcp0005ksp4nnkio7hu', NULL, NULL, 0, NULL, 0, 'DEEPSEEK', 'deepseek-chat', 'Task: Create a highly customized professional job application email.\nReturn strict JSON only: {\"emailSubject\":\"...\",\"emailBody\":\"...\"}.\nRead the complete job description before writing. Identify job title, company, required skills, preferred skills, responsibilities, domain, seniority, work type, tools, and soft skills.\nCompare the job description with the candidate profile in the context. Mention only matching skills, responsibilities, and projects that are supported by the profile.\nDo not mention missing skills in the final email.\nSelect the strongest single positioning based on the job type. Web: Laravel, Next.js, React, JavaScript, HTML, CSS, Tailwind CSS, REST APIs, MySQL, responsive UI, web application development. Backend: Laravel, Node.js, REST APIs, GraphQL, MySQL, PostgreSQL, Redis, authentication, RBAC, API development. Frontend: React, Next.js, JavaScript, TypeScript, HTML, CSS, Tailwind CSS, Bootstrap, responsive UI, SEO-friendly interfaces. Full-stack: Laravel, Next.js, Node.js, React, REST APIs, MySQL, authentication, payment gateway integration, deployment, full application delivery. AI automation: Python, AI-based projects, automation, computer vision, workflow systems, API integration, practical software engineering. Go: use Go only when the job mentions Go, backend systems, decentralized systems, mesh networking, APIs, or high-concurrency systems. DevOps/server: Linux, Docker, Nginx, Apache, CI/CD, AWS, Google Cloud, deployment, monitoring, server maintenance.\nSubject format: Application for {jobTitle}.\nEmail body should be 90-140 words and never exceed 300 words.\nGreeting format: Hello {Company Name or Hiring Team}. Use recruiter name only if provided.\nFirst sentence: I am writing to express my interest in the {Job Title} position at {Company Name}.\nSecond paragraph should mention the strongest matched skill group and specific supported responsibilities from the job description.\nAdd one concise paragraph about previous Web Developer work only when it is relevant to the selected positioning.\nMention one relevant project from the provided profile if it clearly relates to the job. Do not invent project names.\nMention education briefly only if space allows.\nIf attachments are enabled, include this exact sentence: I\'ve attached my CV and cover letter for your review.\nSound confident, polite, and human.\nNo emojis.\nNo markdown tables.\nDo not mention missing skills, weak fit, uncertainty, or anything negative.\nAvoid generic AI phrases: I am excited to leverage; dynamic professional; synergy; passionate individual; fast-paced environment.\nFinal quality check before output: every mentioned skill exists in the profile, every mentioned project exists in the profile, every claim is supported, no fake company information is added, and the email is tailored to the job.\nContext:\n{\n  \"applicant\": {\n    \"name\": \"Hi there, I\'m Shagor\",\n    \"designation\": \"Full-Stack & AI Engineer\",\n    \"summary\": \"Hi, I\'m Shahanur Islam Shagor. I am a Software Engineer specializing in Full Stuck Web Development, Autonomous Systems and AI Engineering Enthusiast focused on building intelligent real-world technologies that combine software engineering, robotics, cybersecurity, and distributed autonomous systems.\\nI am passionate about designing intelligent systems capable of operating in complex real-world environments where AI, autonomy, and cybersecurity work together to solve advanced technological challenges.\",\n    \"email\": \"smshagor.ru@gmail.com\",\n    \"portfolio\": \"md_shahanurislamshagor_\",\n    \"cvUrl\": \"/uploads/job-agent/cv/agent-cv-1780650102256-c81c423a75e8.pdf\",\n    \"skills\": [\n      \"HTML\",\n      \"CSS\",\n      \"Javascript\",\n      \"Typescript\",\n      \"React\",\n      \"Next JS\",\n      \"Tailwind\",\n      \"MongoDB\",\n      \"MySQL\",\n      \"PostgreSQL\",\n      \"Git\",\n      \"AWS\",\n      \"Bootstrap\",\n      \"Docker\",\n      \"Go\",\n      \"Figma\",\n      \"Firebase\",\n      \"MaterialUI\",\n      \"Nginx\",\n      \"Strapi\",\n      \"PHP\",\n      \"Laravel\",\n      \"Express JS\",\n      \"Node JS\",\n      \"GraphQL\",\n      \"C++\",\n      \"C#\",\n      \"Vue JS\",\n      \"Angular JS\",\n      \"React Native\",\n      \"Linux\",\n      \"Apache\",\n      \"CI/CD\",\n      \"CMake\",\n      \"Flutter\",\n      \"Kotlin\",\n      \"Jetson Nano\",\n      \"Google Cloud\",\n      \"Digital Ocean\",\n      \"Kubernetes\",\n      \"Prometheus\",\n      \"Grafana\",\n      \"Jest\",\n      \"PHPUnit\",\n      \"PyTest\",\n      \"Redis\",\n      \"Socket.IO\",\n      \"Microservices\"\n    ],\n    \"education\": [\n      \"[object Object]\",\n      \"[object Object]\"\n    ],\n    \"experience\": [\n      \"[object Object]\",\n      \"[object Object]\",\n      \"[object Object]\"\n    ],\n    \"strongestProjects\": [\n      {},\n      {},\n      {}\n    ],\n    \"optionalNotes\": \"\",\n    \"sourceTablesUsed\": [\n      \"Pro