(309, 309, 1, 5, '[\"Go\"]', '[\"Spanish teaching experience\",\"ELE certification\",\"Teaching qualification\"]', 'The applicant is a software engineer with no teaching experience or Spanish language teaching qualifications. The job requires a Spanish teacher with at least one year of experience and relevant training. The match is very low.', '{\"generatedBy\":\"job-agent-ai\",\"provider\":\"DEEPSEEK\",\"model\":\"deepseek-chat\",\"mocked\":false,\"errors\":[],\"profileContextSourceTablesUsed\":[\"Profile\",\"Skill\",\"Education\",\"Project\",\"Experience\",\"CvProfile optional notes\"],\"profileContextMissingFields\":[]}', 'I am writing to express my interest in the Profesor/a de Español (ELE) position at Apprentus. Although my professional background is in software engineering, I have always enjoyed teaching and working with people from different cultures. I am confident that my communication skills and experience in multilingual environments will allow me to connect with students and deliver effective Spanish lessons.\n\nI have strong verbal and written communication skills, developed through years of collaborating with international teams and clients. I am fluent in Bengali and English, and I have working knowledge of Russian and Hindi. This multilingual experience gives me a practical understanding of the challenges language learners face, and I am patient and adaptable when explaining concepts to others.\n\nIn addition to my technical work, I have experience mentoring junior developers and helping them learn new technologies. I enjoy breaking down complex topics into simple, understandable steps and tailoring my approach to each individual\'s learning style. I believe this same approach will translate well into teaching Spanish to students of varying levels.\n\nI am organized, reliable, and comfortable working with flexible schedules. I understand the importance of creating a supportive and encouraging learning environment, and I am committed to helping stude