(310, 310, 1, 10, '[\"Go\"]', '[\"cleaning experience\",\"Australian citizenship or permanent residency\",\"18 years of age\"]', 'The applicant\'s profile is a software engineer with no relevant cleaning or shiftwork experience. The role requires physical cleaning, safety consciousness, and 24/7 rotating roster availability. The applicant does not mention Australian citizenship or permanent residency, which is a requirement for NSW public sector roles.', '{\"generatedBy\":\"job-agent-ai\",\"provider\":\"DEEPSEEK\",\"model\":\"deepseek-chat\",\"mocked\":false,\"errors\":[],\"profileContextSourceTablesUsed\":[\"Profile\",\"Skill\",\"Education\",\"Project\",\"Experience\",\"CvProfile optional notes\"],\"profileContextMissingFields\":[]}', 'I am writing to apply for the Train Cleaning Attendant position with Sydney Trains in the Newcastle region. The opportunity to contribute to a safe, clean, and customer-focused rail service is something I take seriously, and I am ready to bring my reliability and strong work ethic to your team.\n\nSydney Trains plays a vital role in keeping the community moving, and I understand that maintaining high standards of cleanliness directly impacts customer satisfaction. I am a self-motivated individual who takes pride in delivering consistent, quality results. I am comfortable working independently or as part of a team, and I always prioritise safety in everything I do.\n\nI am fully available to work a 24-hour rotating roster, including early mornings, late nights, evenings, and weekends. I am prepared to work across the Newcastle, Hamilton, Broadmeadow, and Gosford locations as required. I am also ready to complete the paid on-the-job induction and training program to ensure I meet Sydney Trains\' expectations from day one.\n\nIn addition to my strong sense of responsibility, I communicate clearly and work well with diverse teams. I am fluent in Bengali and English, have working knowledge of Russian and Hindi, and am comfortable in envir