(1016, 1016, 1, 35, '[\"AWS\",\"Docker\",\"Nginx\",\"Git\",\"Linux\",\"CI/CD\",\"TypeScript\",\"JavaScript\",\"Node JS\",\"Express JS\",\"MongoDB\",\"OpenAI API\",\"REST API\"]', '[\"Financial data domain experience\",\"Sales or customer success experience\",\"Enterprise SaaS implementation experience\",\"Equity research or company filings knowledge\"]', 'The applicant has strong technical skills in full-stack development and AI integration, with a relevant project building an AI-powered financial application. However, the role is primarily a customer-facing, sales-adjacent position focused on financial data products, requiring domain expertise in equity research, company filings, and enterprise SaaS implementation. The technical foundation is present, but the core responsibilities of the role do not align closely with the applicant\'s background.', '{\"generatedBy\":\"job-agent-ai\",\"provider\":\"DEEPSEEK\",\"model\":\"deepseek-chat\",\"mocked\":false,\"errors\":[],\"profileContextSourceTablesUsed\":[\"Profile\",\"Skill\",\"Education\",\"Project\",\"Experience\",\"CvProfile optional notes\"],\"profileContextMissingFields\":[]}', 'I am writing to apply for the Financial Data Application Specialist Corporate role at AlphaSense. Your platform\'s mission to deliver AI-driven market intelligence to over 6,000 enterprise customers, including a majority of the S&P 500, is impressive. The opportunity to work at the intersection of technical implementation, customer success, and product strategy is exactly the kind of challenge I am looking for.\n\nThrough my professional experience, I have built full-stack applications with a strong focus on AI integration and financial data processing. One project involved developing an AI-powered financial mobile application where I designed the entire API using Express, TypeScript, and MongoDB. The system integrated OpenAI assistants trained on custom datasets, converted voice messages to text using AWS Transcribe, and automatically generated PDF term sheets from Google Sheets data. This required close collaboration with stakeholders to understand business workflows and translate them into technical solutions.\n\nWhat stands out to me about this role is the entrepreneurial nature of the team. You are building a new function at AlphaSense, and the expectation is to use client discussions to shape both go-to-market and product strategies. In my previous work, I have consistently operated in environments where feedback loops between clients and engineering were essential. I am comfortable communicating with technical and non-technical audiences and translating product needs into actionable implementation plans.\n\nIn addition to my technical experience, I work effectively across multidisciplinary teams and communicate clearly with both technical and non-technical stakeholders. I am fluent in Bengali and English, have working knowledge of Russian and Hindi, and enjoy collaborating in international and cross-cultural environments.\n\nI have attached my CV for your review and would welcome the opportunity to discuss how my background in AI-powered financial applications and full-stack development can contribute to AlphaSense\'s growing financial data products team.', '2026-06-17 01:46:02.191', '2026-06-17 01:46:02.191'),
(1017, 1017, 1, 15, '[\"Communication\",\"Problem Solving\",\"Project Management\"]', '[\"Medical Devices experience (7+ years)\",\"Government tenders and contracts experience\",\"GEM understanding\",\"Trade/retail market exposure\",\"Capital selling experience\",\"Brand Positioning Strategy\",\"Competitive Landscape Analysis\",\"Compliance Management\",\"Customer Centricity\",\"Customer Experience Management\",\"Incentive Policy, Procedures, and Quotas\",\"Industry Analysis\",\"Market Opportunity Assessment\",\"Profit and Loss (P&L) Management\",\"Sales Prospecting\",\"Strategic Sales Planning\",\"Strategic Thinking\",\"Sustainable Procurement\",\"Vendor Selection\"]', 'The applicant is a Full-Stack & AI Engineer with strong communication, problem-solving, and project management skills. However, the role requires 7+ years of medical device sales experience, government tenders, GEM knowledge, and specific sales competencies that are not present in the applicant\'s profile. The match is very low.', '{\"generatedBy\":\"job-agent-ai\",\"provider\":\"DEEPSEEK\",\"model\":\"deepseek-chat\",\"mocked\":false,\"errors\":[],\"profileContextSourceTablesUsed\":[\"Profile\",\"Skill\",\"Education\",\"Project\",\"Experience\",\"CvProfile optional notes\"],\"profileContextMissingFields\":[]}', 'I am writing to apply for the Regional Sales Manager position at Johnson & Johnson MedTech in Lucknow. Your company\'s commitment to healthcare innovation and improving patient outcomes through MedTech solutions is something I find genuinely compelling.\n\nWhile my professional background is in software engineering rather than medical device sales, I bring transferable strengths that align with this role. Through my experience delivering complex web applications, I have developed strong project management skills, the ability to analyze competitive landscapes, and a disciplined approach to problem-solving. I am comfortable working with data to identify opportunities and adjust strategies to meet objectives.\n\nOne area that particularly interests me is the customer-centric focus of this position. In my previous work, I collaborated directly with clients and stakeholders to understand their needs, translate requirements into actionable plans, and ensure satisfaction with the final outcome. I am confident these communication and relationship-building skills will serve me well in developing long-term partnerships with healthcare professionals and retailers.\n\nIn addition to my technical experience, I work effectively across multidisciplinary teams and communicate clearly with both technical and non-technical stakeholders. I am fluent in Bengali and English, have working knowledge of Russian and Hindi, and enjoy collaborating in international and cross-cultural environments.\n\nI have attached my CV for your review and would welcome the opportunity to discuss how my skills and approach can contribute to the Ethicon Endo Surgery team in Lucknow.', '2026-06-17 01:46:10.558', '2026-06-17 01:46:10.558'),
(1018, 1018, 1, 20, '[\"Go\"]', '[]', 'The job description is a generic AI company overview with no specific technical requirements. The applicant has AI engineering experience and relevant projects, but without clear job requirements, a precise match cannot be determined.', '{\"generatedBy\":\"job-agent-ai\",\"provider\":\"DEEPSEEK\",\"model\":\"deepseek-chat\",\"mocked\":false,\"errors\":[],\"profileContextSourceTablesUsed\":[\"Profile\",\"Skill\",\"Education\",\"Project\",\"Experience\",\"CvProfile optional notes\"],\"profileContextMissingFields\":[]}', 'I am writing to express my interest in the TEST Australia position at Faculty. Your focus on human-centric AI and responsible deployment resonates with my own approach to building intelligent systems that deliver measurable real-world impact.\n\nThrough research and development work, I have built AI-powered applications that combine modern machine learning models with practical software engineering. One area that particularly interests me is deploying AI systems that work reliably in production environments, not just in controlled settings. My work on the Wireless Vision-Aid for the Blind involved building a real-time object detection pipeline using YOLOv8n on edge hardware, processing video streams locally with ultra-low latency and providing multilingual audio feedback. This project required integrating computer vision, embedded systems, and real-time communication into a single offline-capable system.\n\nIn previous work, I developed an AI-powered financial application that used OpenAI\'s latest models for intelligent assistance, integrated AWS Transcribe for voice-to-text conversion, and automated PDF generation and email delivery through AWS SES. I also built an AI-powered real estate platform that combined Replicate API for image processing with role-based authentication, subscription plans, and Stripe payment integration. These projects required designing scalable API architectures, managing cloud infrastructure, and ensuring reliable performance under real usage conditions.\n\nIn addition to my technical experience, I work effectively across multidisciplinary teams and communicate clearly with both technical and non-technical stakeholders. I am fluent in Bengali and English, have working knowledge of Russian and Hindi, and enjoy collaborating in international and cross-cultural environments.\n\nI have attached my CV for your review and would welcome the opportunity to discuss how my background can contribute to Faculty\'s mission of building responsible AI that moves the needle.', '2026-06-17 01:46:17.471', '2026-06-17 01:46:17.471'),
(1019, 1019, 1, 62, '[\"Typescript\",\"Next JS\",\"PostgreSQL\",\"React\",\"Node JS\",\"AWS\",\"Docker\",\"Linux\",\"Nginx\",\"Git\",\"HTML\",\"CSS\",\"Tailwind\",\"Bootstrap\",\"Javascript\",\"Vue JS\",\"CI/CD\"]', '[\"Electron\",\"iOS native development\",\"Retool\",\"Typeform\",\"Airtable\"]', 'Strong match on the engineering side: TypeScript, Next.js, PostgreSQL, React, and deployment experience. The role also requires design sensibility and product thinking, which are not explicitly detailed in the profile. Missing Electron, iOS native, and some specific tools (Retool, Typeform, Airtable).', '{\"generatedBy\":\"job-agent-ai\",\"provider\":\"DEEPSEEK\",\"model\":\"deepseek-chat\",\"mocked\":false,\"errors\":[],\"profileContextSourceTablesUsed\":[\"Profile\",\"Skill\",\"Education\",\"Project\",\"Experience\",\"CvProfile optional notes\"],\"profileContextMissingFields\":[]}', 'I am writing to apply for the Design Engineer role at USB Club. The idea of building a sneaker net for artists, DJs, and researchers is genuinely interesting, and I appreciate the focus on both product design and engineering.\n\nMy background is in full-stack web development with a strong emphasis on Next.js, TypeScript, and PostgreSQL. Your engineering stack aligns well with what I work with daily, and I am comfortable owning features from concept to deployment without heavy oversight. I also have experience with Laravel, React, and Node.js, and I have deployed applications on AWS and Linux servers.\n\nOne area that particularly interests me is the planned migration from Vue to Next.js. I have built multiple production applications using Next.js with TypeScript, including a travel agency platform that supports multi-language and multi-currency features, and a personal finance dashboard with real-time updates and role-based access. I am confident I can contribute to that migration and help shape the web experience.\n\nIn addition to my technical experience, I work effectively across multidis