(1631, 1633, 1, 15, '[\"C++\",\"Python\",\"Linux\"]', '[\"Siemens S7 / TIA Portal\",\"Beckhoff TwinCAT 3\",\"Automatisierungstechnik\",\"Elektrotechnik\"]', 'The applicant has foundational programming skills (C++, Python) and experience with embedded systems and Linux, but lacks the specific SPS programming expertise (Siemens S7/TIA Portal, Beckhoff TwinCAT 3) and formal automation/electrical engineering qualification required for this role.', '{\"generatedBy\":\"job-agent-ai\",\"provider\":\"DEEPSEEK\",\"model\":\"deepseek-chat\",\"mocked\":false,\"errors\":[],\"profileContextSourceTablesUsed\":[\"Profile\",\"Skill\",\"Education\",\"Project\",\"Experience\",\"CvProfile optional notes\"],\"profileContextMissingFields\":[]}', 'I am writing to apply for the SPS-Programmierer position at SRT Echterhoff GmbH. Your company\'s long-standing expertise in planning and implementing control systems for machine and plant engineering is impressive, and I am interested in contributing to your team.\n\nThrough my work in embedded systems and automation, I have developed practical experience in programming and adapting control logic for hardware systems. I have worked with C++ and Python to build real-time data processing pipelines and communication protocols for devices like Raspberry Pi and ESP32 microcontrollers. This background in low-level system programming and hardware-software integration provides a solid foundation for developing and commissioning SPS programs.\n\nOne area that particularly interests me is adapting existing programs for retrofits and service operations. In a recent project, I built a wireless vision-aid system that required modifying object detection pipelines and streaming protocols to work reliably under different hardware configurations. This involved testing, debugging, and fine-tuning system behavior, similar to the adaptability needed when adjusting SPS programs for machine modifications.\n\nIn addition to my technical experience, I work effectively