(1985, 1987, 1, 45, '[\"Grafana\",\"Prometheus\",\"Docker\",\"Linux\",\"Nginx\",\"CI/CD\",\"AWS\",\"Google Cloud\",\"MySQL\",\"PostgreSQL\",\"Node.js\",\"Express.js\",\"Socket.IO\",\"Git\"]', '[\"Datadog\",\"Splunk\",\"IT strategy consulting experience\",\"German language\",\"Experience in vendor-neutral consulting\"]', 'The applicant has practical experience with Grafana, Prometheus, and Docker-based monitoring systems, and has built a real-time server health monitoring dashboard. However, the role requires senior-level IT strategy consulting experience, vendor-neutral advisory skills, and familiarity with enterprise monitoring tools like Datadog and Splunk, which are not demonstrated in the profile. The match is partial and best suited for a technical advisory or implementation role rather than pure strategy consulting.', '{\"generatedBy\":\"job-agent-ai\",\"provider\":\"DEEPSEEK\",\"model\":\"deepseek-chat\",\"mocked\":false,\"errors\":[],\"profileContextSourceTablesUsed\":[\"Profile\",\"Skill\",\"Education\",\"Project\",\"Experience\",\"CvProfile optional notes\"],\"profileContextMissingFields\":[]}', 'I am writing to apply for the Senior IT Strategy Consultant – Monitoring & Observability position at Wavestone Germany AG. The opportunity to help a major industrial company assess its current monitoring practices and define a forward-looking target architecture aligns well with my technical background and analytical approach.\n\nThrough hands-on project development, I have built a real-time server health monitoring dashboard that tracks availability, latency, and system metrics across multiple target URLs. The system uses Node.js and Express for the backend, streams live data to the browser via Socket.IO, and includes role-based access control. I deployed it with Docker and Nginx in a fully containerized production setup. This experience gives me practical familiarity with the kind of monitoring and observability tools that are central to this engagement.\n\nIn addition to Grafana and Prometheus, I have worked extensively with Linux server administration, Docker, Nginx, and CI/CD pipelines. My broad IT overview spans full-stack development, cloud infrastructure on AWS and Google Cloud, and database management with MySQL and PostgreSQL. This breadth allows me to evaluate solutions from multiple providers without bias toward any specific technology stack.\n\nIn addition to my technical experience, I work effectively across multidisciplinary teams and communicate clearly with both technical and non-technical stakeholders. I am fluent in Bengali and English, have working knowledge of Russian and Hindi, and enjoy collaborating in international and cross-cultural environments.\n\nI have attached my CV for your review and would welcome the opportunity to discuss how my experience can contribute to this project.\n\nBest regards,\nMd Shahanur Islam Shagor', '2026-07-01 13:41:18.181', '2026-07-01 13:41:18.181'),
(1986, 1988, 1, 15, '[\"Git\"]', '[\"History or related field of study\",\"German language proficiency\",\"CRM system experience\",\"Journalistic or editorial writing experience\",\"Library management experience\"]', 'The applicant is a Software Engineering student with strong organizational and data management skills, but the job requires enrollment in History or a related field, German language proficiency, and experience with CRM systems and editorial work. The technical skills do not directly match the backoffice and research focus of this role.', '{\"generatedBy\":\"job-agent-ai\",\"provider\":\"DEEPSEEK\",\"model\":\"deepseek-chat\",\"mocked\":false,\"errors\":[],\"profileContextSourceTablesUsed\":[\"Profile\",\"Skill\",\"Education\",\"Project\",\"Experience\",\"CvProfile optional notes\"],\"profileContextMissingFields\":[]}', 'I am writing to apply for the Studentische Hilfskraft Backoffice & Recherche position at Geschichtsbüro Reder / Köln. As a Software Engineering student at Voronezh State University, I bring strong organizational skills, careful attention to detail, and a methodical approach to research and data management.\n\nThe role involves literature research, library management, CRM data entry, and supporting outreach efforts. These tasks require precision and reliability. In my academic work, I have developed a habit of working carefully with databases and structured information. I understand that accuracy in research and data handling is essential, especially when supporting projects that document company and family histories.\n\nWhat stands out to me about Geschichtsbüro Reder is the opportunity to apply my organizational skills in a context where history is communicated across multiple media forms. I appreciate the blend of backoffice structure with creative storytelling, and I am interested in contributing to projects that make history accessible and engaging.\n\nIn addition to my technical and organizational experience, I work effectively acr