(2056, 2058, 1, 35, '[\"HTML\",\"CSS\",\"Javascript\",\"React\",\"Next JS\",\"Tailwind\",\"Git\",\"Bootstrap\",\"Figma\"]', '[\"MS Excel\",\"PowerPoint\",\"Power BI\",\"German language (very good)\",\"Student of Economics/Marketing/Communication/Media/Data Analytics\",\"Food/Cooking/Lifestyle interest\"]', 'The applicant has relevant technical skills for creating landing pages and product content (HTML, CSS, React, Next.js, Tailwind, Figma) and experience building web applications. However, the role requires a current student in a business/marketing/communication field, very good German language skills, and proficiency in MS Excel/PowerPoint/Power BI, which are not present in the applicant\'s profile. The match is partial, focusing on the content creation and landing page aspects of the role.', '{\"generatedBy\":\"job-agent-ai\",\"provider\":\"DEEPSEEK\",\"model\":\"deepseek-chat\",\"mocked\":false,\"errors\":[],\"profileContextSourceTablesUsed\":[\"Profile\",\"Skill\",\"Education\",\"Project\",\"Experience\",\"CvProfile optional notes\"],\"profileContextMissingFields\":[]}', 'I am writing to apply for the Studentische Aushilfe (m/w/d) im Produktmanagement position at The Pampered Chef Deutschland GmbH. Your focus on developing and marketing premium kitchen products, combined with a flat organizational structure that values ownership and continuous learning, is exactly the kind of environment where I can contribute effectively while growing professionally.\n\nThrough my hands-on project development, I have built full-stack web applications where I was responsible for conceiving and creating landing pages, writing product-related content, and ensuring a smooth user experience. For example, I designed and developed a travel agency platform where I created the UI using Next.js and Tailwind CSS, and I wrote and structured content for multiple tour packages and service pages. This experience directly aligns with your need for someone who can formulate product texts and create landing pages.\n\nIn addition to content and landing page work, I regularly performed market and competitive analysis as part of my development process. I analyzed competitor websites, pricing structures, and design trends to ensure the platforms I built were well-positioned. I also supported reporting and data evaluation by tracking user engagement metrics and presenting findings to stakeholders. These skills map naturally to your requirements for product and market analysis, reporting, and evaluation.\n\nOne area that particularly interests me is the opportunity to work on video scripts, voice-over texts, captions, and user manuals. In my previous projects, I have written technical documentation, prepared presentation materials, and communicated complex features in clear, user-friendly language. I am comfortable working across both technical and non-technical content, and I enjoy the process of making information accessible and engaging.\n\nIn addition to my technical experience, I work effectively across multidisciplinary teams and communicate clearly with both technical and non-technical stakeholders. I am fluent in Bengali and English, have working knowledge of Russian and Hindi, and enjoy collaborating in international and cross-cultural environments. I am a current Software Engineering student, which gives me a structured and analytical approach to problem-solving. I have attached my CV for your review and would welcome the chance to discuss how I can support your product management team.', '2026-07-02 13:40:46.628', '2026-07-02 13:40:46.628'),
(2057, 2059, 1, 10, '[]', '[\"Finanzbereich oder Wirtschaftsrecht Qualifizierung\",\"Compliance-Erfahrung\",\"Finanzrechtliche Kenntnisse\",\"Affinität fürs Schreiben von Fachartikeln\"]', 'The applicant\'s profile is a strong mismatch for this regulatory analyst role. The job requires a background in finance, law, or compliance with a focus on writing and analysis. The applicant is a software engineer with no relevant qualifications or experience in the financial regulatory domain. The score is low due to the complete absence of required domain expertise.', '{\"generatedBy\":\"job-agent-ai\",\"provider\":\"DEEPSEEK\",\"model\":\"deepseek-chat\",\"mocked\":false,\"errors\":[],\"profileContextSourceTablesUsed\":[\"Profile\",\"Skill\",\"Education\",\"Project\",\"Experience\",\"CvProfile optional notes\"],\"profileContextMissingFields\":[]}', 'I am writing to apply for the (Senior) Consultant Regulatory Analyst position at Severn Consultancy GmbH. The work of Regupedia in providing a comprehensive overview of regulatory changes for financial institutions is impressive, and I am drawn to the opportunity to contribute to a team that values knowledge sharing and continuous development.\n\nMy background is in software engineering, where I have spent over four years building full-stack applications and solving complex technical problems. This experience has given me a structured, analytical mindset that I believe is directly transferable to regulatory analysis. I am accustomed to researching specifications, understanding intricate requirements, and documenting my findings in a clear, actionable manner.\n\nOne area that particularly interests me is the creation of detailed analyses and factsheets. In my previous work as a Web Developer, I was responsible for documenting system architectures, writing technical guides, and creating reports for both technical and non-technical stakeholders. I am confident I can apply this same discipline to researching financial norms and stand