(2058, 2060, 1, 35, '[\"C++\",\"Python\",\"Git\",\"ESP32\",\"Raspberry Pi\",\"Linux\",\"Docker\"]', '[\"C (for microcontrollers)\",\"FreeRTOS/ESP-IDF\",\"BLE (Bluetooth Low Energy)\",\"CAN, RS-485/Modbus\",\"UART, SPI, I²C\",\"OTA updates\",\"C1 German\"]', 'The applicant has foundational embedded systems experience with C++, Python, ESP32, and Raspberry Pi, demonstrated through a relevant project (Wireless Vision-Aid for the Blind). However, the role requires professional-level C for microcontrollers, RTOS experience (FreeRTOS), BLE, and specific industrial protocols (CAN, RS-485) which are not present in the profile. The applicant lacks the required C1 German proficiency. The match is partial and would require significant upskilling in core embedded technologies.', '{\"generatedBy\":\"job-agent-ai\",\"provider\":\"DEEPSEEK\",\"model\":\"deepseek-chat\",\"mocked\":false,\"errors\":[],\"profileContextSourceTablesUsed\":[\"Profile\",\"Skill\",\"Education\",\"Project\",\"Experience\",\"CvProfile optional notes\"],\"profileContextMissingFields\":[]}', 'I am writing to apply for the Embedded Software-Entwicklung position at REVOTION GmbH. The idea of building firmware that directly powers smart systems in caravans, boats, and yachts is exactly the kind of work I want to be part of. I appreciate that your team values real ownership over features, from the first commit to a product in the field.\n\nMy technical foundation is in C++ and Python, with practical experience developing embedded systems using ESP32 and Raspberry Pi. I have worked with real-time data streaming, sensor integration, and hardware bring-up. In my project \"Wireless Vision-Aid for the Blind,\" I built a complete embedded system that combined an ESP32-CAM for video capture with a Raspberry Pi running YOLOv8n for object detection. I implemented a custom UDP streaming protocol to achieve low-latency communication between the camera module and the processing unit, and optimized the entire pipeline to run offline on constrained hardware.\n\nThis role involves developing firmware for BRAIN and NODE modules using C on ESP32-S3 with FreeRTOS/ESP-IDF, designing BLE interfaces, and integrating third-party devices over CAN, RS-485, and Modbus. While my direct experience is with C++ and Python rather than C, I am confident in my ability to transition quickly given my strong systems programming background and hands-on work with microcontrollers. I am also familiar with Git, structured code reviews, and debugging with logic analyzers and oscilloscopes.\n\nWhat stands out to me about REVOTION is the combination of embedded systems work with real-world impact. The chance to see your code running on vehicles in active use, and to shape the firmware architecture in a small, focused team, is rare. I also bring experience with AI at the edge, which aligns with your nice-to-have for Edge-AI and TinyML on microcontrollers.\n\nIn addition to my technical experience, I work effectively across multidisciplinary teams and communicate clearly with both technical and non-technical stakeholders. I am fluent in Bengali and English, have working knowledge of Russian and Hindi, and enjoy collaborating in international and cross-cultural environments. I have attached my CV for your review and would welcome the opportunity to discuss how I can contribute to your team.', '2026-07-02 13:41:04.810', '2026-07-02 13:41:04.810'),
(2059, 2061, 1, 15, '[\"Linux\",\"Docker\",\"CI/CD\",\"MySQL\",\"Git\"]', '[\"SAP S/4HANA\",\"SAP ECC\",\"SAP R/3\",\"SAP MM\",\"SAP PP\",\"Customizing\",\"German language (fluent)\",\"Wirtschaftsinformatik degree\"]', 'The applicant has a strong software engineering background but lacks SAP-specific experience, which is the core requirement for this role. The match is low due to the specialized SAP MM/PP consulting nature of the position.', '{\"generatedBy\":\"job-agent-ai\",\"provider\":\"DEEPSEEK\",\"model\":\"deepseek-chat\",\"mocked\":false,\"errors\":[],\"profileContextSourceTablesUsed\":[\"Profile\",\"Skill\",\"Education\",\"Project\",\"Experience\",\"CvProfile optional notes\"],\"profileContextMissingFields\":[]}', 'I am writing to apply for the SAP Inhouse Prozessberater MM/PP position at Lödige Industries GmbH. Your company\'s global leadership in logistics systems and airport solutions is impressive, and I am interested in contributing to your SAP team in Paderborn.\n\nMy background is in full-stack software engineering, where I have developed strong analytical and process-oriented skills. I have experience working with enterprise-level systems, gathering requirements from stakeholders, designing solutions, and coordinating implementations across teams. This has given me a structured approach to problem-solving that aligns well with process consulting work.\n\nIn my professional experience as a Web Developer, I have worked on requirement analysis, solution design, testing support, and documentation. I have supported live production systems, handled incidents, and coordinated deployments. These responsibilities directly mirror the SAP consultant role of supporting systems in live operation, managing changes, and participating in rollout projects.\n\nI am comfortable working independently and taking ownership of tasks. I communicate clearly with both technical and non-technical stakeholders. I am fluent in Bengali and English, have working knowledge of Russ