(2234, 2236, 1, 15, '[]', '[\"Retail experience\",\"Customer service experience\",\"Inventory management\",\"Point-of-sale systems\"]', 'The applicant has strong technical skills in web development and AI engineering, but the Special Services Associate role at The Home Depot Canada is a retail customer service position. There is no direct overlap in required skills or experience. The applicant\'s background in customer-facing technical support and communication could be transferable, but the core retail and service-oriented requirements are not met.', '{\"generatedBy\":\"job-agent-ai\",\"provider\":\"DEEPSEEK\",\"model\":\"deepseek-chat\",\"mocked\":false,\"errors\":[],\"profileContextSourceTablesUsed\":[\"Profile\",\"Skill\",\"Education\",\"Project\",\"Experience\",\"CvProfile optional notes\"],\"profileContextMissingFields\":[]}', 'I am writing to apply for the Special Services Associate position at The Home Depot Canada. The role\'s focus on helping customers succeed and guiding them to the right solutions for their projects aligns well with my experience in customer-facing technical support and problem-solving.\n\nIn my previous work as a Web Developer, I spent a significant amount of time understanding client needs, explaining technical options in plain language, and ensuring they felt confident in their decisions. Whether it was helping a non-technical user choose the right feature set or troubleshooting an issue, I learned that clear communication and genuine care for the person on the other side makes all the difference.\n\nOne area that particularly interests me is the emphasis on being naturally curious and eager to keep learning. I have always approached my work this way, whether I was picking up a new framework for a project or finding a more efficient way to solve a recurring problem. I believe this mindset is essential for a role where customer needs vary and every interaction is an opportunity to learn something new.\n\nIn addition to my technical experience, I work effectively across multidisciplinary teams and communicate clearly with both technical and non-technical stakeholders. I am fluent in Bengali and English, have working knowledge of Russian and Hindi, and enjoy collaborating in international and cross-cultural environments.\n\nI would welcome the opportunity to bring my problem-solving skills and customer-focused approach to The Home Depot Canada. My CV is attached for your review.\n\nThank you for your consideration.', '2026-07-05 01:42:23.940', '2026-07-05 01:42:23.940'),
(2235, 2237, 1, 10, '[]', '[]', 'The job description does not contain specific technical requirements, skills, or responsibilities. It only describes the hiring process and includes a verification keyword. Therefore, the match score is low due to lack of job details to compare against the applicant\'s profile.', '{\"generatedBy\":\"job-agent-ai\",\"provider\":\"DEEPSEEK\",\"model\":\"deepseek-chat\",\"mocked\":false,\"errors\":[],\"profileContextSourceTablesUsed\":[\"Profile\",\"Skill\",\"Education\",\"Project\",\"Experience\",\"CvProfile optional notes\"],\"profileContextMissingFields\":[]}', 'I am writing to apply for the f position at Ajax Systems. I understand that your hiring process includes AI-assisted evaluation, and I appreciate the transparency in your approach.\n\nMy background spans full-stack web development, AI integration, and system architecture. I have built production applications using Laravel, Next.js, React, and Node.js, and I have integrated AI services such as OpenAI and Replicate into real-world platforms. This combination of web engineering and AI experience allows me to build systems that are both functional and intelligent.\n\nIn previous work, I developed RESTful APIs, implemented authentication and role-based access control, and deployed applications on Linux servers using Docker and Nginx. I have also worked with real-time features using WebSockets and Socket.IO, and optimized database performance through query tuning and caching strategies.\n\nIn addition to my technical experience, I work effectively across multidisciplinary teams and communicate clearly with both technical and non-technical stakeholders. I am fluent in Bengali and English, have working knowledge of Russian and Hindi, and enjoy collaborating in international and cross-cultural environments.\n\nI have attached my CV for your review and would welcome the opportunity to discuss how my skills align with the needs of your team.\n\nBest regards,\nMd Shahanur Islam Shagor', '2026-07-05 01:42:29.605', '2026-07-05 01:42:29.605'),
(2236, 2238, 1, 25, '[\"GraphQL\",\"MySQL\",\"PostgreSQL\",\"Git\",\"AWS\",\"Docker\",\"Nginx\",\"Linux\",\"CI/CD\",\"Jest\",\"PHPUnit\",\"PyTest\"]', '[\"Playwright\",\"Dedicated QA experience\",\"E2E test automation experience\",\"Polish language\"]', 'The applicant has relevant backend and API testing skills (GraphQL, MySQL, PostgreSQL) and general testing tools (Jest, PHPUnit, PyTest), but lacks dedicated QA experience, Playwright expertise, and E2E automation background required for this senior-level role.', '{\"generatedBy\":\"job-agent-ai\",\"provider\":\"DEEPSEEK\",\"model\":\"deepseek-chat\",\"mocked\":false,\"errors\":[],\"profileContextSourceTablesUsed\":[\"Profile\",\"Skill\",\"Education\",\"Project\",\"Experience\",\"CvProfile optional notes\"],\"profileContextMissingFields\":[]}', 'I am writing to apply for the Senior Quality Engineer role at Tellent. Your focus on building a test automation strategy and expanding end-to-end coverage across Tellent HR aligns with my background in full-stack development and quality-focused engineering.\n\nTellent\'s mission to empower HR and People teams with an integrated Talent Management Suite is compelling. The opportunity to work on a platform that serves over 7,000 customers globally and to contribute directly to product quality and customer experience is something I find genuinely interesting.\n\nThrough my professional experience as a Web Developer, I have worked extensively with GraphQL APIs and backend services, which directly matches your requirement for API and backend testing proficiency. I have designed and built RESTful and GraphQL APIs using Laravel and Node.js, and I understand the importance of testing these services thoroughly to ensure reliability and accuracy.\n\nIn previous work, I have collaborated closely with development teams to embed quality early in the development process. I have experience designing test plans, writing test cases, and working with automation tools to improve software accuracy. My hands-on work with CI/CD pipelines, Docker, and Linux servers has given me a practical understanding of how quality fits into the full development lifecycle.\n\nIn addition to my technical experience, I work effectively across multidisciplinary teams and communicate clearly with both technical and non-technical stakeholders. I am fluent in Bengali and English, have working knowledge of Russian and Hindi, and enjoy collaborating in international and cross-cultural environments.\n\nI have attached my CV for your review and would welcome the opportunity to discuss how I can contribute to Tellent\'s quality engineering efforts.\n\nThank you for your consideration.', '2026-07-05 01:42:37.163', '2026-07-05 01:42:37.163'),
(2237, 2239, 1, 10, '[]', '[\"General operative experience\",\"Food industry experience\",\"Manual labor skills\"]', 'The applicant\'s profile as a software engineer does not match the General Operative role at ABP Food Group, which requires manual labor and operational skills. No relevant skills or experience align with this position.', '{\"generatedBy\":\"job-agent-ai\",\"provider\":\"DEEPSEEK\",\"model\":\"deepseek-chat\",\"mocked\":false,\"errors\":[],\"profileContextSourceTablesUsed\":[\"Profile\",\"Skill\",\"Education\",\"Project\",\"Experience\",\"CvProfile optional notes\"],\"profileContextMissingFields\":[]}', 'I am writing to apply for the General Operative position at ABP Food Group. While my professional background is in software engineering and systems development, I bring strong problem-solving skills, attention to detail, and a disciplined work ethic that I believe translate well into an operational environment.\n\nThrough my experience as a web developer, I have developed a methodical approach to tasks, whether debugging complex systems or ensuring that production deployments run smoothly. I am comfortable working with structured processes, following safety and quality standards, and adapting quickly to new workflows.\n\nOne area that particularly interests me is working in a team-oriented setting where reliability and consistency matter. I have collaborated across departments in previous roles, communicating clearly with both technical and non-technical colleagues to meet deadlines and maintain quality.\n\nIn addition to my technical experience, I work effectively across multidisciplinary teams and communicate clearly with both technical and non-technical stakeholders. I am fluent in Bengali and English, have working knowledge of Russian and Hindi, and enjoy collaborating in international and cross-cultural environments.\n\nI have attached my CV for your review and would welcome the opportunity to discuss how my skills and work ethic can contribute to the team at ABP Food Group.', '2026-07-05 01:42:42.933', '2026-07-05 01:42:42.933');
