r seamless e-commerce experiences. We provide an unmatched platform for brands and retailers, enabling them to accelerate growth, optimize operations across channels, scale product offerings and enhance margins.\n\nToday, more than 40,000 companies trust Rithum to grow their business across hundreds of channels, representing over $50 billion in annual GMV. Using our commerce, marketing, and delivery solutions, our customers create optimized consumer shopping journeys from beginning to end.\n\nOverview \nAt Rithum, we empower commerce growth by connecting brands, retailers, and suppliers. As the North America Field Marketing & Events Manager, you are responsible for designing and executing a dynamic portfolio of eventsâincluding client conferences, industry trade shows, internal company gatherings, executive dinners, and multi-city roadshowsâwhile driving localized marketing strategies to generate demand, accelerate the sales pipeline, and align with Rithumâs strategic business objectives. You collaborate with cross-functional teams to deliver impactful events that inspire clients and engage industry leaders. In conjunction with senior marketing leadership, you develop regional strategies, optimize processes, and deliver high-impact experiences that elevate Rithumâs brand visibility and client engagement in North America.\n\nResponsibilities\n- Define and execute a North America field events plan to enhance brand visibility and achieve measurable business goals.\n- Develop and execute localized marketing strategies to drive demand, generate leads, and accelerate the sales pipeline in specific regions.\n- Build collaborative relationships with key internal stakeholders (regional sales stakeholders, marketing, content, product, client success) and external partners to create and deliver seamless, impactful events aligned with business goals.\n- Plan and execute a broad range of events, from high-touch executive dinners to mid-scale multi-city roadshows, with clear objectives, tracking, and measurement for each event.\n- Lead event execution, including budgeting, pre- and post-event marketing, logistics, vendor management, and post-event analysis for regional events.\n- Track key event metrics for North America events such as attendance, leads generated, opportunities and pipeline generated, and client feedback to evaluate event success.\n- Track event performance metrics and KPIs, presenting actionable insights to stakeholders to drive continuous improvement.\n- Leverage company websites, online content, industry trends, and emerging technologies to enhance the client experience and event effectiveness.\n\nQualifications  \nMinimum Qualifications  \n- 5+ years in field/corporate events management within a technology, software or e-commerce organization with a focus on North America events.\n- Previous experience in events and field marketing within the e-commerce sector, with a focus on engaging e-commerce audiences.\n- Demonstrated experience leading and executing industry events, similar to Shoptalk, NRF, or eTail.\n- Successful ownership and management of event budgets across varying scale and complexity.\n- Proven experience planning and executing events with<br/><br/>Please mention the word **GRATIFY** and tag RMTU5LjE5OC42Ni4xNjM= when applying to show you read the job post completely (#RMTU5LjE5OC42Ni4xNjM=). This is a beta feature to avoid spam applicants. Companies can search these words to find applicants that read this and see they\'re human.', 'new', NULL, '2026-06-17 01:43:37.557', '2026-06-17 01:43:37.557', '', '', 'Remote', 'Europe', '', 'RemoteOK', 'API', 'READY', '', '', '', 'api', 'https://remoteOK.com/remote-jobs/remote-north-america-field-marketing-and-events-manager-rithum-1133458', 'https://remoteOK.com/remote-jobs/remote-north-america-field-marketing-and-events-manager-rithum-1133458', '[{\"url\":\"https://remoteOK.com/remote-jobs/remote-north-america-field-marketing-and-events-manager-rithum-113345