(1505, NULL, 'api', NULL, 'Capital Planning Investment Control Business Analyst Lead', 'Aretum', 'Remote', 'https://remoteOK.com/remote-jobs/remote-capital-planning-investment-control-business-analyst-lead-aretum-1133900', '<p>Public Trust Eligibility Required</p><p>This is a contingent position, meaning employment is dependent upon the successful award of the associated contract to Aretum and completion of any required background investigation or security clearance verification.Â </p><p></p><p>About Aretum</p><p>Aretum is a mission-driven organization committed to delivering innovative, technology-enabled solutions to our customers across defense, civilian, and homeland security sectors. Our teams work at the intersection of strategy, technology, and transformation, helping agencies solve their most critical challenges. We believe in investing in our people and creating a culture where collaboration, inclusion, and professional growth are at the forefront.Â </p><p></p><p>Job Summary</p><p>Aretum is seeking a Capital Planning Investment Control Business Analyst - Lead. As a Capital Planning Investment Control Business Analyst - Lead you will focus on CPIC and Portfolio Management support activities and oversee Capital Planning Analysts and SMEs.</p><p></p><p>Due to the nature of our work as a federal consulting organization, employees may be expected to handle Controlled Unclassified Information (CUI) and must adhere to applicable safeguarding and compliance requirements.Â Â </p><p></p><p>Responsibilities</p><ul><li>Primary interface with federal Capital Planning leadership</li><li>Oversees development, maintenance, and quality of Business Cases (OMB300 equivalents), EVM reports, AAR submissions, and Investment Manager support</li><li>Ensures alignment with OMB guidance, IT governance processes, and Investment lifecycle activities</li><li>Manages Strategic Planning, Budget Formulation, Spend Planning, and Investment baselines</li></ul>\n<ul><li>8+ years CPIC experience</li><li>Bachelorâs degree (4 years of additional experience is acceptable in lieu of a degree)</li><li>Strong knowledge of OMB A-11</li><li>Experience mentoring analysts and leading gate review preparation</li><li>Ability to understand the needs of the government customer, set priorities and provide appropriate direction to team to implement the identified resolution</li><li>Ability to determine course of action to resolve various Capital Planning issues in a fast paced, highly visible client organization</li><li>Familiarity with FBC business case structures and portfolio data call requirements</li></ul><p></p><p>Travel Requirements</p><p>This is a remote position; however, occasional travel may beÂ requiredÂ based on project needs, client meetings, team collaboration events, or training sessions.Â Travel is expected to be less than 10% and will be communicated in advance whenever possible.Â </p><p></p><p>EEO Statement</p><p>Aretum is committed to fostering a workplace rooted in excellence, integrity, and equal opportunity for all. We adhere to merit-based hiring practices, ensuring that all employment decisions are made based on qualifications, skills, and ability to perform the job, without preference or consideration of factors unrelated to job performance.Â </p><p>As an Equal Opportunity Employer, AretumÂ complies withÂ all applicable federal, state, and local employment laws.Â </p><p>We are proud to support our nationâs veterans and military families,Â providingÂ career opportunities that honor their service and experience.Â </p><p>If you require reasonable accommodation during the hiring process due to a disability, please contactÂ hr@aretum.comÂ forÂ assistance.Â </p><p>Equal Opportunity Employer/Veterans/DisabledÂ </p><p></p><p>U.S. Work Authorization </p><p>Due to federal contract requirements, only U.S. citizens are eligible for this position. This position supports a federal government contract and requires the ability to obtain andÂ maintainÂ a Public Trust or Suitability Determination, depending on the agencyâs background investigation requirements.Â </p>\n<ul><li>Health Care Plan (Medical, Dental &amp; Vision)Â Â Â </li></ul><ul><li>Retirement Plan (401k)Â Â </li></ul><ul><li>Life Insurance (Basic, Voluntary &amp; AD&amp;D)Â Â Â </li></ul><ul><li>Paid Time OffÂ Â </li></ul><ul><li>Family Leave (Maternity, Paternity)Â Â Â </li></ul><ul><li>Short Term &amp; Long-Term DisabilityÂ Â Â </li></ul><ul><li>Training &amp; DevelopmentÂ </li></ul><br/><br/>Please mention the word **BEUTIFULLY** and tag RMTU5LjE5OC42Ni4xNjM= when applying to show you read the job post completely (#RMTU5LjE5OC42Ni4xNjM=). This is a beta feature to avoid spam applicants. Companies can search these words to find applicants that read this and see they\'re human.', '<p>Public Trust Eligibility Required</p><p>This is a contingent position, meaning employment is dependent upon the successful award of the associated contract to Aretum and completion of any required background investigation or security clearance verification.Â </p><p></p><p>About Aretum</p><p>Aretum is a mission-driven organization committed to delivering innovative, technology-enabled solutions to our customers across defense, civilian, and homeland security sectors. Our teams work at the intersection of strategy, technology, and transformation, helping agencies solve their most critical challenges. We believe in investing in our people and creating a culture where collaboration, inclusion, and professional growth are at the forefront.Â </p><p></p><p>Job Summary</p><p>Aretum is seeking a Capital Planning Investment Control Business Analyst - Lead. As a Capital Planning Investment Control Business Analyst - Lead you will focus on CPIC and Portfolio Management support activities and oversee Capital Planning Analysts and SMEs.</p><p></p><p>Due to the nature of our work as a federal consulting organization, employees may be expected to handle Controlled Unclassified Information (CUI) and must adhere to applicable safeguarding and compliance requirements.Â Â </p><p></p><p>Responsibilities</p><ul><li>Primary interface with federal Capital Planning leadership</li><li>Oversees development, maintenance, and quality of Business Cases (OMB300 equivalents), EVM reports, AAR submissions, and Investment Manager support</li><li>Ensures alignment with OMB guidance, IT governance processes, and Investment lifecycle activities</li><li>Manages Strategic Planning, Budget Formulation, Spend Planning, and Investment baselines</li></ul>\n<ul><li>8+ years CPIC experience</li><li>Bachelorâs degree (4 years of additional experience is acceptable in lieu of a degree)</li><li>Strong knowledge of OMB A-11</li><li>Experience mentoring analysts and leading gate review preparation</li><li>Ability to understand the needs of the government customer, set priorities and provide appropriate direction to team to implement the identified resolution</li><li>Ability to determine course of action to resolve various Capital Planning issues in a fast paced, highly visible client organization</li><li>Familiarity with FBC business case structures and portfolio data call requirements</li></ul><p></p><p>Travel Requirements</p><p>This is a remote position; however, occasional travel may beÂ requiredÂ based on project needs, client meetings, team collaboration events, or training sessions.Â Travel is expected to be less than 10% and will be communicated in advance whenever possible.Â </p><p></p><p>EEO Statement</p><p>Aretum is committed to fostering a workplace rooted in excellence, integrity, and equal opportunity for all. We adhere to merit-based hiring practices, ensuring that all employment decisions are made based on qualifications, skills, and ability to perform the job, without preference or consideration of factors unrelated to job performance.Â </p><p>As an Equal Opportunity Employer, AretumÂ complies withÂ all applicable federal, state, and local employment laws.Â </p><p>We are proud to support our nationâs veterans and military families,Â providingÂ career opportunities that honor their service and experience.Â </p><p>If you require reasonable accommodation during the hiring process due to a disability, please contactÂ hr@aretum.comÂ forÂ assistance.Â </p><p>Equal Opportunity Employer/Veterans/DisabledÂ </p><p></p><p>U.S. Work Authorization </p><p>Due to federal contract requirements, only U.S. citizens are eligible for this position. This position supports a federal government contract and requires the ability to obtain andÂ maintainÂ a Public Trust or Suitability Determination, depending on the agencyâs background investigation requirements.Â </p>\n<ul><li>Health Care Plan (Medical, Dental &amp; Vision)Â Â Â </li></ul><ul><li>Retirement Plan (401k)Â Â </li></ul><ul><li>Life Insurance (Basic, Voluntary &amp; AD&amp;D)Â Â Â </li></ul><ul><li>Paid Time OffÂ Â </li></ul><ul><li>Family Leave (Maternity, Paternity)Â Â Â </li></ul><ul><li>Short Term &amp; Long-Term DisabilityÂ Â Â </li></ul><ul><li>Training &amp; DevelopmentÂ </li></ul><br/><br/>Please mention the word **BEUTIFULLY** and tag RMTU5LjE5OC42Ni4xNjM= when applying to show you read the job post completely (#RMTU5LjE5OC42Ni4xNjM=). This is a beta feature to avoid spam applicants. Companies can search these words to find applicants that read this and see they\'re human.', 'new', NULL, '2026-06-24 01:44:22.466', '2026-06-24 01:44:22.466', '', '', 'Remote', 'Europe', '', 'RemoteOK', 'API', 'READY', '', '', '', 'api', 'https://remoteOK.com/remote-jobs/remote-capital-planning-investment-control-business-analyst-lead-aretum-1133900', 'https://remoteOK.com/remote-jobs/remote-capital-planning-investment-control-business-analyst-lead-aretum-1133900', '[{\"url\":\"https://remoteOK.com/remote-jobs/remote-capital-planning-investment-control-business-analyst-lead-aretum-1133900\",\"type\":\"applyUrl\"}]', 'pending', '', NULL),
(1506, NULL, 'api', NULL, 'Program Manager', 'MedTech Innovator', 'California, California, United States', 'https://remoteOK.com/remote-jobs/remote-program-manager-medtech-innovator-1133905', '<strong>Program Manager</strong><p>&nbsp;</p><p>MedTech Innovator is the worldâs largest life science accelerator, committed to improving human health by supporting startups and scale-ups that are transforming healthcare. </p><p><br></p><p>We are seeking a Program Manager to support operational execution across one or more innovation-focused programs and strategic initiatives.</p><p><br></p><p>This role is responsible for coordinating program operations, managing timelines and deliverables, supporting stakeholder communications, and helping ensure successful execution across a range of initiatives and partnerships. The position requires strong organizational skills, attention to detail, adaptability, and the ability to manage multiple priorities in a collaborative, fast-paced environment.</p><p>The ideal candidate is proactive, solutions-oriented, and comfortable working across cross-functional teams, external partners, startups, subject matter experts, and other stakeholders. This role is well suited for someone who enjoys building operational structure, improving processes, and supporting mission-driven innovation programs.</p><p><br></p><p>Program responsibilities may evolve over time as initiatives are launched, expanded, modified, or concluded.</p><p><br></p><strong>Who You Are</strong><p>&nbsp;</p><p>â&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Highly organized and detail-oriented, with strong project and program management skills</p><p>â&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Comfortable managing multiple priorities and deadlines simultaneously in a fast-paced environment</p><p>â&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Strong communicator with the ability to work effectively across internal and external stakeholders</p><p>â&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Proactive, adaptable, and solutions-oriented, with the ability to operate independently in a remote setting</p><p>â&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Interested in healthcare innovation, life sciences, technology, startups, research, public-private partnerships, and/or related sectors</p><p>â&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Experienced in program management, operations, partnerships, project coordination, grants/contracts administration, healthcare innovation, nonprofit programs, research environments, or related fields</p><p>â&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Familiarity with grant-funded, contract-funded, federally supported, or compliance-oriented programs preferred</p><p>â&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Comfortable working with operational systems, trackers, reporting tools, and process development</p><p>â&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Proficient with tools such as Airtable, Google Workspace, Excel, Slack, Zoom, and related collaboration platforms</p><p>â&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Bachelorâs degree required; advanced degree preferred</p><p>&nbsp;</p><strong>What Youâll Do</strong><p>&nbsp;</p>Program Operations<p>â&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Support day-to-day operational execution across one or more programs or initiatives</p><p>â&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Manage timelines, deliverables, workflows, and ongoing coordination across multiple stakeholders</p><p>â&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Develop and maintain operational systems, trackers, templates, SOPs, and internal documentation</p><p>â&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Identify operational challenges, risks, or bottlenecks and help coordinate solutions</p><p>â&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Support cross-functional collaboration across internal teams and external partners</p><p>â&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Contribute to process improvement and operational efficiency efforts across programs</p><p>&nbsp;</p>Stakeholder Coordination<p>â&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Coordinate communications, scheduling, and logistics across internal teams, external partners, reviewers, consultants, startups, and other stakeholders</p><p>â&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Support onboarding and coordination of subject matter experts, reviewers, consultants, and advisors</p><p>â&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Help maintain strong working relationships across program stakeholders</p><p>â&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Support participating organizations and partners throughout program execution by answering questions, coordinating logistics, and tracking deliverables</p><p>&nbsp;</p>Application &amp; Evaluation Support<p>â&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Support development and execution of application materials, review processes, evaluation workflows, and stakeholder guidance</p><p>â&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Coordinate submission tracking, reviewer assignments, communications, and related operational activities</p><p>â&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Facilitate meetings, discussions, and preparation of summaries, recommendations, and supporting materials</p><p>&nbsp;</p>Reporting &amp; Documentation<p>â&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Prepare reports, presentations, summaries, and other programmatic materials</p><p>â&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Maintain organized program documentation and records</p><p>â&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Track program activities, deliverables, communications, and decisions to support effective program management and reporting</p><p>â&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Support program closeout activities, lessons learned documentation, and performance tracking</p><p>&nbsp;</p>Meetings, Events, &amp; Communications<p>â&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Support planning and execution of virtual and in-person meetings, workshops, webinars, showcases, and related activities</p><p>â&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Coordinate agendas, meeting materials, schedules, and follow-up actions</p><p>â&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Represent programs professionally across interactions with stakeholders and partners</p><p>&nbsp;</p><strong>Why This Role</strong><p>&nbsp;</p><p>â&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Opportunity to support innovative, mission-driven programs with meaningful real-world impact</p><p>â&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Exposure to emerging technologies, startups, and healthcare innovation ecosystems</p><p>â&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Collaborative, mission-driven, entrepreneurial, and fast-moving work environment</p><p>â&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Fully remote role (&lt;5% travel annually) with flexibility and ownership over operational responsibilities</p><p>â&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Opportunity to help shape and support growing programs and strategic initiatives</p><p>â&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Meaningful interaction with industry experts, innovators, partners, and cross-functional teams</p><p><br></p><strong>Compensation and Benefits</strong><p>&nbsp;</p><p>â&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Competitive salary commensurate with experience </p><p>â&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Medical, dental, and vision benefits</p><p>â&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Generous PTO and holiday schedule</p><p>â&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Fully remote work environment</p><p>â&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Minimal travel requirements (&lt;5% annually)</p><p>&nbsp;</p><strong>Equal Opportunity Statement</strong><p>&nbsp;</p><p>We are an equal opportunity employer and are committed to building a diverse and inclusive workplace. We do not discriminate on the basis of race, color, religion, sex, gender identity or expression, sexual orientation, national origin, age, disability, veteran status, or any other protected characteristic under applicable law. Candidates must be legally authorized to work 