this plan</h3><p>This plan is built for clients who care about both design quality and technical stability. The goal is not only to make something look good, but also to make it usable, maintainable, secure, and ready for real users. Each plan keeps a balance between visual design, code quality, performance, deployment readiness, and future improvement. That makes it useful for personal brands, small businesses, agencies, startups, online stores, SaaS products, automation platforms, and custom software ideas.</p>'),
(17, 'Enterprise', 'A complete annual enterprise plan for custom software, secure systems, cloud operations, automation, and long-term roadmap execution.', 29999.00, 'Annual', '[\"Responsive UI design for mobile, tablet, laptop, and desktop screens\", \"Modern frontend development using clean reusable components\", \"Backend development support for APIs, dashboards, authentication, and database workflows\", \"Performance optimization for speed, loading time, image delivery, and frontend rendering\", \"SEO-friendly structure with clean headings, metadata planning, and readable content sections\", \"Bug fixing, testing, and quality review before delivery\", \"Deployment guidance for cPanel, VPS, Cloudflare, PM2, Apache, Nginx, or Node hosting\", \"Database design support including schema planning, migrations, indexes, and relational structure\", \"API integration support for payment, messaging, analytics, maps, email, storage, or third-party services\", \"Security-focused implementation with validation, access control, safe configuration, and basic hardening\", \"Admin panel planning and development where required\", \"Clean documentation and handoff notes for future maintenance\", \"Source code organization with scalable folder structure\", \"Communication and progress updates during the active work period\", \"Post-delivery support according to the selected plan duration\", \"Best for full technical partnership\", \"Year-long roadmap and support structure\", \"Priority long-term availability\"]', 1, 0, 17, '2026-04-26 14:52:02.953', '2026-04-26 14:52:02.953', 'enterprise-annual', '<h2>Enterprise Annual Plan</h2><p>The Enterprise Annual plan is designed for clients who need a complete annual enterprise plan for custom software, secure systems, cloud operations, automation, and long-term roadmap execution. This package is structured around practical delivery, clean technical decisions, and a professional result that can be used in real business, portfolio, product, or startup environments.</p><p>This is a annual engagement. The scope, communication depth, feature volume, and support level are matched with the selected duration so the client gets a realistic delivery plan instead of a confusing open-ended promise. The listed price starts from $29,999.00, and the final scope can be adjusted if the project needs more pages, more integrations, advanced backend logic, AI features, automation, or deployment work.</p><h3>What this plan can cover</h3><p>The work can include frontend design, responsive page building, backend development, API integration, dashboard improvements, bug fixing, database planning, deployment support, and technical consulting. It can also support advanced services such as real-time chat systems, SaaS application modules, e-commerce workflows, computer vision integration, IoT dashboards, automation systems, and secure architecture planning when the selected duration gives enough time for that scope.</p><ul><li>Responsive UI design for mobile, tablet, laptop, and desktop screens</li><li>Modern frontend development using clean reusable components</li><li>Backend development support for APIs, dashboards, authentication, and database workflows</li><li>Performance optimization for speed, loading time, image delivery, and frontend rendering</li><li>SEO-friendly structure with clean headings, metadata planning, and readable content sections</li><li>Bug fixing, testing, and quality review before delivery</li><li>Deployment guidance for cPanel, VPS, Cloudflare, PM2, Apache, Nginx, or Node hosting</li><li>Database design support including schema planning, migrations, indexes, and relational structure</li><li>API integration support for payment, messaging, analytics, maps, email, storage, or third-party services</li><li>Security-focused implementation with validation, access control, safe configuration, and basic hardening</li><li>Admin panel planning and development where required</li><li>Clean documentation and handoff notes for future maintenance</li><li>Source code organization with scalable folder structure</li><li>Communication and progress updates during the active work period</li><li>Post-delivery support according to the selected plan duration</li><li>Best for full technical partnership</li><li>Year-long roadmap and support structure</li><li>Priority long-term availability</li></ul><h3>Feature details</h3><p>Every feature is handled with a practical development mindset. Responsive design means the layout is tested for common screen sizes and adjusted so text, cards, buttons, forms, navigation, and images behave properly. Frontend work focuses on clean sections, readable typography, strong spacing, reusable components, modern animation where useful, and a design style that matches the brand. Backend work can include secure routes, database models, admin features, authentication logic, APIs, file handling, dashboards, and integration with third-party services.</p><p>Performance work can include reducing unnecessary assets, improving image handling, checking slow pages, simplifying heavy components, reviewing API response patterns, and fixing layout problems that create poor user experience. SEO structure is not only about keywords; it also includes meaningful headings, clean page hierarchy, readable sections, metadata planning, proper links, and content blocks that help both users and search engines understand the page.</p><h3>Development areas available under this plan</h3><ul><li>Ui/Ux Design</li><li>Web Design</li><li>Full Stack Web Development</li><li>Mobile App Development</li><li>Api Development</li><li>E-Commerce Development</li><li>Real-Time Chat Systems</li><li>Saas Applications</li><li>Database Optimization</li><li>Cloud Deployment</li><li>Cybersecurity Planning</li><li>Ai Integration</li><li>Computer Vision</li><li>Iot Systems</li><li>Drone System Development</li><li>Embedded Systems</li><li>Automation Workflows</li><li>Custom Software Development</li></ul><h3>Process</h3><p>The process starts with understanding the goal, the target users, the required pages or modules, the current technical problem, and the desired result. After that, the work is broken into practical tasks such as design cleanup, frontend development, backend setup, database changes, API work, testing, deployment, and final review. For larger plans, the work can be organized into milestones so each stage has a clear output and the product becomes easier to manage.</p><p>During implementation, the focus stays on maintainable code, safe configuration, consistent UI behavior, and future scalability. The plan can support Laravel, Next.js, React, Node.js, Express, Prisma, MySQL, PostgreSQL, Flutter, React Native, Tailwind CSS, Socket.io, WebRTC, Cloudflare, cPanel, VPS, PM2, Apache, and related tools depending on the project requirement.</p><h3>Best fit</h3><p>The Enterprise Annual plan is a good fit for clients who want a reliable technical partner for annual work. It is suitable for new websites, portfolio upgrades, startup MVPs, business landing pages, admin panels, e-commerce improvements, custom software modules, deployment fixes, UI improvements, backend features, and ongoing product support. It is also useful when the client already has a project but needs a developer to improve structure, fix issues, add features, or prepare the product for public launch.</p><h3>Delivery expectation</h3><p>The exact delivery depends on the selected scope, but the goal is always to provide a useful and professional result. Small plans are best for quick improvements, focused fixes, and limited tasks. Larger plans are better for complete product modules, multiple pages, dashboard systems, complex workflows, integrations, optimization, and long-term support. Any work that requires premium third-party services, paid APIs, hosting, domain renewal, server licenses, SMS gateways, payment gateway fees, or external tools is normally billed separately unless clearly included in the custom scope.</p><h3>Why choose this plan</h3><p>This plan is built for clients who care about both design quality and technical stability. The goal is not only to make something look good, but also to make it usable, maintainable, secure, and ready for real users. Each plan keeps a balance between visual design, code quality, performance, deployment readiness, and future improvement. That makes it useful for personal brands, small businesses, agencies, startups, online stores, SaaS products, automation platforms, and custom software ideas.</p>');
INSERT INTO `Profile` (`id`, `name`, `profile`, `designation`, `description`, `email`, `phone`, `address`, `github`, `facebook`, `linkedIn`, `twitter`, `stackOverflow`, `leetcode`, `devUsername`, `resume`, `heroSkills`, `hardWorker`, `quickLearner`, `problemSolver`, `createdAt`, `updatedAt`, `socialLinks`) VALUES
(1, 'Hi there, I\'m Shagor', '/uploads/1778676468429-1000073591.png', 'Full-Stack & AI Engineer', 'Hi, I\'m Shahanur Islam Shagor. I am a Software Engineer specializing in Full Stuck Web Development, Autonomous Systems and AI Engineering Enthusiast focused on building intelligent real-world technologies that combine software engineering, robotics, cybersecurity, and distributed autonomous systems.\nI am passionate about designing intelligent systems capable of operating in complex real-world environments where AI, autonomy, and cybersecurity work together to solve advanced technological challenges.', 'smshagor.ru@gmail.com', '+79954949836', '87, Lomonosova, Voronezh - 394087, Russia', 'https://github.com/smshagor-dev', 'https://www.facebook.com/smshagor1', 'https://www.linkedin.com/in/sm-shagor', 'https://twitter.com/shahanur_shagor', 'https://stackoverflow.com//23340584/md-shahanur-islam-shagor', 'https://leetcode.com/smshagor1/', 'md_shahanurislamshagor_', '/uploads/1782293732590-resume.pdf', '{\"title\":\"Core technologies I work with\",\"items\":[{\"name\":\"React\",\"image\":\"\"},{\"name\":\"Next JS\",\"image\":\"\"},{\"name\":\"MySql\",\"image\":\"\"},{\"name\":\"MongoDB\",\"image\":\"\"},{\"name\":\"Docker\",\"image\":\"\"},{\"name\":\"AWS\",\"image\":\"\"},{\"name\":\"PHP\",\"image\":\"\"},{\"name\":\"Laravel\",\"image\":\"/uploads/1777179296797-image.svg\"},{\"name\":\"Express JS\",\"image\":\"/uploads/1777179166022-expressjs-dark.svg\"},{\"name\":\"Node JS\",\"image\":\"/uploads/1777180192346-nodejs-icon.svg\"},{\"name\":\"GraphQL\",\"image\":\"/uploads/1777180290076-image-1.svg\"},{\"name\":\"GO\",\"image\":\"\"},{\"name\":\"C++\",\"image\":\"\"},{\"name\":\"C#\",\"image\":\"\"},{\"name\":\"Vue JS\",\"image\":\"/uploads/1777180952165-vue.svg\"},{\"name\":\"Angular JS\",\"image\":\"/uploads/1777181045017-image-3.svg\"},{\"name\":\"React Native\",\"image\":\"/uploads/1777181153470-image-4.svg\"},{\"name\":\"TypeScript\",\"image\":\"\"},{\"name\":\"SQLite\",\"image\":\"/uploads/1777181223076-image-5.svg\"},{\"name\":\"PostgreSQL\",\"image\":\"\"},{\"name\":\"Linux\",\"image\":\"\"},{\"name\":\"Nginx\",\"image\":\"\"},{\"name\":\"Apache\",\"image\":\"/uploads/1777181586562-image-40.svg\"},{\"name\":\"CI/CD\",\"image\":\"/uploads/1777181440122-image-6.svg\"},{\"name\":\"CMake\",\"image\":\"/uploads/1777181595835-cmake-logo-svg.svg\"},{\"name\":\"Flutter\",\"image\":\"\"},{\"name\":\"Kotlin\",\"image\":\"\"},{\"name\":\"Jetson Nano\",\"image\":\"/uploads/1777181732357-image-7.svg\"},{\"name\":\"Google Cloud\",\"image\":\"/uploads/1777181820494-image-8.svg\"},{\"name\":\"Digital Ocean\",\"image\":\"/uploads/1777181867787-digitalocean-icon.svg\"},{\"name\":\"Kubernetes\",\"image\":\"\"},{\"name\":\"Prometheus\",\"image\":\"/uploads/1777181963538-image-9.svg\"},{\"name\":\"Grafana\",\"image\":\"/uploads/1777182018776-image-10.svg\"},{\"name\":\"Jest\",\"image\":\"/uploads/1777182059934-jest.svg\"},{\"name\":\"PHPUnit\",\"image\":\"/uploads/1777182219586-image-11.svg\"},{\"name\":\"PyTest\",\"image\":\"/uploads/1777182154729-icon-icons.svg\"}]}', 1, 1, 1, '2026-04-25 20:38:07.383', '2026-07-02 05:59:13.051', '[{\"icon\":\"facebook\",\"label\":\"\",\"image\":\"\",\"link\":\"https://www.facebook.com/smshagor1\"},{\"icon\":\"twitter\",\"label\":\"\",\"image\":\"\",\"link\":\"https://twitter.com/shahanur_shagor\"},{\"icon\":\"github\",\"label\":\"\",\"image\":\"\",\"link\":\"https://github.com/smshagor1\"},{\"icon\":\"linkedin\",\"label\":\"\",\"image\":\"\",\"link\":\"https://www.linkedin.com/in/sm-shagor\"},{\"icon\":\"telegram\",\"label\":\"\",\"image\":\"\",\"link\":\"https://t.me/smshagor1\"},{\"icon\":\"whatsapp\",\"label\":\"\",\"image\":\"\",\"link\":\"https://wa.ma/+79954949836\"},{\"icon\":\"stackoverflow\",\"label\":\"\",\"image\":\"\",\"link\":\"https://stackoverflow.com/users/23340584/md-shahanur-islam-shagor\"},{\"icon\":\"leetcode\",\"label\":\"Academia\",\"image\":\"\",\"link\":\"https://vsu.academia.edu/smshagor\"}]');
INSERT INTO `Project` (`id`, `name`, `description`, `tools`, `role`, `code`, `demo`, `sortOrder`, `createdAt`, `updatedAt`, `image`, `views`, `impressionCount`, `buttons`, `slug`, `content`) VALUES
(1, 'AI Powered Financial App', 'I have designed and developed an AI-powered financial mobile application. I have developed API using Express, Typescript, OpenAI, AWS, and MongoDB. Used OTP via AWS SES, Google, and Facebook for the authentication system. Built AI assistants using OpenAI\'s latest model and trained using our dataset. Voice messages are converted to text using AWS Transcribe. The app fetches data from Google Sheets and generates a PDF term sheet, sent via AWS SES.', '[\"Express\",\"MongoDB\",\"OpenAI API\",\"AWS SES\",\"AWS S3\",\"Node Mailer\",\"Joi\",\"Puppeteer\",\"EC2\",\"PM2\",\"Nginx\"]', 'Backend Developer', 'https://github.com/smshagor-dev/smart_finance', '', 1, '2026-05-01 22:58:25.574', '2026-07-06 09:32:16.364', '/uploads/1777299567771-image-of-ai-powered-financial-app.png', 76, 28, '[]', 'ai-powered-financial-app', '<p style=\"text-align:justify;\">There’s no shortage of finance applications in today’s market. Expense trackers, budgeting platforms, investment dashboards, and accounting tools are everywhere. But after looking closely at most of them, one limitation became impossible to ignore: they are passive systems. They wait for users to input data, display numbers on a screen, and stop there.</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">The problem is that people don’t really want more charts or spreadsheets. What they actually want is clarity. They want automation. They want systems that reduce complexity instead of adding more of it.</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">&nbsp;</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">That realization became the starting point for this project.</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">&nbsp;</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">Instead of building another traditional finance application, we decided to build something that behaves more like an intelligent financial assistant than a conventional tool. The vision was simple but ambitious: create a system where users can interact naturally, automate repetitive work, and receive meaningful financial assistance in real time.</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">&nbsp;</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">From the beginning, the goal was not to add AI as a small feature hidden somewhere inside the application. AI needed to become the core experience itself.</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">&nbsp;</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">One of the biggest frustrations we noticed was how much manual effort still exists in modern financial workflows. Users constantly switch between platforms, manually create financial documents, organize scattered information, and spend unnecessary time performing repetitive administrative tasks. Even basic communication often feels fragmented and inefficient. Voice interactions are rarely utilized properly, and generating financial insights usually requires technical expertise that most users simply do not have.</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">What made the problem worse was that most systems force users to adapt to the software instead of adapting the software to users.</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">&nbsp;</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">That approach felt outdated.</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">&nbsp;</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">So we asked ourselves a different question: what if finance could become conversational, intelligent, and automated all at once?</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">&nbsp;</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">That single idea shaped the entire architecture of the platform.</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">&nbsp;</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">At the center of the system is a backend built with Express and TypeScript. Rather than functioning as a simple API layer, the backend acts more like a central orchestration engine. It manages requests, coordinates AI processing, handles authentication, communicates with cloud services, processes external data, and ensures everything works together in a structured way.</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">&nbsp;</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">Around that backend, we connected multiple systems including OpenAI models, AWS services, authentication providers, Google Sheets integrations, document generation pipelines, and cloud-based communication services.</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">&nbsp;</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">Even though many moving parts exist behind the scenes, the experience for the user needed to feel simple and natural.</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">&nbsp;</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">The AI assistant became the heart of the application.</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">&nbsp;</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">We integrated OpenAI models to power the conversational layer, but simply connecting an API was never enough. The system needed to behave like a financial assistant rather than a generic chatbot. To achieve that, we refined prompts carefully, trained the workflows using structured datasets, and controlled how responses were generated.</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">&nbsp;</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">As a result, the assistant can understand financial questions, generate structured outputs, assist with financial decision-making, and maintain conversational context throughout interactions.</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">&nbsp;</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">The difference is subtle but important.</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">&nbsp;</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">The system does not simply reply to prompts. It understands intent, context, and workflow.</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">To make the experience even more natural, we integrated voice input functionality using Amazon Transcribe.</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">Typing financial requests can feel slow and repetitive, especially on mobile devices. Voice interaction removes much of that friction. Users can simply speak naturally, and the application handles the rest.</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">&nbsp;</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">The process works through a streamlined pipeline. A user records a voice message, the audio is securely processed through AWS Transcribe, speech is converted into structured text, and the AI assistant interprets the result before generating an intelligent response.</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">This creates a far more human interaction model compared to traditional financial applications.</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">&nbsp;</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">Authentication and security were equally important considerations throughout development.</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">&nbsp;</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">Because financial platforms deal with sensitive information, we designed a hybrid authentication system that balances convenience with security. Users can log in through Google or Facebook for faster access while still having additional verification layers through OTP authentication powered by AWS SES.</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">&nbsp;</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">The result is a login experience that feels smooth without sacrificing account protection.</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">One of the most impactful features of the platform is automated financial document generation.</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">&nbsp;</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">Traditionally, preparing structured financial documents requires significant manual formatting and repetitive data handling. We wanted to eliminate that entirely.</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">&nbsp;</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">The application pulls financial data dynamically from Google Sheets, processes the information automatically, and generates professional PDF term sheets without requiring user intervention. Once generated, the documents are delivered directly through email using AWS SES.</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">&nbsp;</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">Tasks that previously took hours of manual work can now be completed within seconds.</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">Using Google Sheets as a dynamic data source turned out to be one of the most practical architectural decisions in the entire project.</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">&nbsp;</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">Instead of forcing non-technical users to learn a complicated admin dashboard, we leveraged a tool they were already comfortable using. Teams can update information directly inside spreadsheets, and those changes immediately flow into the application without requiring redeployment or developer assistance.</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">&nbsp;</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">This dramatically reduced operational friction while keeping the system flexible.</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">&nbsp;</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">For data storage, we selected MongoDB because the application deals with constantly evolving and semi-structured information. The platform manages user profiles, AI conversation history, generated financial documents, workflow states, and dynamic financial records. A flexible schema allowed the product to evolve quickly without the overhead of rigid database migrations every time the data model changed.</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">&nbsp;</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">Although the application feels simple from the user’s perspective, there was significant complexity beneath the surface.</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">&nbsp;</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">One major challenge involved controlling AI output consistency. Large language models can produce unpredictable responses if not carefully managed. We had to enforce structured response formatting, validate outputs, refine prompts repeatedly, and create fallback mechanisms to ensure reliability.</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">&nbsp;</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">Voice processing introduced another challenge. Financial terminology, accents, pronunciation differences, and noisy environments sometimes reduced transcription accuracy. To improve reliability, we added post-processing layers and validation logic to clean and refine transcription results before they reached the AI assistant.</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">&nbsp;</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">Email delivery created its own infrastructure challenges as well. Sending automated PDFs reliably required proper AWS SES configuration, verified domains, authentication records, and careful deliverability optimization.</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">&nbsp;</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">Data synchronization also became more complicated than expected. Google Sheets was never designed as a real-time database system, so we implemented caching layers and fallback handling to improve consistency and performance.</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">&nbsp;</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">Performance optimization became a major focus throughout development because AI-driven systems can quickly feel slow if response times are not carefully managed.</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">&nbsp;</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">We optimized database queries, API request handling, AI processing pipelines, caching strategies, and asynchronous operations with one primary objective in mind: everything should feel immediate.</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">&nbsp;</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">The philosophy behind the user experience was intentionally simple.</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">&nbsp;</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">Reduce friction everywhere possible.</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">&nbsp;</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">That meant minimizing unnecessary steps, supporting natural interaction methods, providing clear outputs, and ensuring users always receive fast feedback from the system. Users should never feel like they are fighting the application to accomplish basic tasks.</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">They should simply interact with it naturally.</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">&nbsp;</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">This is ultimately what separates the platform from most traditional financial applications.</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">Conventional finance apps mainly focus on storing data, displaying charts, and requiring manual user effort. This system takes a fundamentally different approach. It understands user intent, automates workflows, generates meaningful outputs, and communicates conversationally.</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">&nbsp;</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">That changes the relationship between the user and the software entirely.</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">&nbsp;</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">And this is only the beginning.</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">&nbsp;</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">The next phase of the platform includes predictive financial insights, personalized AI recommendations, multilingual voice interaction, advanced automation pipelines, and real-time analytics capable of proactively assisting users before they even ask questions.</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">&nbsp;</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">More than anything, this project changed how we think about financial systems themselves.</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">&nbsp;</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">The future is no longer about building passive tools that simply display information.</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">&nbsp;</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">The future is about building intelligent systems that can understand, assist, automate, and act.</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">&nbsp;</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">Once you experience that shift, it becomes very difficult to go back to traditional software.</p>'),
(2, 'Travel Agency App', 'I have designed and developed a full-stack web app for 2Expedition, a travel agency in Armenia. I created the UI using NextJS, Typescript, MUI, TailwindCSS, Google Maps, Sun-Editor, and React Slick. The app supports multiple languages and currencies. I developed the API using NestJS, Typescript, MySQL, TypeORM, AWS, and Nodemailer. I deployed the front-end app to AWS Amplify and the back-end app to AWS EC2.', '[\"NextJS\",\"Tailwind CSS\",\"Google Maps\",\"NestJS\",\"TypeScript\",\"MySQL\",\"AWS S3\",\"Sun-Editor\",\"Gmail Passkey\"]', 'Full Stack Developer', 'https://github.com/smshagor-dev/Travel-Agency-App', '', 2, '2026-05-01 22:58:25.574', '2026-07-02 18:51:53.630', '/uploads/1777299677579-image-of-travel-agency-app.png', 91, 49, '[]', 'travel-agency-app', '<p style=\"text-align:justify;\">Travel websites often look polished on the surface, but behind the scenes many of them struggle with performance, flexibility, and real-world usability. For smaller travel agencies especially, managing tours, bookings, customer data, pricing, content, and regional support across multiple disconnected tools quickly becomes overwhelming. That was exactly the challenge behind the development of 2Expedition.</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">&nbsp;</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">The goal was never to create just another travel website. The agency needed a complete digital platform capable of supporting real business operations while remaining scalable, manageable, and user-friendly for both travelers and administrators. So instead of patching together existing systems, we built the platform from the ground up with scalability, usability, and long-term maintainability in mind.</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">&nbsp;</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">From the beginning, the vision was clear. We wanted to create something that could do far more than simply display destinations and tour packages. The system needed to support operational workflows, handle growing user demand, manage localized experiences, and remain flexible enough to evolve alongside the business itself. The focus was always practicality, not just visual appearance.</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">&nbsp;</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">For the frontend, we chose Next.js with TypeScript, a decision that heavily influenced the overall architecture of the platform. In the travel industry, performance and discoverability directly impact business growth. Users often browse multiple destinations before making decisions, which means page speed, smooth navigation, and strong SEO performance are critical. Next.js helped solve many of these challenges through server-side rendering, faster initial loading, scalable routing, and improved performance across slower networks. The result is a frontend experience that feels responsive, modern, and optimized for real-world usage.</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">&nbsp;</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">To build the interface itself, we combined several technologies that balanced flexibility with development speed. Material UI provided structured and reusable components, while Tailwind CSS allowed rapid styling and responsive layouts. React Slick was used to create smooth destination showcases and interactive sliders, and SunEditor enabled rich content editing throughout the platform. Together, these tools helped create a polished UI that feels lightweight and easy to navigate without sacrificing maintainability.</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">&nbsp;</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">Because travel experiences are naturally location-driven, maps could not simply exist as decorative elements. We integrated Google Maps to make destinations more interactive and meaningful for users. Instead of only reading about locations, travelers can visually explore destinations, understand travel routes, and engage with places more naturally. This small change significantly improves usability and creates a more immersive browsing experience.</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">&nbsp;</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">Another major focus was global accessibility. The platform supports multiple languages and currencies, but the objective went beyond basic translation. Localization affects how users experience a platform emotionally and practically. People naturally feel more comfortable when they can browse content in their own language and view pricing in familiar currency formats. By dynamically adapting content and pricing based on the user’s region, the platform creates a more trustworthy and frictionless experience for international travelers.</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">&nbsp;</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">For the backend architecture, we selected NestJS with TypeScript. While lightweight frameworks can work well for smaller projects, this platform required a stronger architectural foundation capable of supporting long-term growth. NestJS introduced a modular structure, cleaner separation of concerns, dependency injection, and scalable service organization. As features expanded over time, this structure became increasingly important. The backend now handles everything from tour management and booking workflows to user handling, dynamic content APIs, regional configuration, and pricing logic while remaining maintainable and organized.</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">&nbsp;</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">The platform uses MySQL with TypeORM because travel-related information is highly structured by nature. Tours, bookings, schedules, pricing, and availability all rely heavily on relational data management. TypeORM helped streamline development by simplifying migrations, relationship handling, and data organization while keeping the backend stable as the data model continued expanding.</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">&nbsp;</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">One of the most important priorities throughout development was reducing dependency on developers for routine content updates. That is where SunEditor became especially valuable. Administrators can now create and edit tour descriptions, update destination pages, and publish rich formatted content without touching code. This transformed the platform from a static website into a practical content management system that the agency team can manage independently.</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">&nbsp;</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">Communication also plays a critical role in the travel industry, especially when bookings and customer coordination are involved. To support this workflow, we integrated Nodemailer for email functionality. The system now handles booking confirmations, customer notifications, automated updates, and internal communication processes, helping both travelers and administrators stay informed throughout the booking journey.</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">&nbsp;</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">Deployment and infrastructure were treated with the same level of importance as development itself. The frontend was deployed using AWS Amplify to ensure fast global delivery, automated builds, and continuous deployment workflows. The backend was hosted on Amazon EC2 to provide greater server-level control and infrastructure flexibility. Separating the frontend and backend environments made the system easier to scale, maintain, and optimize independently.</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">&nbsp;</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">Like any real-world production system, the project introduced several technical challenges along the way. Travel platforms naturally contain large amounts of media content, so maintaining performance required careful optimization of image loading, lazy rendering, and component-level performance handling. Multi-language support also introduced UI complexity because different languages affect text length, spacing, alignment, and responsive layouts in different ways. Currency handling required reliable conversion logic and consistent formatting to maintain pricing accuracy across regions. Meanwhile, as features expanded, backend complexity increased rapidly, making the structured architecture provided by NestJS even more valuable.</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">&nbsp;</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">What emerged from the project was far more than a standard travel website. The final platform became a complete operational system where travelers can explore destinations smoothly, tours and bookings can be managed efficiently, content updates happen without developer involvement, and data flows seamlessly across the entire ecosystem. Most importantly, the platform supports both customer experience and business operations equally well.</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">&nbsp;</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">What truly makes 2Expedition stand out is that it was designed around real operational needs instead of surface-level aesthetics alone. Many travel platforms focus heavily on appearance while overlooking scalability, maintainability, and internal usability. This platform balances modern frontend performance, scalable backend architecture, localization support, cloud infrastructure, and practical business workflows in a way that makes the system genuinely sustainable long-term.</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">&nbsp;</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">Building 2Expedition was never just about writing code or designing interfaces. It was about solving real operational challenges that travel agencies face every single day. By combining modern frontend technologies, structured backend architecture, localization systems, cloud deployment infrastructure, and flexible content management, we created a platform that is not only visually polished but also genuinely practical for long-term business growth.</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">&nbsp;</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">And in real-world software development, that practicality matters more than anything else.</p>'),
(3, 'AI Powered Real Estate', 'I have designed and developed a full-stack web app an AI-based real estate app using Replicate API and OpenAI. We used Express, Typescript, OpenAI, Replicate, Stripe, and Mongoose to develop the API. We utilized NextJS, Formik, TailwindCSS, and other npm libraries for the UI. We have trained multiple AI assistants using the latest GPT model and integrated Replicate API for image processing. We added role-based auth, subscription plans, Cron job scheduling, and payment integration with Stripe.', '[\"React\",\"Bootstrap\",\"SCSS\",\"Stripe\",\"Express\",\"TypeScript\",\"MongoDB\",\"Azure Blob\",\"OpenAI API\",\"Replicate AI\",\"Cronjob\",\"JWT\"]', 'Full Stack Developer', 'https://github.com/smshagor-dev/RealEstate', '', 3, '2026-05-01 22:58:25.574', '2026-07-05 12:39:51.233', '/uploads/1781018311614-home.png', 90, 51, '[]', 'ai-powered-real-estate', '<p style=\"text-align:justify;\">Real estate platforms have not changed much in years. Most of them follow the same predictable pattern: users scroll through listings, filter by price, look at a few images, and move on. The experience is functional, but it is still very limited.</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">&nbsp;</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">Buying or renting property is not just about browsing listings. It is about understanding value, comparing options, visualizing possibilities, and making decisions with confidence. That is where we saw the real gap.</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">&nbsp;</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">Instead of building another traditional listing platform, we built something smarter: an AI-powered real estate system that does not simply show properties, but helps users analyze, understand, and interact with them more intelligently.</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">&nbsp;</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">The core idea was to move from static browsing to intelligent assistance. We wanted users to do more than search and filter. They should be able to ask questions about properties, receive AI-driven insights, process images intelligently, access premium tools through subscriptions, and interact with the platform in a more natural way. The goal was never to replace real estate agents. It was to improve the overall property discovery experience with AI.</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">&nbsp;</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">To build the system, we used a modern technology stack focused on speed, scalability, and flexibility. The backend was developed with Express, TypeScript, and Mongoose, giving the system a clean API structure and flexible data handling. The frontend was built with Next.js, Tailwind CSS, and Formik, allowing us to create a fast, responsive, and user-friendly interface. For AI and image processing, we integrated OpenAI and Replicate. Stripe was used to manage payments and subscriptions.</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">&nbsp;</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">A lot of platforms claim to use AI, but in many cases it feels like a small add-on rather than a core part of the product. We took a different approach. AI was built directly into the experience. We developed multiple AI assistants tailored specifically for real estate use cases, allowing users to analyze property descriptions, ask questions, receive recommendations, generate summaries, and get support during decision-making.</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">&nbsp;</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">The important part was making the AI useful, not random. Instead of relying on one generic model, we shaped the assistants with structured prompts, domain-specific logic, and controlled response formats. This made the output more relevant to property search, comparison, and user decision-making.</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">&nbsp;</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">Real estate is also highly visual, so image processing became an important part of the platform. Property photos can strongly influence user interest, trust, and engagement. By integrating the Replicate API, the platform can process and enhance listing visuals, analyze property images, and support AI-driven visual transformations. This adds a layer of intelligence that traditional real estate platforms usually do not provide.</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">&nbsp;</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">The frontend experience was designed to stay fast, clean, and simple. Next.js gave us strong performance and a scalable application structure, while Tailwind CSS helped us build a modern responsive interface. Formik was used to manage complex forms such as property submissions, filters, and user inputs. Every interaction was designed to reduce friction, because users should be able to move through the platform without feeling slowed down by unnecessary steps.</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">&nbsp;</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">Role-based authentication was another key part of the system. Not all users need the same access or capabilities, so we created separate permission layers for admins, agents, and regular users. Each role has different views, actions, and responsibilities inside the platform. This keeps the application organized, secure, and easier to scale as more features are added.</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">&nbsp;</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">To support premium functionality, we integrated Stripe for subscription management. This allowed the platform to offer advanced AI tools, premium features, and upgraded access based on user needs. Stripe handled the payment flow, billing cycles, subscription status, and related payment logic, making the business model easier to manage and more reliable.</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">&nbsp;</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">Automation also played an important role behind the scenes. Some processes should not depend on manual user actions, so we used cron jobs to handle scheduled tasks such as subscription updates, data cleanup, and other background processes. These automations help keep the system running smoothly without requiring constant manual maintenance.</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">&nbsp;</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">For database management, we used MongoDB with Mongoose because the platform needed flexibility. The system handles user data, property listings, AI interaction logs, subscription records, and role-based information. A flexible schema made it easier to evolve the product as new AI features, property workflows, and user interactions were introduced.</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">&nbsp;</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">Of course, the project came with real technical challenges. One of the biggest was AI relevance. Early responses were sometimes too generic, which made them less useful for real estate decisions. We solved this by improving prompt structure, adding domain-specific context, and controlling the response format more carefully.</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">&nbsp;</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">Image processing also introduced performance challenges. AI-powered image workflows can be slow if they are not handled properly, so we optimized API calls, improved asynchronous processing, and added caching where it made sense. The goal was to keep the experience smooth even when heavier AI operations were running in the background.</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">The subscription flow created its own complexity as well. Payment systems need to be reliable, especially when users are paying for premium access. We focused on clean billing logic, reliable webhook handling, proper error management, and accurate subscription state updates to make sure users received the correct access at the right time.</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">&nbsp;</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">Role management also required careful planning. Admins, agents, and regular users all interact with the platform differently, so we built clear permission layers and middleware-based access control. This helped keep sensitive actions protected while still allowing each user type to work efficiently.</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">&nbsp;</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">What makes this platform different is the shift from passive browsing to active assistance. Most real estate platforms show listings and let users filter them. This system goes further. It understands user intent, enhances property images with AI, provides intelligent recommendations, offers premium AI-powered tools, and automates important workflows.</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">For users, this changes the experience completely. They are no longer just scrolling through properties. They can ask questions, get insights, analyze listings, compare options, and make better decisions with more confidence. The platform becomes faster, smarter, and more intuitive.</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">&nbsp;</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">This is only the beginning. Future improvements could include predictive property pricing, AI-powered investment analysis, smart alerts, personalized recommendations, and more advanced image generation features. There is a lot of potential to make real estate platforms more intelligent, practical, and user-centered.</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">&nbsp;</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">Real estate platforms do not simply need more features. They need better intelligence. This project is a step in that direction, moving from static listings to dynamic AI-driven experiences. Once users start interacting with properties this way, the old model begins to feel outdated.</p>'),
(4, 'Newsroom Management', 'I have designed and developed a full-stack web app a newspaper management dashboard application called Newsroom Management. As a front-end developer, I worked on creating the dashboard using NextJS, Material UI, Redux, Calendar, and other necessary npm libraries. We used React Redux to manage the application\'s state and React-hook-form and Sun Editor to handle forms.', '[\"NextJS\",\"Material UI\",\"Redux\",\"Sun Editor\",\"Calendar\"]', 'Full Stack Developer', '', '', 4, '2026-05-01 22:58:25.574', '2026-07-03 15:07:15.692', '/uploads/1777299877799-image-of-newsroom-management.png', 76, 50, '[]', 'newsroom-management', '<p style=\"text-align:justify;\">Stories break fast, edits happen in minutes, and multiple people often touch the same content before it goes live. But most newsroom tools are still built like traditional admin panels slow, cluttered, and disconnected from how modern publishing teams actually work.</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">That was the gap we stepped into while building Newsroom Management, a publishing dashboard designed specifically for the speed, pressure, and complexity of modern newsroom workflows.</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">&nbsp;</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">This project was never just about creating clean UI screens or another content management panel. The real challenge was building a system that editors, writers, and administrators could genuinely rely on during high-pressure publishing cycles where speed and coordination matter most.</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">&nbsp;</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">From the outside, publishing can look simple. Write an article, edit it, and publish it. But internally, newsroom operations are far more complex. Multiple writers work on different stories simultaneously, editors constantly review and revise content, deadlines shift rapidly, and publishing schedules change throughout the day. In many organizations, content and communication end up scattered across multiple disconnected tools, making collaboration slower and workflow visibility almost impossible.</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">&nbsp;</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">The biggest issue was the lack of a centralized system that could tie everything together clearly and efficiently.</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">&nbsp;</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">That realization shaped the entire direction of the project.</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">&nbsp;</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">Instead of starting with visual components or dashboard layouts, we started with workflow. We wanted to understand exactly how stories move through a newsroom environment. A draft gets created, content gets edited, revisions happen, reviews are completed, and eventually the story is either scheduled or published. Every part of the dashboard was designed around supporting this lifecycle naturally and efficiently.</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">&nbsp;</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">For the frontend architecture, we used Next.js as the foundation. Newsroom systems require speed, scalability, and responsive navigation because users constantly move between articles, schedules, drafts, and publishing tools. Next.js helped provide fast rendering, cleaner routing, better application performance, and a scalable structure capable of handling growing feature complexity over time.</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">&nbsp;</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">For the interface itself, we combined Material UI with custom styling approaches to create a system that feels both structured and flexible. Responsive design was also a major priority because newsroom teams often work across different devices and screen sizes throughout the day. The result is a dashboard that feels fast, organized, and consistent without becoming visually overwhelming.</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">&nbsp;</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">State management became one of the most important technical considerations during development. Newsroom systems deal with constantly changing information including articles, drafts, publishing schedules, permissions, role updates, and workflow states. To manage this complexity, we used Redux along with React Redux to create centralized and predictable state management across the application.</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">&nbsp;</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">This allowed the system to stay synchronized in real time. When an article status changes, when a review is completed, or when publishing schedules are updated, those changes are immediately reflected throughout the dashboard without creating inconsistent states or workflow confusion.</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">&nbsp;</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">Because content-heavy platforms rely heavily on forms, form handling also needed to remain fast and reliable even with large content inputs. We used React Hook Form to improve performance, simplify form management, and maintain cleaner validation handling throughout the application. This helped keep the experience smooth even when users were working with long-form content or complex editorial workflows.</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">&nbsp;</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">Rich text editing was another critical part of the platform. Writers and editors need flexibility when creating content, formatting articles, embedding media, and structuring stories visually. To support this properly, we integrated SunEditor into the system. This gave users a writing experience that feels much closer to professional publishing tools instead of simple text fields inside an admin panel.</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">&nbsp;</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">Scheduling also plays a massive role in newsroom coordination, so we introduced calendar integration directly into the dashboard. Editors and administrators can now visually manage publishing timelines, track upcoming deadlines, and schedule articles more efficiently. Instead of relying on disconnected spreadsheets or manual coordination, teams can clearly see what content is moving through the pipeline and when it is expected to go live.</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">&nbsp;</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">One of the biggest design priorities throughout the project was clarity. Many dashboards try to display everything at once, which usually creates clutter and slows teams down. We intentionally took the opposite approach. The dashboard was designed around clean sections, logical grouping, minimal visual noise, and fast navigation. Users should never feel lost inside the interface. They should immediately understand where they are, what content they are managing, and what actions they need to take next.</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">&nbsp;</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">The impact on workflow was significant. Writers can now draft and edit content more smoothly, editors can review stories faster, publishing schedules are easier to manage visually, and teams can track article status in real time without constantly switching between tools. By centralizing the workflow into a single environment, the system reduces confusion and improves operational efficiency across the entire publishing process.</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">&nbsp;</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">Of course, the project introduced several technical challenges along the way.</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">&nbsp;</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">Managing application state became increasingly complex as more workflow features and user interactions were introduced. With multiple users interacting with live content and publishing states simultaneously, keeping everything synchronized required careful architectural planning. Redux played a major role in helping maintain predictable data flow and consistent updates across the system.</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">&nbsp;</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">Rich text editing also introduced challenges. Editors needed flexibility without creating layout inconsistencies or unstable formatting behavior. SunEditor provided the balance between usability and control that the platform needed while still keeping the interface clean and manageable.</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">&nbsp;</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">Performance optimization became another important focus because newsroom content can become very large very quickly. Long-form articles, media-heavy stories, and constant updates can slow applications down if rendering is not handled properly. We optimized rendering behavior, form handling, and component updates carefully to keep the dashboard responsive even during heavier workflows.</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">&nbsp;</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">UI scalability also became more challenging as the platform expanded. As more features, permissions, and content workflows were introduced, the interface could easily have become disorganized. Maintaining consistent design patterns and structured component organization helped keep the dashboard clean and maintainable as complexity increased.</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">&nbsp;</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">What makes this platform different is that it was built around actual newsroom workflows instead of generic admin panel patterns. Most content dashboards are essentially forms with navigation menus attached to them. This system behaves more like a collaborative working environment.</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">&nbsp;</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">It reflects how publishing teams actually operate. It keeps workflows synchronized, reduces friction between different user roles, simplifies content coordination, and makes publishing operations significantly faster and clearer.</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">&nbsp;</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">And this is only the beginning.</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">&nbsp;</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">Future improvements could include real-time collaborative editing similar to Google Docs, AI-assisted writing and editorial support, article performance analytics, automated workflow routing, and more advanced role-based publishing automation.</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">&nbsp;</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">Newsrooms do not necessarily need more disconnected tools. They need better systems systems that bring structure, visibility, and speed into one environment.</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">&nbsp;</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">That is ultimately what this project was built to achieve.</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">&nbsp;</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">Once publishing workflows become centralized, organized, and intuitive, the entire newsroom operates more smoothly. And in fast-moving media environments, that efficiency becomes incredibly valuable.</p>');
INSERT INTO `Project` (`id`, `name`, `description`, `tools`, `role`, `code`, `demo`, `sortOrder`, `createdAt`, `updatedAt`, `image`, `views`, `impressionCount`, `buttons`, `slug`, `content`) VALUES
(5, 'Free Games Hub', 'There\'s something deeply satisfying about building a platform where people can just show up, click a button, and play. No subscription. No gatekeeping. Just games. That was the core idea behind Free Games Hub — a full-stack web application I built with Laravel 12 and Tailwind CSS that brings together a curated library of browser-based free games under one clean, modern roof.', '[\"Laravel 12\",\"PHP 8.2+\",\"Laravel Tinker\",\"Laravel UI\",\"Laravel Sail\",\"Artisan CLI\",\"Tailwind CSS\",\"Alpine.js\",\"Livewire\",\"Vite\",\"Sass\",\"MySQL\",\"Pusher\"]', 'Full Stack Developer', '', '', 5, '2026-05-01 22:58:25.574', '2026-07-09 00:39:06.642', '/uploads/1777407655781-image-1votws1votws1vot-1.png', 65, 52, '[]', 'free-games-hub', '<p style=\"text-align:justify;\">Free Games Hub started as a simple idea: create a modern web platform where users can discover, filter, and play free online games directly from their browser without downloads or installations. On the surface, that sounds straightforward. But as the platform evolved, it became much more than a game directory. Underneath the interface sits a surprisingly complex ecosystem that includes user authentication, KYC verification, a points economy, casino integrations, lottery systems, referral tracking, deposit and withdrawal flows, VIP rewards, two-factor authentication, real-time notifications, and a full administrative backend.</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">&nbsp;</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">From the beginning, the goal was not just to create another gaming website. The platform needed to feel modern, scalable, secure, and engaging enough to support long-term user retention while also giving administrators full control over operations.</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">&nbsp;</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">To build the system, I intentionally chose technologies that were mature, stable, well-documented, and capable of supporting production-level complexity without unnecessary friction. Laravel 12 became the backbone of the platform, handling routing, ORM relationships, authentication, middleware, queues, broadcasting, and event handling cleanly. Tailwind CSS was used for utility-first styling, making it possible to move quickly without fighting against rigid UI frameworks. Alpine.js added lightweight frontend interactivity without introducing the overhead of a full SPA architecture, while Livewire enabled reactive user experiences without needing to build a completely separate frontend API layer.</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">&nbsp;</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">For the database, MySQL provided a reliable relational structure that worked well for handling financial transactions, user relationships, game analytics, and referral tracking. Pusher was integrated for real-time event broadcasting and notifications, while Google 2FA added secure two-factor authentication flows. Laravel Socialite simplified OAuth authentication for Google, Facebook, and Telegram logins, and Progressive Web App support was added using erag/laravel-pwa to make the platform installable across desktop and mobile devices.</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">&nbsp;</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">The dependency structure alone tells the story of the project. This was never designed as a small experimental application. It was built as production-ready infrastructure capable of handling multiple interconnected systems at once.</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">&nbsp;</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">At its core, the platform functions as a game library where users can discover and launch online games directly from the browser. Games are organized through categories and tags, with each game storing structured information such as name, description, image, URL, play time, and SEO-friendly slugs. Categories also maintain their own metadata, images, and subtitles to support richer homepage presentation and navigation.</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">&nbsp;</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">The GameController handles administrative CRUD operations while also tracking gameplay activity through the GameOpen model. Every time a user launches a game, the action is logged. This data feeds into play history tracking, analytics systems, engagement calculations, and the broader points economy built into the platform.</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">&nbsp;</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">User accounts are another major part of the ecosystem. Users can register traditionally through email and password authentication or use social login providers such as Google, Facebook, and Telegram. Email verification is enforced before full access is granted, and once authenticated, users gain access to dashboards where they can manage their profile, monitor gameplay history, track balances, review deposits and withdrawals, and manage account security settings.</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">&nbsp;</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">To support financial operations safely, the system also includes a KYC verification layer. Users submit identity documents, which are reviewed manually by administrators before sensitive financial functionality becomes available. This helps improve trust and regulatory compliance across the platform.</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">&nbsp;</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">One of the more interesting parts of the project was designing the points economy. Instead of making gameplay purely passive, the system rewards users for activity. Every game session can generate points through the GamePoint system, and those points contribute to progression through a level structure powered by the Level model. Users can later convert points into rewards or account balances through the PointConverterController.</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">&nbsp;</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">This created a gamification layer that encourages retention naturally. The more users interact with the platform, the more value they gain from staying engaged.</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">&nbsp;</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">The platform also includes a casino subsystem powered through CasinoController and CasinoGameSession. Individual casino sessions are tracked independently, creating a framework capable of supporting multiple reward systems simultaneously. Welcome bonuses, deposit bonuses, cashback configurations, and VIP rewards are all handled through dedicated controllers and models such as CasinoBonusController, BonusUser, CasinoCashbackController, CashbackSetting, CasinoVipBonusController, and VipBonus.</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">One important architectural decision was ensuring these systems remained configurable instead of hardcoded. Almost every financial parameter inside the casino environment can be adjusted directly from the admin panel without requiring code changes.</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">&nbsp;</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">Financial functionality itself is managed through a gateway-driven deposit and withdrawal system. UserDeposit and UserWithdrew models track transactional activity, while DepositSetting allows administrators to configure payment methods, limits, and gateway behavior dynamically. Withdrawal access is protected by multiple security layers including deposit verification and KYC approval enforced through middleware such as CheckDepositForWithdraw and CheckKyc.</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">&nbsp;</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">Supporting financial documentation is also stored and managed through dedicated models for deposit and withdrawal verification files, allowing administrators to review submitted evidence directly from the backend.</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">&nbsp;</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">To increase engagement further, the platform includes a built-in lottery system powered by the Lottary and LottaryWinner models. Users can purchase lottery entries, transactions are recorded through LotteryTransaction, and winners can be displayed publicly. This added another layer of interaction beyond standard gameplay mechanics.</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">&nbsp;</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">The referral system became another important retention and growth mechanism. Through ReferralSetting and UserReferralController, users receive unique referral links while administrators retain control over commission percentages, signup bonuses, and reward structures. This allows the platform to support growth campaigns without changing application logic manually.</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">&nbsp;</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">On the administrative side, the system functions almost like a separate product entirely. Administrators can manage users, suspend accounts, review KYC requests, configure deposit gateways, manage homepage banners, edit static pages, organize games and categories, adjust points and level thresholds, and monitor logs across the platform. The admin environment was designed to centralize operational control instead of scattering management tools across different systems.</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">&nbsp;</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">Security was treated as a core architectural concern rather than an afterthought. Middleware plays a major role throughout the platform. TwoFactorMiddleware enforces two-factor authentication for protected accounts, CheckKyc restricts access to financial functionality until identity verification is approved, and CheckDepositForWithdraw prevents abuse of withdrawal systems without prior deposit activity. Email verification and OAuth authentication through Laravel Socialite further strengthen account security while keeping authentication flows consistent and manageable.</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">&nbsp;</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">The platform also includes Progressive Web App functionality through service workers and web manifests. Users can install the application directly onto their devices, and an offline page provides a smoother fallback experience when connectivity is lost. While relatively small from a technical perspective, this dramatically improves the perception of the platform by making it feel closer to a native application than a traditional website.</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">&nbsp;</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">Structurally, the project follows Laravel conventions while maintaining strong separation between public-facing, user-level, and administrative functionality. Controllers are grouped by responsibility, Eloquent models handle relationships across more than thirty entities, services manage heavier business logic, and broadcasting events support real-time updates throughout the application.</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">&nbsp;</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">One of the biggest lessons from building Free Games Hub was understanding how powerful middleware chaining can become in Laravel. By centralizing security rules such as KYC enforcement, deposit validation, and two-factor checks into middleware layers, the controllers remained significantly cleaner and easier to maintain.</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">&nbsp;</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">Another major lesson was the importance of separating business logic from models and controllers. The Services layer became essential for handling bonus calculations, cashback processing, referral math, and other heavier operational workflows. Keeping this logic isolated made the application easier to test, refactor, and expand over time.</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">&nbsp;</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">Building PWA functionality also proved surprisingly valuable relative to the amount of implementation work required. A service worker and manifest can be added relatively quickly, but the resulting installable mobile experience dramatically improves long-term user engagement.</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">&nbsp;</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">Perhaps the most important architectural decision overall was prioritizing configurability over hardcoding. Almost every financial rule, reward percentage, cashback rate, referral commission, and deposit limitation is stored dynamically inside the database and editable through the admin panel. While this required more planning upfront, it made the platform dramatically more flexible and scalable in the long run.</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">&nbsp;</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">Free Games Hub ultimately became far more than a simple browser gaming platform. It evolved into a complete ecosystem that combines entertainment, gamification, financial systems, user engagement mechanics, real-time functionality, and administrative control into one unified application.</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">&nbsp;</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">And that complexity is exactly what made building it so valuable.</p>'),
(6, 'Multivendor E-commerce Management Ecosystem', 'A full-stack, scalable multi-vendor e-commerce platform designed to streamline marketplace operations across web and mobile. It integrates multiple role-based Flutter applications with a Laravel backend, enabling seamless coordination between customers, sellers, delivery agents, and logistics teams.', '[\"Laravel\",\"REST API\",\"Authentication\",\"MySQL\",\"Flutter\",\"Dart\",\"Role-Based Access Control\",\"PHP\",\"AJAX\",\"Firebase Notification\",\"Google Maps API\",\"Redis\",\"Cloudflare CDN\"]', 'Full Stuck Developer', '', 'https://vexlina.com', 6, '2026-05-01 22:58:25.574', '2026-07-07 13:37:29.280', '/uploads/1777671151224-1776343570960.jpg', 65, 115, '[{\"text\":\"Live Demo\",\"link\":\"https://vexlina.com\"}]', 'multivendor-e-commerce-management-ecosystem', '<p style=\"text-align:justify;\" data-start=\"0\" data-end=\"573\">Building a scalable multi-vendor e-commerce platform is no longer just about listing products and processing orders it’s about designing a complete ecosystem where multiple stakeholders operate in sync. In this project, I developed a full-stack marketplace management system that connects customers, sellers, delivery agents, pickup points, and logistics teams within a unified infrastructure. The goal was simple but challenging: create a system that handles complexity behind the scenes while delivering a smooth and efficient experience on both web and mobile platforms.</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\" data-start=\"0\" data-end=\"573\">&nbsp;</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\" data-start=\"575\" data-end=\"1160\">At the core of the system is a Laravel-based backend that acts as a centralized engine, managing business logic, API communication, and data flow. Paired with a MySQL database, the architecture ensures structured and reliable data handling across all modules. On the frontend side, instead of building a single overloaded application, I implemented multiple Flutter-based mobile apps tailored to specific user roles. This decision keeps each interface focused, lightweight, and optimized for its purpose, whether it’s a customer browsing products or a delivery agent navigating routes.</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\" data-start=\"575\" data-end=\"1160\">&nbsp;</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\" data-start=\"1162\" data-end=\"1818\">The platform introduces a dedicated mobile application for each role in the ecosystem. Customers can explore products, place orders, and track deliveries in real time. Sellers get a powerful dashboard to manage inventory, process orders, and analyze their sales performance. Delivery personnel are equipped with tools for real-time tracking, route optimization, and delivery confirmation. Pickup point operators handle parcel verification and inventory movement, while logistics teams oversee shipment coordination and fleet operations. By separating responsibilities into role-specific apps, the system avoids clutter and significantly improves usability.</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\" data-start=\"1162\" data-end=\"1818\">&nbsp;</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\" data-start=\"1820\" data-end=\"2251\">One of the most critical aspects of this system is real-time synchronization. Every action whether it’s an order placement, inventory update, or delivery status change is instantly reflected across all connected applications. This eliminates communication gaps and reduces operational delays. Alongside this, role-based access control ensures that each user interacts only with relevant data, enhancing both security and usability.</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\" data-start=\"1820\" data-end=\"2251\">&nbsp;</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\" data-start=\"2253\" data-end=\"2680\">Automation plays a major role in improving efficiency. The platform streamlines logistics workflows by automatically assigning orders, updating delivery statuses, and managing pickup point operations. This reduces manual intervention and minimizes human error, which is crucial in high-volume marketplaces. Secure payment integration further strengthens the system by ensuring safe transactions and reliable financial tracking.</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\" data-start=\"2253\" data-end=\"2680\">&nbsp;</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\" data-start=\"2682\" data-end=\"3100\">From a technical perspective, scalability was a key focus during development. The system is designed to handle multiple vendors, high traffic loads, and large volumes of transactions without performance degradation. The modular backend structure allows easy expansion, making it possible to add new features or services without disrupting existing operations. This flexibility is essential for any growing marketplace.</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\" data-start=\"2682\" data-end=\"3100\">&nbsp;</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\" data-start=\"3102\" data-end=\"3421\">What sets this project apart is its ecosystem-driven approach. Instead of treating e-commerce as a single application, it is built as a network of interconnected systems working together seamlessly. This not only improves operational efficiency but also creates a more reliable and scalable platform for real-world use.</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\" data-start=\"3102\" data-end=\"3421\">&nbsp;</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\" data-start=\"3423\" data-end=\"3751\" data-is-last-node=\"\" data-is-only-node=\"\">This project represents more than just an e-commerce solution it’s a complete digital infrastructure designed to support modern marketplace operations. It demonstrates how thoughtful system design, combined with the right technology stack, can transform complex workflows into a streamlined and intelligent platform.</p><h3 style=\"text-align:justify;\" data-section-id=\"1bfrcq0\" data-start=\"286\" data-end=\"326\">1. Customer Side (Frontend / App)</h3><ul><li data-list-item-id=\"e1453815051e93c5aed241ca03f9f070f\"><p style=\"text-align:justify;\" data-start=\"327\" data-end=\"369\">This is where the business actually earns.</p></li><li data-section-id=\"12ck91d\" data-start=\"371\" data-end=\"424\" data-list-item-id=\"e091e7b7e16be981bea734c8dc579e2c4\"><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">User registration &amp; login (email, Google, Facebook)</p></li><li data-section-id=\"lbdc4n\" data-start=\"425\" data-end=\"470\" data-list-item-id=\"e274245dc7f34186fa2e225b2adf967f9\"><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">Product browsing (category, filter, search)</p></li><li data-section-id=\"1o9av5p\" data-start=\"471\" data-end=\"513\" data-list-item-id=\"e26c0a70f6a522dc226b9ace0b8f44d92\"><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">Product details (images, reviews, stock)</p></li><li data-section-id=\"dkc7l9\" data-start=\"514\" data-end=\"531\" data-list-item-id=\"ed8d61e145577942dc622496fc523bc25\"><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">Cart &amp; wishlist</p></li><li data-section-id=\"wjw46y\" data-start=\"532\" data-end=\"578\" data-list-item-id=\"e9e1f6d542d80b0001cb0f770351963ee\"><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">Checkout system (address, shipping, payment)</p></li><li data-section-id=\"1lwyh3y\" data-start=\"579\" data-end=\"614\" data-list-item-id=\"e0efc20b41c3828317ceafd2f54831d60\"><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">Order tracking (real-time status)</p></li><li data-section-id=\"110vo4z\" data-start=\"615\" data-end=\"634\" data-list-item-id=\"eee42fd26c037157846fcc93e9fa5424a\"><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">Reviews &amp; ratings</p></li><li data-section-id=\"16y5enw\" data-start=\"635\" data-end=\"674\" data-list-item-id=\"e7cade8a24c71fa3a302aae2b2f36ef89\"><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">Notifications (order updates, offers)</p></li><li data-section-id=\"1p6kh2s\" data-start=\"675\" data-end=\"716\" data-list-item-id=\"eb2dc28a80c8420d0a2050047f692ac9e\"><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">Multi-language &amp; multi-currency support</p></li></ul><h3 style=\"text-align:justify;\" data-section-id=\"1dv4nsg\" data-start=\"723\" data-end=\"754\">2. Seller / Vendor Panel</h3><ul><li data-list-item-id=\"ed2930e8fedd597d7d35c2bce46f28505\"><p style=\"text-align:justify;\" data-start=\"755\" data-end=\"812\">Each vendor runs their own mini-store inside your system.</p></li><li data-section-id=\"ylpijd\" data-start=\"814\" data-end=\"853\" data-list-item-id=\"e8a88a848d1d2d03f948aa1aff7a48600\"><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">Vendor registration &amp; approval system</p></li><li data-section-id=\"17vyhat\" data-start=\"854\" data-end=\"892\" data-list-item-id=\"e04d80e252ae892ff760ad82634182684\"><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">Product management (add/edit/delete)</p></li><li data-section-id=\"bstjrl\" data-start=\"893\" data-end=\"915\" data-list-item-id=\"e989ed291f2497cebc4b17ece2a15a75e\"><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">Inventory management</p></li><li data-section-id=\"ui9sbo\" data-start=\"916\" data-end=\"969\" data-list-item-id=\"efb956dca0fe32b1dc924f52f50cc0b6f\"><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">Order management (pending → processing → delivered)</p></li><li data-section-id=\"zg42h6\" data-start=\"970\" data-end=\"999\" data-list-item-id=\"e9d1943f3870e323f12c4ec94b20f0690\"><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">Discount &amp; campaign control</p></li><li data-section-id=\"1hia6vx\" data-start=\"1000\" data-end=\"1042\" data-list-item-id=\"ec9d47144cfca8b2d53f9f750db98ec6c\"><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">Sales analytics (daily, monthly, profit)</p></li><li data-section-id=\"hg2e1m\" data-start=\"1043\" data-end=\"1066\" data-list-item-id=\"e7144a0e66b7dd4c609bc125a0d97f07f\"><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">Payout request system</p></li><li data-section-id=\"1odvn9h\" data-start=\"1067\" data-end=\"1093\" data-list-item-id=\"e4ec36678d564b926dd219d0be316529e\"><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">Return &amp; refund handling</p></li></ul><h3 style=\"text-align:justify;\" data-section-id=\"1o373dy\" data-start=\"1100\" data-end=\"1140\">3. Admin Panel (Super Control)</h3><p style=\"text-align:justify;\" data-start=\"1141\" data-end=\"1180\">This is the brain of the entire system.</p><ul data-start=\"1182\" data-end=\"1539\"><li data-section-id=\"sejbex\" data-start=\"1182\" data-end=\"1227\" data-list-item-id=\"eec8380bbfc4fd2107025ca500fdad89f\"><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">Dashboard (orders, revenue, users, traffic)</p></li><li data-section-id=\"moxamv\" data-start=\"1228\" data-end=\"1275\" data-list-item-id=\"e0a58d1626f01871e59788e0ae41242eb\"><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">Vendor management (approve, suspend, monitor)</p></li><li data-section-id=\"q7ad5b\" data-start=\"1276\" data-end=\"1296\" data-list-item-id=\"e688ae87b71f7d26d62359269498b4b2d\"><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">Product moderation</p></li><li data-section-id=\"1sb1cc6\" data-start=\"1297\" data-end=\"1330\" data-list-item-id=\"e47dae5dc3df21c2a9e0572cb44e83045\"><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">Order control &amp; override system</p></li><li data-section-id=\"1agb3sb\" data-start=\"1331\" data-end=\"1378\" data-list-item-id=\"e5b710ca618126ad0b5a93c3ef9a2711b\"><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">Commission management (per vendor / category)</p></li><li data-section-id=\"2cg8z8\" data-start=\"1379\" data-end=\"1422\" data-list-item-id=\"e4e2331804e2d6e214d1f6b8c3a2b6c47\"><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">Campaign management (social, spin, promo)</p></li><li data-section-id=\"15wwz86\" data-start=\"1423\" data-end=\"1459\" data-list-item-id=\"e10f54b380517c4b735a89d4399e4cb1d\"><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">User management (customers, staff)</p></li><li data-section-id=\"o7b7dz\" data-start=\"1460\" data-end=\"1488\" data-list-item-id=\"ee88509b7a1249a8340d8e132af99e4bf\"><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">Payment &amp; transaction logs</p></li><li data-section-id=\"15uay3p\" data-start=\"1489\" data-end=\"1539\" data-list-item-id=\"e67ab48f654bbbfe0933bf94a2d488967\"><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">System settings (currency, tax, delivery charge)</p></li></ul><h3 style=\"text-align:justify;\" data-section-id=\"1t9xtrr\" data-start=\"1546\" data-end=\"1583\">4. Logistics &amp; Delivery System</h3><p style=\"text-align:justify;\" data-start=\"1584\" data-end=\"1644\">This is where most systems fail—but your project handles it.</p><ul data-start=\"1646\" data-end=\"1851\"><li data-section-id=\"ik0ofy\" data-start=\"1646\" data-end=\"1673\" data-list-item-id=\"ef1bfb3ef3f4f457e307121ea649ffa5d\"><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">Delivery agent assignment</p></li><li data-section-id=\"16u0dzs\" data-start=\"1674\" data-end=\"1707\" data-list-item-id=\"e8580dc9bc0c63dbc91688be5963addec\"><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">Delivery tracking (live status)</p></li><li data-section-id=\"7yyt2o\" data-start=\"1708\" data-end=\"1728\" data-list-item-id=\"e36a775cbf686ec844a0c6cacb1a5b894\"><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">Route optimization</p></li><li data-section-id=\"1ydtpfb\" data-start=\"1729\" data-end=\"1765\" data-list-item-id=\"ed2f73d4365e90a3be5d13de681a2066d\"><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">Delivery verification (scan / OTP)</p></li><li data-section-id=\"n5eqfs\" data-start=\"1766\" data-end=\"1792\" data-list-item-id=\"e876acb82e90843121f1219da771a95c0\"><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">Failed delivery handling</p></li><li data-section-id=\"54jdpq\" data-start=\"1793\" data-end=\"1819\" data-list-item-id=\"e432f6867aa68696250d2b7cd3ad92f3f\"><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">Return to warehouse flow</p></li><li data-section-id=\"1eac4qr\" data-start=\"1820\" data-end=\"1851\" data-list-item-id=\"ea562e395663a0340a4bbcbbb777be1b2\"><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">Delivery performance tracking</p></li></ul><h3 style=\"text-align:justify;\" data-section-id=\"rq3a3c\" data-start=\"1858\" data-end=\"1899\">5. Warehouse &amp; Pickup Point System</h3><p style=\"text-align:justify;\" data-start=\"1900\" data-end=\"1932\">Critical for scaling operations.</p><ul data-start=\"1934\" data-end=\"2180\"><li data-section-id=\"a5jjgs\" data-start=\"1934\" data-end=\"1983\" data-list-item-id=\"e8b4ebc45a07ff5d050a36b0622bd65ac\"><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">Main warehouse → sub warehouse (division based)</p></li><li data-section-id=\"nu6xr3\" data-start=\"1984\" data-end=\"2019\" data-list-item-id=\"e36c53ff89569a36f1f2b6761ce4979c4\"><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">Stock transfer between warehouses</p></li><li data-section-id=\"15bz82u\" data-start=\"2020\" data-end=\"2059\" data-list-item-id=\"e371dce45db674f36d9ce8f009aaa2213\"><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">Pickup point management (thana level)</p></li><li data-section-id=\"ku9buh\" data-start=\"2060\" data-end=\"2082\" data-list-item-id=\"e17cf9a546fce907004ba446a556d9289\"><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">Parcel scan (in/out)</p></li><li data-section-id=\"13xbytd\" data-start=\"2083\" data-end=\"2113\" data-list-item-id=\"ed5ed32f8ddd3e374b05c80c3128e6d3a\"><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">Customer pickup verification</p></li><li data-section-id=\"1buadtk\" data-start=\"2114\" data-end=\"2140\" data-list-item-id=\"e70affa428589ecb6cf0dbcc3d0899306\"><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">Instant return at pickup</p></li><li data-section-id=\"6983iv\" data-start=\"2141\" data-end=\"2180\" data-list-item-id=\"e3b6af6c5e29da5e36d6a70766452d6df\"><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">Pickup point earnings / payout system</p></li></ul><h3 style=\"text-align:justify;\" data-section-id=\"cbyxxr\" data-start=\"2187\" data-end=\"2211\">6. Payment System</h3><p style=\"text-align:justify;\" data-start=\"2212\" data-end=\"2237\">Money flow must be solid.</p><ul data-start=\"2239\" data-end=\"2414\"><li data-section-id=\"283ak7\" data-start=\"2239\" data-end=\"2283\" data-list-item-id=\"ecce18cca058ea92ee1903e97821ff2b4\"><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">Online payments (Stripe, SSLCommerz, etc.)</p></li><li data-section-id=\"ccn0it\" data-start=\"2284\" data-end=\"2308\" data-list-item-id=\"edaefc358ee03728454ad9f6884695cb2\"><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">Cash on Delivery (COD)</p></li><li data-section-id=\"u8yt0l\" data-start=\"2309\" data-end=\"2335\" data-list-item-id=\"e2d1a37972efc190c1db7557bc9a28cd6\"><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">Wallet system (optional)</p></li><li data-section-id=\"1ctls8z\" data-start=\"2336\" data-end=\"2358\" data-list-item-id=\"e09cac07e3d6a37062737e9683e239cd3\"><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">Transaction tracking</p></li><li data-section-id=\"vhz7g8\" data-start=\"2359\" data-end=\"2391\" data-list-item-id=\"e910318ceaaaaa6e814a74b50bbdeb62c\"><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">Refund &amp; partial refund system</p></li><li data-section-id=\"pp2ymn\" data-start=\"2392\" data-end=\"2414\" data-list-item-id=\"e7e621c6649a3214fa085654272fd7852\"><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">Vendor payout system</p></li></ul><h3 style=\"text-align:justify;\" data-section-id=\"x2pn6h\" data-start=\"2421\" data-end=\"2458\">7. Marketing &amp; Campaign System</h3><p style=\"text-align:justify;\" data-start=\"2459\" data-end=\"2489\">Growth engine of the platform.</p><ul data-start=\"2491\" data-end=\"2695\"><li data-section-id=\"lf3kx4\" data-start=\"2491\" data-end=\"2519\" data-list-item-id=\"e8fd2268f995e58ee391a22e418e1ddc8\"><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">Coupon / promo code system</p></li><li data-section-id=\"1gwl4qg\" data-start=\"2520\" data-end=\"2545\" data-list-item-id=\"e118edcf55dd000803c44300b973baf1e\"><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">Flash sales &amp; discounts</p></li><li data-section-id=\"8fw578\" data-start=\"2546\" data-end=\"2601\" data-list-item-id=\"e582edb6620100e7d330562b0c22ad95c\"><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">Social campaigns (FB/Instagram like/comment tracking)</p></li><li data-section-id=\"v2bu9y\" data-start=\"2602\" data-end=\"2630\" data-list-item-id=\"efdabbbf194ff774c9f6783f7d6a1ff60\"><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">Spin-to-win rewards system</p></li><li data-section-id=\"ecxrt2\" data-start=\"2631\" data-end=\"2660\" data-list-item-id=\"e4363da5e8006ba5c752778b60ec514f0\"><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">Affiliate / referral system</p></li><li data-section-id=\"1o7gz3d\" data-start=\"2661\" data-end=\"2695\" data-list-item-id=\"ea2f73394256fdd095e4c10d7c547477e\"><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">Email / SMS / push notifications</p></li></ul><h3 style=\"text-align:justify;\" data-section-id=\"ddlkem\" data-start=\"2702\" data-end=\"2737\">8. Security &amp; Access Control</h3><p style=\"text-align:justify;\" data-start=\"2738\" data-end=\"2766\">Without this, system breaks.</p><ul data-start=\"2768\" data-end=\"2953\"><li data-section-id=\"1ur78zz\" data-start=\"2768\" data-end=\"2821\" data-list-item-id=\"ebfca5ee36969666ee07b8f7a78da2a94\"><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">Role-based access (admin, seller, delivery, pickup)</p></li><li data-section-id=\"yhrsb4\" data-start=\"2822\" data-end=\"2856\" data-list-item-id=\"e5126fd2a4ddbb5c57b3524d39ced9956\"><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">API authentication (JWT / OAuth)</p></li><li data-section-id=\"1d9srq2\" data-start=\"2857\" data-end=\"2889\" data-list-item-id=\"e69d42523a1eb0b19c6a263645b4d0072\"><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">Data validation &amp; sanitization</p></li><li data-section-id=\"hnym4y\" data-start=\"2890\" data-end=\"2927\" data-list-item-id=\"eb5ddc2d8f479174ce2d2c814552e2f4e\"><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">Fraud detection (optional advanced)</p></li><li data-section-id=\"3vr4ui\" data-start=\"2928\" data-end=\"2953\" data-list-item-id=\"ebe69ce1358bac1be658c9a2956164114\"><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">Secure payment handling</p></li></ul><h3 style=\"text-align:justify;\" data-section-id=\"14nltzs\" data-start=\"2960\" data-end=\"2991\">9. Analytics &amp; Reporting</h3><p style=\"text-align:justify;\" data-start=\"2992\" data-end=\"3012\">For decision making.</p><ul data-start=\"3014\" data-end=\"3176\"><li data-section-id=\"8lfl33\" data-start=\"3014\" data-end=\"3057\" data-list-item-id=\"ec3474b29f7c37bddc03b6b21200a4654\"><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">Sales reports (vendor-wise, product-wise)</p></li><li data-section-id=\"mytzyz\" data-start=\"3058\" data-end=\"3073\" data-list-item-id=\"eadc845b350c0fb986ba98881f4c3eca7\"><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">Order reports</p></li><li data-section-id=\"1vv2fu7\" data-start=\"3074\" data-end=\"3102\" data-list-item-id=\"e601dff807a0d2e8e925f65035484fbf1\"><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">Customer behavior tracking</p></li><li data-section-id=\"1fd1f97\" data-start=\"3103\" data-end=\"3133\" data-list-item-id=\"e6cf174c7b1fe7c3c6e8ec21449aae8da\"><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">Delivery performance metrics</p></li><li data-section-id=\"xo3ycf\" data-start=\"3134\" data-end=\"3153\" data-list-item-id=\"eec2ef3506c9d8197cdc6f842b3f97564\"><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">Revenue breakdown</p></li><li data-section-id=\"1u791m6\" data-start=\"3154\" data-end=\"3176\" data-list-item-id=\"e6e315b010db52675c4465fd0b2d72e1a\"><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">Campaign performance</p></li></ul><h3 style=\"text-align:justify;\" data-section-id=\"p4xemk\" data-start=\"3183\" data-end=\"3218\">10. System &amp; Technical Layer</h3><ul data-start=\"3220\" data-end=\"3441\"><li data-section-id=\"1tezq10\" data-start=\"3220\" data-end=\"3248\" data-list-item-id=\"e3af16e50a32159959bae0463d6316093\"><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">REST API (Laravel backend)</p></li><li data-section-id=\"1h19jl3\" data-start=\"3249\" data-end=\"3285\" data-list-item-id=\"eb50127948648de8956989f81682022fb\"><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">Database (MySQL optimized queries)</p></li><li data-section-id=\"rngzs8\" data-start=\"3286\" data-end=\"3330\" data-list-item-id=\"e6384e2012d3cdf4fce53de3cae2dcb3b\"><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">Queue system (emails, notifications, jobs)</p></li><li data-section-id=\"1veoxvr\" data-start=\"3331\" data-end=\"3357\" data-list-item-id=\"ee3ae4bf81e7f84da2ad4f15b4d54e700\"><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">Caching (Redis optional)</p></li><li data-section-id=\"z0mcy\" data-start=\"3358\" data-end=\"3392\" data-list-item-id=\"ecd5143a1f0c7da51b7798365926909ba\"><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">File storage (images, documents)</p></li><li data-section-id=\"11v4a9z\" data-start=\"3393\" data-end=\"3412\" data-list-item-id=\"e166e88cc7cd44c0bf6bf0ec74d661219\"><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">API rate limiting</p></li><li data-section-id=\"ulwjax\" data-start=\"3413\" data-end=\"3441\" data-list-item-id=\"e7d15cfbe7c67bfb6032e2a608dca2050\"><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">Error logging &amp; monitoring</p></li></ul><p style=\"text-align:justify;\" data-start=\"18\" data-end=\"349\">A modern e-commerce platform isn’t just about buying and selling products—it’s about orchestrating an entire ecosystem. From customers placing orders to sellers managing inventory, and from logistics teams handling deliveries to pickup points verifying parcels, every component must work together seamlessly.</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\" data-start=\"18\" data-end=\"349\">&nbsp;</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\" data-start=\"351\" data-end=\"770\">This system is designed with that bigger picture in mind. By combining a Laravel-powered backend, a structured MySQL database, and multiple role-based Flutter applications, it creates a unified yet flexible environment where each stakeholder operates efficiently without overlap or confusion. Real-time synchronization, automation, and role-based access ensure that operations remain smooth even as the platform scales.</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\" data-start=\"351\" data-end=\"770\">&nbsp;</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\" data-start=\"772\" data-end=\"1039\">What this really means is scalability without chaos. As more vendors join, orders increase, and logistics expand, the system remains stable, organized, and responsive. That’s the difference between a basic online store and a truly scalable marketplace infrastructure.</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\" data-start=\"772\" data-end=\"1039\">&nbsp;</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\" data-start=\"1041\" data-end=\"1199\" data-is-last-node=\"\" data-is-only-node=\"\">In short, this project represents a shift from building features to building systems where technology doesn’t just support the business, it drives it forward.</p>'),
(7, 'Real-Time Server Health Monitoring', 'A full-stack, real-time server monitoring dashboard that tracks the health, availability, and latency of multiple target URLs simultaneously. Built with a scalable architecture, it streams live system metrics directly to the browser using Socket.IO, with role-based access control and a fully Dockerized production setup.', '[\"React.js\",\"TypeScript\",\"Node.js\",\"Express.js\",\"Socket.IO\",\"Python\",\"Flask\",\"psutil\",\"JWT\",\"SQLite\",\"Docker\",\"Docker Compose\",\"Nginx\"]', 'Full Stuck Developer', '', '', 7, '2026-05-01 22:58:25.574', '2026-07-09 05:10:23.959', '/uploads/1777672077408-1776343401478.jpg', 69, 115, '[]', 'real-time-server-health-monitoring', '<p style=\"text-align:justify;\" data-start=\"557\" data-end=\"990\">Monitoring system health in real time is critical for maintaining reliability in modern applications. In this project, I built a full-stack server monitoring dashboard designed to track the availability, latency, and overall performance of multiple target URLs simultaneously. The idea was to create a system that doesn’t just log data, but actively streams live metrics to the frontend, giving instant visibility into system status.</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\" data-start=\"557\" data-end=\"990\">&nbsp;</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\" data-start=\"992\" data-end=\"1419\">At the core of the platform is a Node.js and Express-based backend that handles API communication, scheduling, and real-time updates through Socket.IO. Instead of relying on static polling, the system pushes live data directly to connected clients, ensuring that users always see the latest system state without refreshing the page. This makes the dashboard highly responsive and suitable for real-time monitoring environments.</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\" data-start=\"992\" data-end=\"1419\">&nbsp;</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\" data-start=\"1421\" data-end=\"1809\">To extend monitoring beyond basic uptime checks, I integrated a Python-based telemetry agent built with Flask and psutil. This agent collects system-level metrics such as CPU usage, memory consumption, and process data, providing deeper insights into server performance. By combining URL health checks with internal system metrics, the platform offers a more complete monitoring solution.</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\" data-start=\"1421\" data-end=\"1809\">&nbsp;</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\" data-start=\"1811\" data-end=\"2282\">The architecture is designed with scalability in mind. The system separates the API layer from the scheduler, allowing independent scaling and smoother deployment in containerized environments. It supports both SQLite and PostgreSQL as database backends, making it flexible for development and production use cases. Role-based authentication using JWT ensures that access is controlled, with Admin users having full control and Viewers limited to monitoring capabilities.</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\" data-start=\"1811\" data-end=\"2282\">&nbsp;</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\" data-start=\"2284\" data-end=\"2624\">From an infrastructure perspective, the entire system is fully Dockerized, making deployment consistent and reproducible across environments. Nginx is used as a reverse proxy to handle routing and improve production readiness. This setup ensures that the platform can handle real-world workloads while maintaining stability and performance.</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\" data-start=\"2626\" data-end=\"2815\">Overall, this project demonstrates how real-time technologies, combined with a modular and scalable architecture, can transform simple monitoring into a powerful, live observability system.</p><h2 style=\"text-align:justify;\" data-section-id=\"1b6xs1m\" data-start=\"2822\" data-end=\"2849\">Tools &amp; Technologies</h2><ul><li data-list-item-id=\"e07d8992fed8d8fef30c0ef011cb67fd8\"><p style=\"text-align:justify;\" data-start=\"2851\" data-end=\"2887\"><strong data-start=\"2851\" data-end=\"2864\">Frontend:</strong> React.js, TypeScript</p></li><li data-list-item-id=\"e724fdeb763fbebb001c44e1292a2e8f2\"><p style=\"text-align:justify;\" data-start=\"2889\" data-end=\"2946\"><strong data-start=\"2889\" data-end=\"2901\">Backend:</strong> Node.js, Express.js, TypeScript, Socket.IO</p></li><li data-list-item-id=\"e4b9eb86c3fdd608e47469f82a81b388e\"><p style=\"text-align:justify;\" data-start=\"2948\" data-end=\"2992\"><strong data-start=\"2948\" data-end=\"2968\">Telemetry Agent:</strong> Python, Flask, psutil</p></li><li data-list-item-id=\"e3732c7c93b5100b356388c75138bb446\"><p style=\"text-align:justify;\" data-start=\"2994\" data-end=\"3054\"><strong data-start=\"2994\" data-end=\"3013\">Authentication:</strong> JWT-based role access (Admin / Viewer)</p></li><li data-list-item-id=\"ea408de201129c8fe06dfffc6710153f6\"><p style=\"text-align:justify;\" data-start=\"3056\" data-end=\"3090\"><strong data-start=\"3056\" data-end=\"3069\">Database:</strong> SQLite, PostgreSQL</p></li><li data-list-item-id=\"ec289993b558e9b9f360ce1c4559b7531\"><p style=\"text-align:justify;\" data-start=\"3092\" data-end=\"3143\"><strong data-start=\"3092\" data-end=\"3111\">Infrastructure:</strong> Docker, Docker Compose, Nginx</p></li></ul><p style=\"text-align:justify;\" data-start=\"3145\" data-end=\"3162\"><strong data-start=\"3145\" data-end=\"3162\">Core Systems:</strong></p><ul data-start=\"3163\" data-end=\"3314\"><li data-section-id=\"mh1ek0\" data-start=\"3163\" data-end=\"3215\" data-list-item-id=\"e11bbc1768df8dafd5b3596f9e30524b8\"><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">Real-time data streaming (WebSocket / Socket.IO)</p></li><li data-section-id=\"1dgvul2\" data-start=\"3216\" data-end=\"3247\" data-list-item-id=\"eaf1b4662bd48df1f57bb41ff8045c664\"><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">Health &amp; latency monitoring</p></li><li data-section-id=\"1nbaz7t\" data-start=\"3248\" data-end=\"3282\" data-list-item-id=\"eba8857cacc7d2bc34c73c184962a97b1\"><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">Scheduler-based probing system</p></li><li data-section-id=\"11syhpc\" data-start=\"3283\" data-end=\"3314\" data-list-item-id=\"e693c597002cf7cd3a85580e71c4e7541\"><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">Role-based dashboard access</p></li></ul><p style=\"text-align:justify;\" data-start=\"3316\" data-end=\"3340\"><strong data-start=\"3316\" data-end=\"3340\">Deployment Features:</strong></p><ul data-start=\"3341\" data-end=\"3430\"><li data-section-id=\"1cy8x4j\" data-start=\"3341\" data-end=\"3367\" data-list-item-id=\"e3373644fd90ab5cdf44a13746654fb69\"><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">Containerized services</p></li><li data-section-id=\"in0b7n\" data-start=\"3368\" data-end=\"3391\" data-list-item-id=\"e5d26d4382780b85f19a3b4f98f1e6894\"><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">Reverse proxy setup</p></li><li data-section-id=\"ig7c7j\" data-start=\"3392\" data-end=\"3430\" data-list-item-id=\"e06c6e1e5653bb7c21597d5ceba6b2163\"><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">Scalable API + worker architecture</p></li></ul><p style=\"text-align:justify;\" data-start=\"18\" data-end=\"383\">This project goes beyond basic uptime monitoring and moves toward a real-time observability system that provides immediate insight into both external service health and internal server performance. By combining live data streaming with system-level telemetry, it delivers a clear and continuous view of what’s happening across multiple services at any given moment.</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\" data-start=\"385\" data-end=\"722\">&nbsp;</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\" data-start=\"385\" data-end=\"722\">The use of a modular architecture with a separate API layer, scheduler, and telemetry agent ensures that the system remains scalable and easy to extend. Real-time updates via Socket.IO eliminate delays in monitoring, while Dockerized deployment and Nginx integration make the platform production-ready and consistent across environments.</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\" data-start=\"724\" data-end=\"1011\" data-is-last-node=\"\" data-is-only-node=\"\">&nbsp;</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\" data-start=\"724\" data-end=\"1011\" data-is-last-node=\"\" data-is-only-node=\"\">In the end, this dashboard demonstrates how modern tools and thoughtful system design can transform monitoring from a passive process into an active, real-time experience helping developers and teams respond faster, make better decisions, and maintain system reliability with confidence.</p>');
INSERT INTO `Project` (`id`, `name`, `description`, `tools`, `role`, `code`, `demo`, `sortOrder`, `createdAt`, `updatedAt`, `image`, `views`, `impressionCount`, `buttons`, `slug`, `content`) VALUES
(8, 'Wireless Vision-Aid for the Blind', 'A low-cost, real-time assistive system designed for visually impaired users that combines YOLOv8n-based object detection, ultra-low latency UDP streaming, and multilingual audio feedback. WVAB delivers directional navigation cues with high accuracy, operating fully offline with hardware costs under $15.', '[\"YOLOv8n\",\"Python\",\"C++\",\"Raspberry Pi\",\"ESP32-CAM\",\"Text-to-Speech (TTS)\",\"COCO dataset\"]', 'System Architect & Developer', 'https://github.com/smshagor-dev/wireless-Vision-Aid-for-the-blind', '', 8, '2026-05-01 22:58:25.574', '2026-07-07 13:37:29.273', '/uploads/1777672757741-1776343238023.jpg', 75, 114, '[{\"text\":\"Code\",\"link\":\"https://github.com/smshagor-dev/wireless-Vision-Aid-for-the-blind\"}]', 'wireless-vision-aid-for-the-blind', '<p style=\"text-align:justify;\" data-start=\"538\" data-end=\"1048\">Visual impairment continues to be a major global challenge, affecting over 285 million people and limiting independent mobility in daily life. While existing assistive technologies offer partial solutions, they often come with high costs, language limitations, and dependency on cloud-based services. In this research, I developed WVAB (Wireless Vision-Aid for the Blind), a cost-effective, real-time navigation system designed to address these limitations through edge computing and intelligent system design.</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\" data-start=\"538\" data-end=\"1048\">&nbsp;</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\" data-start=\"1050\" data-end=\"1517\">The system is built around a YOLOv8n-based object detection pipeline, optimized for lightweight performance and real-time inference. Instead of relying on cloud processing, WVAB performs all computations locally, ensuring faster response times and complete offline functionality. A custom UDP-based streaming protocol enables ultra-low latency communication between the camera module and the processing unit, allowing continuous video transmission with minimal delay.</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\" data-start=\"1050\" data-end=\"1517\">&nbsp;</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\" data-start=\"1519\" data-end=\"2034\">To convert visual data into meaningful guidance, the system integrates a C++-based NavigationPlanner engine that analyzes detected objects and assigns risk levels based on proximity and position. This allows the system to generate simple yet effective navigation instructions such as Left, Center, or Right, combined with proximity levels like Immediate, Near, or Far. These instructions are delivered through multilingual audio feedback, making the system accessible to users across different language backgrounds.</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\" data-start=\"1519\" data-end=\"2034\">&nbsp;</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\" data-start=\"2036\" data-end=\"2547\">A key strength of WVAB is its performance efficiency. Experimental results show end-to-end latency below 50 milliseconds while maintaining 15–30 FPS, ensuring real-time responsiveness. The system achieves a mAP@0.5 score of 0.472 on the COCO dataset and demonstrates over 91% accuracy in navigation decision-making within complex indoor environments. Despite these capabilities, the entire hardware setup costs less than 15 USD, making it significantly more accessible compared to existing commercial solutions.</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\" data-start=\"2036\" data-end=\"2547\">&nbsp;</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\" data-start=\"2549\" data-end=\"2835\">By combining affordability, real-time performance, and multilingual accessibility, WVAB represents a practical step toward inclusive assistive technology. It demonstrates how edge AI and optimized system design can create impactful solutions without relying on expensive infrastructure.</p><h2 style=\"text-align:justify;\" data-section-id=\"1b6xs1m\" data-start=\"2842\" data-end=\"2869\">Tools &amp; Technologies</h2><ul><li data-list-item-id=\"ee32241f4c2899e006d337243f2fb43a5\"><p style=\"text-align:justify;\" data-start=\"2871\" data-end=\"2920\"><strong data-start=\"2871\" data-end=\"2891\">Computer Vision:</strong> YOLOv8n (object detection)</p></li><li data-list-item-id=\"eccd0110d26d815f25e2f66c6af668fdb\"><p style=\"text-align:justify;\" data-start=\"2922\" data-end=\"2962\"><strong data-start=\"2922\" data-end=\"2948\">Programming Languages:</strong> Python, C++</p></li><li data-list-item-id=\"ef8785ba0ab77fe4b2962d8e53838eedf\"><p style=\"text-align:justify;\" data-start=\"2964\" data-end=\"3034\"><strong data-start=\"2964\" data-end=\"2987\">Streaming Protocol:</strong> Custom UDP-based low-latency video streaming</p></li><li data-list-item-id=\"e1fc03f47b5a0686323ef24fe6d1ff5dc\"><p style=\"text-align:justify;\" data-start=\"3036\" data-end=\"3097\"><strong data-start=\"3036\" data-end=\"3054\">AI Processing:</strong> Edge-based real-time inference (offline)</p></li><li data-list-item-id=\"e86f1121d78ecc93a820ee95a3be719ef\"><p style=\"text-align:justify;\" data-start=\"3099\" data-end=\"3159\"><strong data-start=\"3099\" data-end=\"3121\">Navigation Engine:</strong> C++ Risk-weighted NavigationPlanner</p></li><li data-list-item-id=\"eac20de44d80d7d2375c48eb80c602fd6\"><p style=\"text-align:justify;\" data-start=\"3161\" data-end=\"3214\"><strong data-start=\"3161\" data-end=\"3178\">Audio System:</strong> Multilingual Text-to-Speech (TTS)</p></li><li data-list-item-id=\"ef24ecd3553be8d9bfae866128df62d22\"><p style=\"text-align:justify;\" data-start=\"3216\" data-end=\"3266\"><strong data-start=\"3216\" data-end=\"3234\">Data Handling:</strong> JSON-based label architecture</p></li><li data-list-item-id=\"e51aee871b0409d18feab56166533b2b5\"><p style=\"text-align:justify;\" data-start=\"3268\" data-end=\"3318\"><strong data-start=\"3268\" data-end=\"3280\">Dataset:</strong> COCO dataset (for model evaluation)</p></li></ul><p style=\"text-align:justify;\" data-start=\"3320\" data-end=\"3333\"><strong data-start=\"3320\" data-end=\"3333\">Hardware:</strong></p><ul data-start=\"3334\" data-end=\"3443\"><li data-section-id=\"2q4uzd\" data-start=\"3334\" data-end=\"3363\" data-list-item-id=\"e1592845df20f68626ac056f9eead191a\"><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">ESP32-CAM (video capture)</p></li><li data-section-id=\"9y6w43\" data-start=\"3364\" data-end=\"3398\" data-list-item-id=\"ef408fb6d0549b8ade5df839393254dea\"><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">Raspberry Pi (processing unit)</p></li><li data-section-id=\"52mg5a\" data-start=\"3399\" data-end=\"3443\" data-list-item-id=\"e64dba18a64d71bdaf74621e11ec066d9\"><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">Audio output (Bluetooth / wired headset)</p></li></ul><p style=\"text-align:justify;\" data-start=\"3445\" data-end=\"3463\"><strong data-start=\"3445\" data-end=\"3463\">Core Features:</strong></p><ul data-start=\"3464\" data-end=\"3650\"><li data-section-id=\"bfr6i8\" data-start=\"3464\" data-end=\"3494\" data-list-item-id=\"e2b507323a963daa17b2bbe7b6e9b4171\"><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">Real-time object detection</p></li><li data-section-id=\"1jgk8ez\" data-start=\"3495\" data-end=\"3545\" data-list-item-id=\"e2bd32fe5d829ed1605c9658d5aff0f59\"><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">Directional navigation (Left / Center / Right)</p></li><li data-section-id=\"cr1kgh\" data-start=\"3546\" data-end=\"3588\" data-list-item-id=\"ea0d25537222e14413f65214a9f36f9e0\"><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">Proximity estimation (Immediate → Far)</p></li><li data-section-id=\"178i8yy\" data-start=\"3589\" data-end=\"3620\" data-list-item-id=\"e148dcec12591ec0e78df91afb6aed134\"><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">Multilingual voice feedback</p></li><li data-section-id=\"1axngo1\" data-start=\"3621\" data-end=\"3650\" data-list-item-id=\"e031ae62ddfed2f4d613224985210478a\"><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">Ultra-low latency (&lt;50ms)</p></li></ul><p style=\"text-align:justify;\" data-start=\"3675\" data-end=\"4130\">WVAB demonstrates that advanced assistive technology does not need to be expensive or cloud-dependent to be effective. By combining real-time object detection, low-latency communication, and intelligent navigation logic, the system delivers reliable guidance in a lightweight and affordable form. Its ability to operate بالكامل offline while maintaining high accuracy and responsiveness makes it especially valuable for users in low-resource environments.</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\" data-start=\"3675\" data-end=\"4130\">&nbsp;</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\" data-start=\"4132\" data-end=\"4479\">Ultimately, this project highlights how thoughtful integration of edge AI, efficient system design, and accessibility-focused features can create meaningful impact. WVAB is not just a prototype it represents a scalable direction for building inclusive technologies that empower visually impaired individuals with greater independence and mobility.</p>'),
(9, 'SyncChat – Real-Time Communication Engine', 'A high-performance, real-time communication system designed for seamless messaging across web and mobile platforms. SyncChat leverages WebSocket and WebRTC technologies to deliver instant messaging, live interactions, and scalable communication with low latency and high reliability.', '[\"Node.js\",\"React.js (Web)\",\"Flutter (Mobile)\",\"WebSocket\",\"WebRTC\",\"TypeScript\",\"JavaScript\",\"MySQL\",\"Firebase Intregration\",\"Micro Server\"]', 'Full Stuck Developer', '', '', 9, '2026-05-01 22:58:25.574', '2026-07-07 14:54:03.742', '/uploads/1777673866469-0c741297-8cbf-4310-9695-cf18f91c6f79.png', 68, 116, '[]', 'syncchat-real-time-communication-engine', '<p style=\"text-align:justify;\" data-start=\"528\" data-end=\"951\">Real-time communication has become a core requirement in modern applications, where users expect instant responses and seamless interactions. SyncChat was built to meet this demand by providing a fast, reliable, and scalable messaging system that works across both web and mobile platforms. The focus of this project was to create a smooth communication experience while maintaining high performance under concurrent usage.</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\" data-start=\"528\" data-end=\"951\">&nbsp;</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\" data-start=\"953\" data-end=\"1430\">At the heart of SyncChat is a real-time architecture powered by WebSocket technology, enabling instant message delivery without the need for repeated requests. This ensures that messages, typing indicators, and read receipts are updated in real time, creating a natural and responsive chat experience. For more advanced communication, WebRTC is integrated to support peer-to-peer data exchange, making the system suitable for future expansion into voice or video communication.</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\" data-start=\"953\" data-end=\"1430\">&nbsp;</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\" data-start=\"1432\" data-end=\"1817\">The platform supports both one-to-one and group conversations, allowing users to communicate in different contexts. It also includes media and file sharing capabilities, enabling users to send images, documents, and other content directly within chats. Message synchronization ensures that conversations remain consistent across devices, providing a seamless cross-platform experience.</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\" data-start=\"1432\" data-end=\"1817\">&nbsp;</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\" data-start=\"1819\" data-end=\"2166\">On the backend, Node.js and Laravel are used to manage APIs, real-time events, and business logic, while MySQL handles structured data storage. The frontend is built with React for web and Flutter for mobile, ensuring consistency across platforms. TypeScript is used throughout the system to improve code quality, maintainability, and scalability.</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\" data-start=\"1819\" data-end=\"2166\">&nbsp;</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\" data-start=\"2168\" data-end=\"2442\">The architecture is designed to handle high concurrency and real-time event processing efficiently. By combining scalable backend services with optimized real-time communication protocols, SyncChat delivers a stable and responsive messaging experience even under heavy load.</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\" data-start=\"2168\" data-end=\"2442\">&nbsp;</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\" data-start=\"2444\" data-end=\"2624\">Overall, SyncChat represents a modern communication engine that combines speed, scalability, and flexibility making it suitable for building next-generation messaging applications.</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\" data-start=\"2444\" data-end=\"2624\">Tools &amp; Technologies</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\" data-start=\"2660\" data-end=\"2691\"><strong data-start=\"2660\" data-end=\"2672\">Backend:</strong> Node.js, Laravel</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\" data-start=\"2693\" data-end=\"2738\"><strong data-start=\"2693\" data-end=\"2706\">Frontend:</strong> React (Web), Flutter (Mobile)</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\" data-start=\"2740\" data-end=\"2789\"><strong data-start=\"2740\" data-end=\"2768\">Real-Time Communication:</strong> WebSockets, WebRTC</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\" data-start=\"2791\" data-end=\"2842\"><strong data-start=\"2791\" data-end=\"2817\">Programming Languages:</strong> TypeScript, JavaScript</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\" data-start=\"2844\" data-end=\"2865\"><strong data-start=\"2844\" data-end=\"2857\">Database:</strong> MySQL</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\" data-start=\"2867\" data-end=\"2885\"><strong data-start=\"2867\" data-end=\"2885\">Core Features:</strong></p><ul data-start=\"2886\" data-end=\"3072\"><li data-section-id=\"15umjhe\" data-start=\"2886\" data-end=\"2928\" data-list-item-id=\"e577bd49b6d1a5b6da3b4e03da9e60347\"><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">Real-time messaging (instant delivery)</p></li><li data-section-id=\"1j0xh8\" data-start=\"2929\" data-end=\"2966\" data-list-item-id=\"e7cb95501bc0135e7febd612ab118e461\"><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">Typing indicators &amp; read receipts</p></li><li data-section-id=\"rvvfw6\" data-start=\"2967\" data-end=\"3004\" data-list-item-id=\"ef2fadeff7ef56442982ddcd2b451a2fe\"><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">One-to-one and group chat support</p></li><li data-section-id=\"15zfzt0\" data-start=\"3005\" data-end=\"3029\" data-list-item-id=\"ec19a5ca4eb67883e4888f2516ed34443\"><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">Media &amp; file sharing</p></li><li data-section-id=\"57iy11\" data-start=\"3030\" data-end=\"3072\" data-list-item-id=\"e1c031113242d845abdd5e9d494c1d2d4\"><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">Message synchronization across devices</p></li></ul><p style=\"text-align:justify;\" data-start=\"3074\" data-end=\"3098\"><strong data-start=\"3074\" data-end=\"3098\">System Capabilities:</strong></p><ul data-start=\"3099\" data-end=\"3234\"><li data-section-id=\"1cb5dpo\" data-start=\"3099\" data-end=\"3128\" data-list-item-id=\"e057a88efb2ea072ed410f7d64dcfef9c\"><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">High concurrency handling</p></li><li data-section-id=\"rj0526\" data-start=\"3129\" data-end=\"3158\" data-list-item-id=\"eb49dcf0da183bf0343e50fdab3a66143\"><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">Event-driven architecture</p></li><li data-section-id=\"1f6oj01\" data-start=\"3159\" data-end=\"3192\" data-list-item-id=\"ec09aaa79f413599cccd66ec57baaed17\"><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">Scalable communication engine</p></li><li data-section-id=\"1avemy9\" data-start=\"3193\" data-end=\"3234\" data-list-item-id=\"e911a80856af63af46bc90924e6369331\"><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">Cross-platform support (Web + Mobile)</p></li></ul><h2 style=\"text-align:justify;\" data-section-id=\"65tu0p\" data-start=\"3241\" data-end=\"3264\">Developer Role</h2><p style=\"text-align:justify;\" data-start=\"3266\" data-end=\"3309\"><strong data-start=\"3266\" data-end=\"3309\">Full-Stack Developer &amp; System Architect</strong></p><ul data-start=\"3311\" data-end=\"4066\"><li data-section-id=\"bwtld7\" data-start=\"3311\" data-end=\"3410\" data-list-item-id=\"e12a07b2ac3f5adfc8fc18ce39b53abff\"><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">Designed the <strong data-start=\"3326\" data-end=\"3366\">real-time communication architecture</strong> using WebSockets and event-driven systems</p></li><li data-section-id=\"1fr76h9\" data-start=\"3411\" data-end=\"3496\" data-list-item-id=\"e78129c71b027c8394a42c4bb8b77fc2d\"><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">Implemented <strong data-start=\"3425\" data-end=\"3453\">instant messaging system</strong> with typing indicators and read receipts</p></li><li data-section-id=\"1r70um4\" data-start=\"3497\" data-end=\"3566\" data-list-item-id=\"ec2bcc7bf2caa8ad8f459afa8de45e67f\"><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">Integrated <strong data-start=\"3510\" data-end=\"3564\">WebRTC for peer-to-peer communication capabilities</strong></p></li><li data-section-id=\"9mdexg\" data-start=\"3567\" data-end=\"3650\" data-list-item-id=\"e3e162ad38002902cd121c129c6f83d3c\"><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">Built backend services using <strong data-start=\"3598\" data-end=\"3621\">Node.js and Laravel</strong> for API and event handling</p></li><li data-section-id=\"1tazk7y\" data-start=\"3651\" data-end=\"3731\" data-list-item-id=\"e3be1042c76b08b8c998de7cd8705975a\"><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">Developed <strong data-start=\"3663\" data-end=\"3690\">cross-platform frontend</strong> using React (web) and Flutter (mobile)</p></li><li data-section-id=\"1c3ml9r\" data-start=\"3732\" data-end=\"3812\" data-list-item-id=\"eba99df8418921e4a95b632d85197c565\"><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">Designed and managed <strong data-start=\"3755\" data-end=\"3780\">MySQL database schema</strong> for chat, users, and messages</p></li><li data-section-id=\"1mm0s49\" data-start=\"3813\" data-end=\"3874\" data-list-item-id=\"e65db95a3a8e14aff6015cb66375f4632\"><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">Implemented <strong data-start=\"3827\" data-end=\"3860\">media and file sharing system</strong> within chat</p></li><li data-section-id=\"gp71uj\" data-start=\"3875\" data-end=\"3929\" data-list-item-id=\"eb362832dad8d858b15a0a7e53668f117\"><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">Ensured <strong data-start=\"3885\" data-end=\"3927\">message synchronization across devices</strong></p></li><li data-section-id=\"19e86dw\" data-start=\"3930\" data-end=\"3992\" data-list-item-id=\"ef81bf437b8e7edfb93f5a2c73fa9a0a6\"><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">Used <strong data-start=\"3937\" data-end=\"3990\">TypeScript for scalable and maintainable codebase</strong></p></li><li data-section-id=\"p2ga5r\" data-start=\"3993\" data-end=\"4066\" data-list-item-id=\"ed886cef652bb5e71525c9b1aa8c5cf39\"><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">Optimized system for <strong data-start=\"4016\" data-end=\"4066\">performance, low latency, and high concurrency</strong></p></li></ul><p style=\"text-align:justify;\" data-start=\"4091\" data-end=\"4388\">SyncChat demonstrates how real-time technologies can be combined to create a fast, scalable, and user-friendly communication system. By leveraging WebSockets for instant updates and WebRTC for advanced communication capabilities, the platform delivers a smooth and responsive messaging experience.</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\" data-start=\"4390\" data-end=\"4682\">&nbsp;</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\" data-start=\"4390\" data-end=\"4682\">The system’s modular and scalable architecture ensures that it can grow with user demand while maintaining performance and stability. With support for cross-platform applications and real-time synchronization, SyncChat provides a strong foundation for building modern communication platforms.</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\" data-start=\"4684\" data-end=\"4846\" data-is-last-node=\"\" data-is-only-node=\"\">&nbsp;</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\" data-start=\"4684\" data-end=\"4846\" data-is-last-node=\"\" data-is-only-node=\"\">In the end, this project reflects a shift toward event-driven, real-time systems where speed, responsiveness, and seamless interaction define the user experience.</p>'),
(10, 'Privacy-Preserving Blockchain Framework for Autonomous Vehicles', 'A decentralized, privacy-first security framework designed to protect Vehicle-to-Everything (V2X) communication using blockchain and advanced cryptography. OmniGuard V2X ensures data integrity, anonymity, and resilience against cyber and post-quantum threats in smart city environments.', '[\"C++\",\"Python\",\"YOLOv8\",\"NVIDIA Jetson Nano\",\"ESP32\",\"Raspberry Pi\",\"Zero-Knowledge Proofs\",\"Post-Quantum Cryptography\"]', 'Security Engineer', 'https://github.com/smshagor-dev/Next-Gen-Blockchain-for-Vehicle-Security', '', 10, '2026-05-01 22:58:25.574', '2026-07-07 13:37:29.259', '/uploads/1777676244363-1111.png', 68, 117, '[{\"text\":\"Code\",\"link\":\"https://github.com/smshagor-dev/Next-Gen-Blockchain-for-Vehicle-Security\"}]', 'privacy-preserving-blockchain-framework-for-autonomous-vehicles', '<h2 style=\"text-align:justify;\">OmniGuard V2X – Privacy-Preserving Blockchain Framework for Autonomous Vehicle Networks</h2><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">&nbsp;</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">As autonomous vehicles and smart city infrastructures continue to evolve, secure communication between vehicles and surrounding systems has become a critical challenge. Vehicle-to-Everything (V2X) networks enable real-time data exchange between vehicles, infrastructure, and other entities, but they also introduce significant risks related to data integrity, privacy, and cyberattacks. OmniGuard V2X was developed to address these challenges by building a decentralized, privacy-preserving security framework tailored for next-generation autonomous systems.</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">&nbsp;</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">At its core, OmniGuard V2X integrates blockchain technology to create a tamper-proof communication layer. Instead of relying on centralized authorities, the system uses a distributed ledger to validate and store inter-vehicle communication data. Each message is cryptographically linked using SHA3-256 chaining, ensuring that any attempt to alter data is immediately detectable. This approach significantly enhances trust and transparency within the network.</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">&nbsp;</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">Privacy is a central focus of the framework. Traditional authentication systems often expose sensitive information such as vehicle identity or location. To solve this, OmniGuard V2X implements Zero-Knowledge Proofs (ZKP) and Pedersen Commitments, allowing vehicles to verify their authenticity without revealing private data. This ensures that communication remains both secure and anonymous, which is essential in real-world deployments where privacy concerns are paramount.</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">&nbsp;</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">To prepare for future cybersecurity challenges, the system also incorporates post-quantum cryptographic techniques. As quantum computing continues to advance, many existing encryption methods risk becoming obsolete. OmniGuard V2X addresses this by integrating cryptographic layers designed to remain secure even in the presence of quantum-capable adversaries, making the system forward-compatible with emerging threats.</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">&nbsp;</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">Another critical aspect of the system is its resilience. In distributed networks, nodes may fail or behave maliciously. To handle this, the framework is optimized with Byzantine Fault Tolerance (BFT), ensuring that the system continues to operate reliably even when some nodes are compromised. This level of robustness is essential for maintaining safety in autonomous vehicle environments.</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">&nbsp;</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">The implementation leverages a combination of edge computing and embedded systems, including devices like NVIDIA Jetson Nano, Raspberry Pi, and ESP32, enabling localized processing and real-time decision-making. Integration with perception systems using YOLOv8 further enhances situational awareness, allowing the framework to operate effectively in dynamic environments.</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">&nbsp;</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">Overall, OmniGuard V2X represents a comprehensive approach to securing autonomous vehicle networks. By combining blockchain, advanced cryptography, and edge computing, it delivers a scalable, future-ready solution that prioritizes both security and privacy in intelligent transportation systems.</p><h3 style=\"text-align:justify;\">Tools &amp; Technologies</h3><ul><li data-list-item-id=\"efd43ef6ec627d1f625ddb7765d52670a\"><h4 style=\"text-align:justify;\">Cryptography &amp; Security</h4></li><li data-list-item-id=\"ed81ae80fe8164f5f76539763dfa1b843\"><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">Post-Quantum Cryptography (PQC)</p></li><li data-list-item-id=\"ed9f75fce72bcd4e13a22b37ef8934e76\"><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">Zero-Knowledge Proofs (ZKP)</p></li><li data-list-item-id=\"e4d524ed379226c9f6e48fb7ab9e6b820\"><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">Pedersen Commitments</p></li><li data-list-item-id=\"e517805c24c428b4ba14a35ef16001f72\"><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">SHA3-256 Hashing</p></li><li data-list-item-id=\"eec0b59a4dbea7eb63246f5b2709d52c6\"><h4 style=\"text-align:justify;\">Blockchain</h4></li><li data-list-item-id=\"ebfd8b349c37987a97982f77fdb04278d\"><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">Decentralized Ledger System</p></li><li data-list-item-id=\"e66b69485063dcce25b86daa3356b9d7d\"><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">Smart Contract Logic</p></li><li data-list-item-id=\"e81af3fc191a0b369853d3eea1c319b10\"><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">Byzantine Fault Tolerance (BFT)</p></li><li data-list-item-id=\"ed88d3e43cfdfa241f6f43e613e3d3cd6\"><h4 style=\"text-align:justify;\">Programming Languages</h4></li><li data-list-item-id=\"e66de62a9f6ef42d1f5ea2a25a977ecf7\"><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">Python</p></li><li data-list-item-id=\"edaca1438f92585ba3df5bccc57883b6d\"><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">C++</p></li></ul><h4 style=\"text-align:justify;\">AI &amp; Perception</h4><ul><li data-list-item-id=\"ed34ea3548e66941b9fd66200dcae43a4\"><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">YOLOv8 Object Detection Integration</p></li><li data-list-item-id=\"e63e6664ee1313eb16e1901a72362ceba\"><h4 style=\"text-align:justify;\">Hardware &amp; Embedded Systems</h4></li><li data-list-item-id=\"ec8fa3fe3441660c8b97ca2d0a50620fe\"><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">NVIDIA Jetson Nano</p></li><li data-list-item-id=\"e7a82e72f2202cb8b468458561b44afd7\"><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">Raspberry Pi</p></li><li data-list-item-id=\"edffe128aaad65eadd6b8f8e522c2a07e\"><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">ESP32</p></li></ul><h4 style=\"text-align:justify;\">Environment &amp; Tools</h4><ul><li data-list-item-id=\"e89b78462c902fffb377f497eed069b1a\"><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">Linux</p></li><li data-list-item-id=\"e8ae78bf7caed2d6cb3d694c2e3d68839\"><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">ROS (Robot Operating System)</p></li></ul><h4 style=\"text-align:justify;\">Core Features</h4><ul><li data-list-item-id=\"e12910ddaaa970f0240d918c9b0f4c55c\"><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">Privacy-preserving authentication</p></li><li data-list-item-id=\"e7c2c400240efa9fad58866b75c29bb38\"><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">Tamper-proof data communication</p></li><li data-list-item-id=\"e5ce5b792564fbf06f1fb98e6b1fcfb80\"><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">Post-quantum security readiness</p></li><li data-list-item-id=\"ed073e35066e4284bbbde1b6015084dca\"><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">Fault-tolerant distributed system</p></li><li data-list-item-id=\"e0f94b98aa534eb341f85c1025b6df38c\"><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">Edge-based real-time processing</p></li></ul><h3 style=\"text-align:justify;\">Developer Role</h3><p style=\"text-align:justify;\"><strong>Researcher, System Architect &amp; Security Engineer</strong></p><ul><li data-list-item-id=\"e23ee09fdbdc92141d0177c7e45252617\"><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">Designed the end-to-end decentralized security architecture for V2X communication.</p></li><li data-list-item-id=\"eeba7d18cff9212cc09d415c30ebad14e\"><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">Implemented blockchain-based data integrity system using SHA3-256 chaining.</p></li><li data-list-item-id=\"e108b12136da24bc440674802a3c8475b\"><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">Developed privacy-preserving authentication using ZKP and Pedersen Commitments.</p></li><li data-list-item-id=\"e5fece3d8ae6265fe2d47f3732fbeec8c\"><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">Integrated post-quantum cryptographic mechanisms for future-proof security.</p></li><li data-list-item-id=\"e6a980f7b8f82626a9d31959f2bca82b3\"><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">Engineered Byzantine Fault Tolerant system design for resilient network operation.</p></li><li data-list-item-id=\"e13c4f1b8ce7b48de1c66ab3e47d267a8\"><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">Built and tested the system on embedded edge devices including Jetson Nano, Raspberry Pi, and ESP32.</p></li><li data-list-item-id=\"e620ed142a1536c3fdc286af2a1d93f9f\"><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">Integrated AI perception module using YOLOv8 for real-world environment awareness.</p></li><li data-list-item-id=\"ecb504a6f77355e5af46fc107e0b04f44\"><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">Optimized the system for real-time performance and scalability in smart city scenarios.</p></li></ul><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">OmniGuard V2X demonstrates how emerging technologies can be combined to address some of the most critical challenges in autonomous vehicle networks. By integrating blockchain with advanced cryptographic techniques, the system ensures secure, private, and reliable communication without relying on centralized control.</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">&nbsp;</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">Its focus on privacy, fault tolerance, and post-quantum resilience makes it not just a solution for today’s challenges, but a forward-looking framework prepared for future threats. As smart cities and autonomous systems continue to expand, solutions like OmniGuard V2X will play a key role in building secure and trustworthy transportation ecosystems.</p>'),
(11, 'Smart Finance — Developer-Centric Personal Finance Platform', 'Smart Finance is a modern full-stack personal finance management platform designed for users who want both simplicity and technical depth. Built with Next.js App Router and a scalable modular architecture, the platform combines budgeting, transaction management, savings tracking, debt monitoring, AI-powered insights, real-time updates, and advanced reporting into a single unified system.\nThe application was engineered around a reusable data-driven architecture using a custom ModulePage abstraction, allowing multiple finance modules to share the same CRUD engine with dynamic schemas, filtering, pagination, and real-time synchronization. This significantly reduced code duplication and improved long-term maintainability.\nThe platform includes secure server-side authentication, role-based admin controls, live updates through Server-Sent Events (SSE), Progressive Web App (PWA) support, Docker-based deployment, and production-grade security headers. Smart Finance focuses not only on usability, but also on scalability, maintainability, and developer experience.', '[\"Next.js 16\",\"React 19\",\"Tailwind CSS v4\",\"Recharts\",\"Sonner\",\"Lucide React\",\"Node.js 24\",\"Prisma ORM\",\"SSE / EventSource\",\"Docker\"]', 'Full-Stack Developer', 'https://github.com/smshagor-dev/smart_finance_front', 'https://smart-finance.live', 11, '2026-05-07 05:15:34.179', '2026-07-07 13:37:29.253', '/uploads/1778130912840-1000073721.png', 56, 99, '[{\"text\":\"Live Demo\",\"link\":\"https://smart-finance.live\"},{\"text\":\"Code\",\"link\":\"https://github.com/smshagor-dev/smart_finance_front\"}]', 'smart-finance-developer-centric-personal-finance-platform', '<p style=\"text-align:justify;\">The idea for Smart Finance came from a frustration I have felt for years: existing personal finance apps are either too simple or too complex, and none of them feel like something a developer would actually want to use. Spreadsheets are powerful but painful. Budgeting apps are polished but shallow. I wanted to build something in the middle technically deep, but genuinely usable.</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">&nbsp;</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">I started with the architecture. Before writing a single JSX component, I spent time designing the routing structure and the API integration pattern. The decision to use Next.js App Router with an API proxy in next.config.mjs was deliberate. It keeps the frontend completely decoupled from the backend URL, allows CORS to be handled cleanly on the Next.js layer, and means the client-side code never touches backend secrets or direct API endpoints. The browser always talks to Next.js, and Next.js talks to the backend.</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">&nbsp;</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">The biggest architectural challenge was managing state across 16 feature modules income, expenses, transactions, budgets, wallets, savings goals, debts, recurring payments, categories, currencies, groups, receipts, notifications, AI insights, reports, and more. The naive approach would have been to build each as a bespoke page. I recognized early that this would create a maintenance nightmare and enormous code duplication.</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">&nbsp;</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">Instead, I designed the ModulePage component &nbsp;a fully generic, data-driven CRUD component that accepts column definitions, form field schemas, endpoint URLs, and filter configurations as props, and handles everything else automatically: pagination, search, sorting, create/edit modals, delete confirmation, file uploads, and icon pickers.</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">&nbsp;</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">This single component eliminated approximately 70% of the code that would otherwise have been written. Each feature page became a thin configuration file just column and field definitions passed to ModulePage. The result is that adding a new module to the application is a matter of minutes, not hours, and bugs fixed in ModulePage are automatically fixed everywhere.</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">&nbsp;</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">Real-time updates were the next major challenge. Financial data changes constantly a transaction recorded on one tab should immediately appear on another, and a notification triggered by the backend should surface without a page refresh. I implemented this using Server-Sent Events (SSE) via a persistent EventSource connection in LiveUpdatesProvider.</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">&nbsp;</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">Rather than broadcasting raw DOM updates, I built a custom event bus on top of the browser’s native CustomEvent API. Components that care about specific resources register themselves using the useLiveUpdateListener hook, passing a list of resource names. A resource aliasing system maps domain-specific names like income and expenses to their canonical transactions resource, so components stay synchronized automatically.</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">&nbsp;</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">Security was not an afterthought. I configured ten security headers in next.config.mjs — including X-Frame-Options: DENY to prevent clickjacking, X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff, Cross-Origin isolation policies, and production-only HSTS with a one-year max age. Server-side authentication uses cookie forwarding to the backend on every protected request, with requireUser() and requireAdmin() guards on all protected routes, redirecting unauthenticated or unauthorized users before the page even renders. Credentials never touch the client.</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">&nbsp;</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">The admin panel was a separate design challenge. It needed to feel distinct from the main finance UI, yet coherent with it. I implemented a context-aware sidebar that switches between two navigation trees based on the current path, and a role-based guard at the layout level that redirects non-admins back to the dashboard.</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">&nbsp;</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">Admin features include user management with a full detail view, an activity log, integrity checks, platform configuration, and a site-settings page all powered by the same underlying component patterns as the main app.</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">&nbsp;</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">Toward the end of the build, I added PWA support: a web app manifest with theme colors, icons, and display modes; a service worker registration component; and an install banner that detects when the app can be added to the home screen. The application is also containerized with a multi-stage Dockerfile targeting a minimal Node.js Alpine runtime, keeping the production image lean.</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">&nbsp;</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">Looking back, the most valuable decision I made was the ModulePage abstraction. It forced me to think in data shapes rather than UI shapes, and it made every subsequent feature faster to build.</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">&nbsp;</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">The real-time system was technically the most interesting challenge designing a clean pub/sub layer on top of SSE without any external dependencies, just browser primitives, was something I am genuinely proud of.</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">&nbsp;</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">This project represents my maturity as a frontend engineer: not just building things that work, but building systems that scale.</p>');
